{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.236176+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94889910eca615ba87935b9381b2f8766461876870bf8fb068831c3c8dc74857","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 90 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] For any finite subset $F$ of $\G$, we write $\S^\rm{u}_k(F)$ for the set of all positive semidefinite elements $Q$ of $\rmM_F(\rmM_k)$ that (i) have all diagonal blocks $Q(g,g)$ equal to $I_k$, and (ii) satisfy the symmetry
\begin{equation}
	Q(g_1,h_1) = Q(g_2,h_2) \quad \hbox{whenever}\ g_1,g_2,h_1,h_2 \in F\ \hbox{and}\ g_1^{-1}h_1 = g_2^{-1}h_2.
\end{equation}
	We refer to the elements of $\S^\rm{u}_k(F)$ as \textbf{partial positive definite functions over $F$}.

	We write $\S_k^\circ(F)$ for the subset of nonsingular members of $\S^\rm{u}_k(F)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.085844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_948dd27fec84f4cced9d6f50513041208a6170dc85fe735b23aadfe7938deab9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 2 of arXiv:2609.03819, 'Stochastic damped wave and Euler-Bernoulli equations with singular locally H\"older contin'] Assume \ref{H0}--\ref{H3} hold. 
\begin{itemize}
\item[(Weak)] We say that weak uniqueness holds for \eqref{abstract_formulation} if for every $x\in H$ and every pair $(X_1,W_1)$ and $(X_2,W_2)$ of weak mild solutions to \eqref{abstract_formulation} defined on probability spaces $(\Omega_1,\mathcal F_1,\{\mathcal F_{1,t}\}_{t\geq0},\mathbb P_1)$ and $(\Omega_2,\mathcal F_2,\{\mathcal F_{2,t}\}_{t\geq0},\mathbb P_2)$, respectively, with $X_1(0)=X_2(0)=x$, it holds that $X_1$ and $X_2$ have the same law on $C([0,T]; H)$, namely that for every measurable bounded $\psi:C([0,T]; H)\to \R$
\[
\mathbb{E}_1\left[\psi(X_1)\right] =\mathbb{E}_2\left[\psi(X_2)\right].
\]
\item[(Pathwise)] We say that pathwise $($or strong$)$ uniqueness holds for \eqref{abstract_formulation}
if for every $x\in H$ and for every pair $(X_1,W)$ and $(X_2,W)$ of weak mild solutions to \eqref{abstract_formulation}
with the same $U$-cylindrical process $W$ defined on the same probability space $(\Omega,\mathcal F,\{\mathcal F_t\}_{t\geq0},\mathbb P)$ with $X_1(0)=X_2(0)=x$, it holds that
\[
\mathbb{P}\left(X_1(t)=X_2(t), \;\;\forall\,t\in [0,T] \right)=1.
\]
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.222097+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9495364de508db761b7fc6d3a3880c503d71692a33d50a13cf8dc6f9fae067fd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:wave-lower of arXiv:2608.20537, 'Persistent anisotropy in multi-dimensional\\ branching Brownian motion'] There exists a constant $\underline{C}(d) > 0$ and a uniformly bounded $\mathcal{C}^1$ function $\xi \colon [2, t] \to [0, \infty)$ such that for all $s \in [\underline{C}, t]$ and $\lambda \geq 1$,
  \begin{equation}

    \underline{w}(s, r; t, \lambda) \coloneqq \phi\bigl(\hat{b}_s + \xi_s - \frac{1}{2} \log \lambda - r\bigr)
  \end{equation}
  satisfies 
  \begin{equation}

    -\partial_s \underline{w} \leq \partial_r^2 \underline{w} + \frac{d-1}{r} \partial_r \underline{w} + \underline{w} (1 - \underline{w}).
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.952231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_949750252b9103e317541d101135bd4d7a00147ee997f9969d8e82dff24779a8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:tool_gao_bernstein of arXiv:2609.01576, '\normalfont Pointwise Majorization for sub-Weibull and Mixed Tail Processes with Applicati'] Let $X$ be the stationary diffusion in
Section (sec:pointwise_ergodic_diffusion of the paper). Suppose that it is reversible
with respect to $\pi$ and that,  $\exists\ 0<C_P<\infty$ such that
\begin{align}
\operatorname{Var}_\pi(h)
\le
\frac{C_P}{2}
\int_{\RR}a(x)|h'(x)|^2\pi(x)dx

\end{align}
for every locally absolutely continuous $h\in L^2(\pi)$ for which the
right-hand side is finite. Let $g$ be bounded and Borel with $\pi(g)=0$.
Then, for every $t,u>0$,
\begin{align}
\PP_\pi\cbr{
\left|
\frac1{\sqrt t}\int_0^t g(X_s)ds
\right|
>
2\sqrt{C_P}\|g\|_{L^2(\pi)}\sqrt u
+
\frac{C_P\|g\|_\infty}{\sqrt t}u
}
\le2e^{-u}.

\end{align}
If the long-run variance of $g$ equals $\cV_\pi(g)^2$, i.e., 
$\cV_\pi(g)^2
=
\lim_{t\to\infty}
\frac1t
\operatorname{Var}_{\PP_\pi}
\left(
\int_0^t g(X_s)ds
\right)$, then we have that
\begin{align}
\cV_\pi(g)^2
\le
2C_P\|g\|_{L^2(\pi)}^2,

\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\PP_\pi\cbr{
\left|
\frac1{\sqrt t}\int_0^t g(X_s)ds
\right|
>
\cV_\pi(g)\sqrt{2u}
+
\frac{C_P\|g\|_\infty}{\sqrt t}u
}
\le2e^{-u}.

\end{align}
The two-sided statements follow by applying the one-sided result of
[gao2014bernstein] to $g$ and $-g$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.798910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94a330c6d0fe1e50a91a0a1cbf70a2b87fd7591f307d46a40641a772d0387609","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme 62 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Assume that \ref{potentialh1} holds. Then there exists universal non-negative finite constants $C_1',C_2'$
