{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.064520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94aeaf267c6812cf6899749d33484b1da43a0090c4ec52e19c75c376490407d7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 22 (Dubins' inequality with portfolio bands, $T < \infty$) of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] Let $g_0, \ldots, g_T$ be a given, real valued, supermartingale. Also, $\Pi_{0, k}^{c, H}$ is a portfolio process as indicated above and such that $g_j \geq  \Pi_{0, j}^{c, H}$ on $\mathcal{S}$ and for all $0 \leq j \leq T$.

 Assume the definitions of $\rho_k, \tau_k$ as above, in particular $c \leq a <b$ are given  and $T < \infty$. Furthermore assume that $(L)-a.e.$ holds, then for any $k \geq 0$:
\begin{equation} 
\overline{\sigma}({\bf 1}_{\{\tau_{k+1} < T\}}) \leq
\Big(\frac{a-c}{b-c} \Big)^{k+1}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.642688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94b081d17ccde35b0165777f39270ab2c237eb24563a36bec3b6ffc1a6eeb7f9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l32 of arXiv:2411.13875, 'Large deviations at the origin of random walk in random environment'] Fix $\kappa > 0$, $j\ge 1$ and $\mathcal S:=\{\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_j\} \subseteq \mathcal P_{\mathbb V}^{(\kappa)}$ with all $\sigma_i$'s distinct. Assume that there exists some $u \in \mathbb Q^d$, with $|u|_2=1$,  such that
\begin{equation}

\langle \mathrm d(\sigma_i), u \rangle =0
\end{equation}
for all $1\le i\le j$, where $\mathrm d(\sigma_i)$ is the drift of $\sigma_i$ as defined in (equation eq:defdrift of the paper). Then, given $\varepsilon > 0$, for any $\overline{\lambda}=(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_j) \in \Delta_j$  

there exists some periodic environment $\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}$ with $\mathbf p=(\vec{p}(x)) \in \mathcal S^{\mathbf{B}_\mathbf n}$ such that $P_{0,\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}}$-almost surely, for every $1 \leq m \leq j$,
\begin{equation}

\limsup_{n\to\infty}\left|\frac{\sum_{i=0}^n1_{\{X_i\in S_m\}}}{n}-\lambda_m\right|\le\varepsilon,
\end{equation}
where $S_m$ is the set of sites $x\in \mathbb Z^d$ such that $\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}(x)=\sigma_m$. As a matter of fact, $\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}$ can be chosen as a $(u;r_1,\dots,r_j)$-strip periodic environment generated by the $\sigma_1,\ldots,\sigma_j$ for some $r_1,\dots,r_j$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.483211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94b4a6884c68f1cd2c7f2663d5445f2975dcdc3d60af6c9ec68e6aeefe12a0d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 40 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let be $\eta>0$, $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$ and $b\geq (2v)\vee(2\lambda)$. Then
\begin{equation}

\E\Big[\big\Vert\ind_{U_{0,b,\varepsilon}}\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\Big]^{1/2}
\leq \dfrac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}\big\Vert\ind_{D}\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}\,
\varepsilon^{\pi/(32 b^{2})},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

\E\Big[\big\Vert\ind_{\widetilde{U}_{0,b,\varepsilon}}\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\Big]^{1/2}
\leq \dfrac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}
\Big(\int_{D^{2}}
\Big(\Big(\dfrac{\varepsilon}{\CR(z,D)}\Big)\wedge 1\Big)^{\pi/(16 b^{2})}
\LK_{\eta}(\vert w-z\vert)\,d^{2}z\,d^{2}w\Big)^{1/2}.
\end{equation}
Fix a deterministic smooth cutoff function $f_{0}:D\rightarrow [0,1]$, compactly supported in $D$.
Assume that
\begin{displaymath}
\varepsilon\,\leq \inf_{z\in\operatorname{Supp}(f_{0})}\CR(z,D).
\end{displaymath}
Then
\begin{equation}

\E\Big[\big\Vert f_{0}\ind_{\widetilde{U}_{0,b,\varepsilon}}\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\Big]^{1/2}
\leq \dfrac{2}{\sqrt{\pi}}
\big\Vert f_{0}\big\Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}
\Big(
\dfrac{\varepsilon}{\inf_{\operatorname{Supp}(f_{0})}\CR(z,D)}
\Big)^{\pi/(32 b^{2})}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.875759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94b5c64ce12783fd9eabd6a9e5dfdf5efd9e3f6f6454c7adb6f7b86c1dd6de9e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Let $\beta>0$ and assume that $(\hat Y^x_t)_{t \ge 0}$ is $2$-dissipative with constant $\beta$. Suppose that $f$ is $L_f$-Lipschitz and twice differentiable in $y$ with $D_y f$ as well as $D^2_y f$ bounded and jointly continuous on $\R^{d_1+d_2}$. Under the hypotheses of Lemma~\ref{___lem_DyFlow}, $\Phi$ is twice differentiable in $y$, its second-order derivative is jointly continuous on $\R^{d_1+d_2}$, and there exists a constant $C_\beta >0$ with
    \begin{align*}
        |D^2_y \Phi (x,y)| \leq C_{\beta}
    \end{align*}
    for all $x \in \R^{d_1}$ and $y \in \R^{d_2}$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.918059+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94b9997cfab1c3c8cb59adbbd4c5223d0e7df4dd09ba3d24e352489c3b78ea14","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:positive-form of arXiv:2608.12147, 'The Average Singular Value of a Complex Gaussian Random Matrix Strictly Decreases with Dim'] For every $N\geqslant2$,
