\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.973992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94bc70a4b59b84b30db03c5a28834f99131a8eaed284a912d907967a4e0381f5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Fix a finite subset $J\subset \N_{\geqslant1}$. 
We denote by $\mathcal{P}(J)$ the set of all partitions of $J$. For $\rho\in \mathcal{P}(J)$, we write $|\rho|$ for the number of elements of $\rho$. We denote the elements of $\rho$ by $(\rho_q)_{q\in[|\rho|]}$: they are non-empty subsets of $J$, non-overlapping, and their union is $J$.
We adopt the convention of ordering these subsets by the order of their minima, writing $\rho=(\rho_q)_{q\in[|\rho|]}$ where $k<p\Rightarrow\min\rho_k<\min\rho_p$. 

Moreover, for two finite non-empty subsets $I,J \subset \N_{\geqslant1}$ we define 
\begin{equs}
    \mathcal{Q}(I,J)\eqdef\Big\{(\pi,\rho):\rho\in\mathcal{P}(J)\;\text{and}\;\pi:I\rightarrow[|\rho|]\Big\}\,,
\end{equs}

and we adopt the convention that if $I=\emptyset$, then we set $  \mathcal{Q}(I,J)=\mathcal{P}(J)$.

Finally, given $(\pi,\rho)\in\mathcal{Q}(I,J)$, for every $q\in[|\rho|]$, we use the shorthand $\pi_q\eqdef \pi^{-1}(q)$. The $\pi_q$'s are therefore some possibly empty subsets of $I$, non-overlapping, and whose union is $I$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.319963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94bccde44fa60466b0bc52b965e6a7b09eceb0caeb671d20ef66ff5a23be6013","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:p_solution of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $p,q\in (2,\infty)$, and assume that $u_0\in \mathbb{B}^{1-2/p}_{q,p}(\mathbb{T}^3)$ and that $\theta=(\theta_k)_{k\in {\mathbb Z}^3_0}\in \ell^2$ is  normalized and radially symmetric. Let $\tau:\Omega\to [0,\infty]$ and $u:[0,\tau)\times \Omega\to \mathbb{H}^{1,q}(\mathbb{T}^3) $ 
be a stopping time and a progressively measurable process, respectively.

\begin{itemize}
\item We say that $(u,\tau)$ is a \emph{local $(p,q)$-solution} to (equation eq:navier_stokes_intro of the paper) if there exists a sequence of stopping times $(\tau_n)_{n\geq 1}$ such that $ \tau_n\uparrow \tau$ a.s., for which the following are satisfied for every $n\geq 1$:
\begin{enumerate}[{\rm(a)}]
\vspace{0.1cm}
\item $u\in L^p(0,\tau_n;\mathbb{H}^{1,q}(\mathbb{T}^3))$ a.s.;
\vspace{0.1cm}
\item $u\otimes u\in L^p(0,\tau_n;L^{q}(\mathbb{T}^3;{\mathbb R}^{3\times 3}))$ a.s.;
\vspace{0.1cm}
\item a.s.\ for all $t\in [0,\tau_n]$ it holds that 
\begin{align*}
u(t)-u_0
= &\int_0^t \Big((1+\mu)\Delta u(s) -\mathcal{P}u(s) -\mathbb{P}\big[\nabla \cdot (u(s)\otimes u(s))\big]\Big) \,\mathrm{d} s\\
+ &\, \sqrt{\frac{3\mu}{2}}
\int_0^t {{\bf 1}}_{[0,\tau_n]}\Big(\mathbb{P}[(\theta_k\,\sigma_{k,\alpha}\cdot\nabla)u(s)\big]\Big)_ {k,\alpha}\,\mathrm{d} 
\mathcal{W}_{\ell^2}.
\end{align*}
\end{enumerate}
\item A local $(p,q)$-solution $(u,\tau)$ to (equation eq:navier_stokes_intro of the paper) is said to be a \emph{unique (pathwise) local $(p,q)$-solution} to (equation eq:navier_stokes_intro of the paper) if for any local solution $(u',\tau')$ we have $u'=u$ a.e.\ on $[0,\tau'\wedge \tau)\times \Omega$. 

\item A unique local $(p,q)$-solution $(u,\tau)$ to (equation eq:navier_stokes_intro of the paper) is said to be a \emph{unique maximal $(p,q)$-solution} to (equation eq:navier_stokes_intro of the paper) if for any local solution $(u',\tau')$ we have $\tau'\leq \tau$ a.s.\ and $u'=u$ a.e.\ on $[0,\tau')\times \Omega$. 
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.720828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94bf4db437ed0d91a49ec69702eb68a2343262c8a5ffe4db62ba9181ea89898b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:detect_intersection_right of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $z\in D$ and $r>0$ such that $2r < \delta^{1+a_3}$ and $B(z,r) \subseteq D$. Let $e \in \mathcal {E}^\delta_2(\mathcal {L})$ for some $\mathcal {L} \in \widehat{\Gamma}_2^\delta$, and suppose that $U_e \subseteq B(z,r/4)$. Then there exist $z_1,z_2 \in \partial B(z,r/2)$, $w_1 \in \partial B(z,r/4)$ (where $z_1=z_2$ is allowed) such that one of the following is true.
