{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.060289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94ec27038ecabb5afd93c030b4574bc53f4f33bb65e22636c4e65396e6fe9f4a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary propTW of arXiv:2607.14792, 'On the degree distribution of large tentacular Bienaymé--Galton--Watson trees'] Let $\mu$ be an offspring distribution and $T_n^{k_n}$ a $\mu$-BGW tree conditioned to have $n$ vertices and $k_n$ leaves. Then, we have the following equality
\begin{equation*}
 \mathbb{P}\left(T \in \mathbb{T}^{k_n}_{n}\right) = \frac{1}{n}\mathbb{P}\left(B_{n}=k_n\right)\mathbb{P}\left(W'_{n-k_n} = k_n-1\right),   
\end{equation*}
where $B_{n}$ is the sum of $n$ independent Bernoulli random variables with parameter $\mu(0)$ and  $W'$ the random walk started from $W'_0=0$ with step distribution $\xi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.234516+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94ed88f61d7028754215d4c6ecdaffe9483c1dc099d970a4eb2e3ad26e565dc3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 73 (Annealed AP entropy) of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Let $\phi \in \B(\A,\rmM_k)_+$. Its \textbf{annealed almost periodic} (`\textbf{AP}') \textbf{entropy along $\bspi$} is the quantity
\begin{equation}
\rmh^\ann_{\bspi}(\phi) := \inf_O \limsup_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{d_n}\log \bbE\frac{\vol_{2kd_n}\X(\pi_n,O)}{v(d_n)^k},
\end{equation}
where the infimum runs over all neighbourhoods of $\phi$.

Similarly, the \textbf{lower AP entropy of $\phi$ along $\bspi$} is the quantity
\begin{equation}
\ul{\rmh}^\ann_{\bspi}(\phi) := \inf_O \liminf_{n\to\infty} \frac{1}{d_n}\log \bbE\frac{\vol_{2kd_n}\X(\pi_n,O)}{v(d_n)^k},
\end{equation}
where the infimum runs over all neighbourhoods of $\phi$.","status":"unverified"}

