{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.095324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_958f55f65377ee4e9377aea1992cace44abe7a8a7c12839034e8d7aac04eb8bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop proposition:ManyToOneL* of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix $r\geq 0$.  For every non-negative measurable function $\Phi$ on $\mathcal{M}^2_f(\mathbb{R}_+) \times \mathcal{W}_{\overline{E}}$, we have:
