{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.588433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95c11dd47f5400cfc3b3d7a55bc7e68cebc121a0bec7934c8bfebd076fc11677","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] [AGS08]
    Let $(S,d)$ be a metric space and $F:S\to (-\infty,\infty]$ measurable. A function $g:S\to [0,\infty]$ is a strong upper gradient for $F$ if for every absolutely continuous curve $v\in AC(a,b;S)$ the function $g\circ v$ is Borel and \begin{align*}
        \left\lvertF(v(t))-F(v(s))\right\rvert\leq \int_s^tg(v(r))\left\lvertv'\right\rvert(r)dr \quad \forall a< s\leq t< b.
    \end{align*}
    In particular, if $g\circ v \left\lvertv'\right\rvert\in L^1(a,b)$ then $F\circ v$ is absolutely continuous and \begin{align*}
        \left\lvert(F\circ v)'(t)\right\rvert\leq g(v(t))\left\lvertv'(t)\right\rvert\quad \text{ for a.e. } t\in (a,b).
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.625120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95c3a505ec280610b0e446913f7e4ce40767c7597e620bda46970ed7c0d7d1bf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:weightedore of arXiv:2609.00889, 'Dominant-Degree Conditions for Ramsey--Tur\'an Factors of Non-Directed Cycle Orientations'] Suppose that $D$ is an oriented graph of sufficiently large order $n$  with
