{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.963242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95e1f178a9c6a62b83250f2a147c89eeb5ad7e63fef91a7cff013ca3eac7e5bc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:grad-var-rmulmc of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Let $h \lesssim 1/\beta^{1/2}$, $\gamma \lesssim \sqrt{\beta}$, and let $(\hat X_{\mathsf{u} h}^+, X_{\mathsf{u}h})$ be as defined in~(eq:rm-ulmc of the paper) and~(eq:ULD of the paper) respectively, where both processes are started at $(x, p)$ and synchronously coupled with the same Brownian motion ${\{B_t\}}_{t \geqslant 0}$. Then, for any $\mathsf{u} \in [0, 1]$,
    \begin{align*}
