{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.903303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95e52b4c5619419fcf533284c568286cd68f8254b279d54ea0b6ce3b0a7f2ea5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 ($\sigma$-Martingale Criterion) of arXiv:2606.20925, 'Explicit Predictable Compensators for Single Jump Processes with Initial Information'] Let $X$ be an adapted right-continuous process of finite variation with the canonical representation $X_t=F(t)\ind_{\{t<\gamma\}}+L\ind_{\{t\ge\gamma\}}$. The process $X$ is a $\sigma$-martingale in the filtration $\FF$ if and only if there exists a strictly positive predictable process $\varphi$, defined by an $\cH$-measurable function $\varphi(t)$, such that the following two conditions hold:
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item Local integrability of the localized jump:
        \begin{equation}
            \EE\left[\varphi(\gamma)|L-F(\gamma-)|\right]<\infty.
        \end{equation}
        \item The drift balance conditions: on the interval $s<t_G$, the differential equation holds,
        \begin{equation}
            \overline{G}_{\cH}(s-)dF(s)+F(s)dG_{\cH}(s)+H(s)dG_{\cH}(s)=0
        \end{equation}
        and at the terminal atom $t_G$, the boundary condition holds,
        \begin{equation}
            H(t_G)=F(t_G-).
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

