{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.536261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96469243b5e429dc37b1936fbe7f1deb00c3b8c55654d39e5f61dcb5d5796d9d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pr:key_estimate_avg of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] Given $i,j \in \mathbb{N}$, there exist constants $\{C_{i,j}(\mathfrak{p},\mathsf{r}, d)\}_{i,j \in \mathbb{N}}$ independent of $m \in \mathbb{N}_+$ such that the following statement holds for $\overline{I}_m(i,j)$ that
