\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.881188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_966eeda1229f5650565a1d8ee5a7819faf149aa862775b04c9d098066fc92dfe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:upper-gradient of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $K \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be a compact $C(v,\theta)$-cone null set and $f \in C^1(\mathbb{R}^n)$, for some $v \in \mathbb{S}^{n-1}$ and $\theta \in (0,\pi/2)$.
		Then,
		\[
		g = {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex \nabla f \kern-0.25ex\right\vert} \mathds{1}_{\mathbb{R}^n \setminus K} + \sup_{w \in \mathbb{S}^{n-1} \setminus (C^\circ \cup( -C^\circ))} {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex \langle \nabla f, w \rangle \kern-0.25ex\right\vert}
		\]
