{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.822340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96b14d4157c0cf48e2ca1d441f5ec8fc59a1c8c03d733d4b34980caaf8a3db06","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2604.10244, 'Ergodicity for regime-switching neutral stochastic functional differential equations with '] There exist constants \( 0<c_{1}<c_{2}< \) \( \infty \) such that for any \( i \in \S \) and \( 0 \leq  u<t \),
