{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.194606+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96d66f4a020c902f38aa51f8b8e3ec9b79c42dc1c40966637535c2e9c5ead90d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Fix $p\ge 3$, $n_{1,j},n_{2,j}\in \N\cup\{0\}$ and multi-indices $\bm{k}_j\in\N^{n_{1,j}}$, $\bm{l}_j\in\N^{n_{2,j}}$ for $j\in [p]$. Denote $n:=\sum_{j=1}^p (n_{1,j}+n_{2,j})$ and assume that $n<2p-2$. Then for $\beta=2$ we have
