{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.303027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9706d937fa5f31047f99e2edfb820bbc63bbe37ab6756bd5eb38370c9e1cf44c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem imp_ind of arXiv:2608.07236, 'Negative association of Busemann functions \\in exponential last-passage percolation'] Fix a direction parameter $\lambda\in(0,1)$ and a unit edge $[\![\mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b}]\!]$, where $\mathbf {b}\in\{\mathbf a+\mathbf e_1,\mathbf a-\mathbf e_2\}$.
