{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.334617+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9719169b7009257fb935c9298db2d701741172b5cfccdd32adff81cfd976705e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=\left(V,E\right)$ be a locally finite weighted graph satisfying the $CD\psi\left(n,-K\right)$ condition with $K\geq0$, where $\psi\in C^{1}\left(0,+\infty\right)$ is a concave function. Then for any $0<f\in \ell^{\infty}\left(V\right)$ with $R_{f}<\infty$, 
