{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.453043+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_973ac1a45e90e0e22ece5035b489fc34d588ee13249c0c739d4286b4a275a380","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:nested of arXiv:2609.02234, 'An $n(\log n)^{o(1)}$ bound for nested cycles without geometric crossings'] A sequence $C_1,\ldots,C_k$ of cycles in a graph is a family of \emph{$k$ nested cycles without geometric crossings} if
\begin{enumerate}
  \item $V(C_k)\subseteq V(C_{k-1})\subseteq\cdots\subseteq V(C_1)$;
  \item the cycles are pairwise edge-disjoint; and
  \item for every $i<k$, the cyclic order induced by $C_i$ on $V(C_{i+1})$ agrees, up to reversal, with the cyclic order of $C_{i+1}$.
\end{enumerate}
For $k\ge2$, let $f_k(n)$ be the least integer such that every $n$-vertex graph with at least $f_k(n)$ edges contains such a family.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.239686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97403817adce7fb55797920bf995449e5a6dad15b8eb42e0acb039e5cead6c61","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 61 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(\mcalM\) be the category of morphisms \(R \to T\) in \(\Perfd\) such that \(R\) is \(p\)-torsion-free and \(T\) is an \(\setF_p\)-algebra.
