  where \(\rho'\) is the natural transformation induced from \(\rho \colon \mcalG \to \mcalF\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.188090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_974c2116c8941434d1208d745ff3943d8221cd8c875ceedda26b8e1ffbce1399","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.30411, 'Notes on constants for maxima of Rademacher averages'] For $n=2m$,
\begin{equation}
    \Eb\max_{1\leq j\leq p}\Abs{\sum_{i=1}^n\epsilon_{ij}}
    =
    2\sum_{k=0}^{m-1}
    \left[1-\{1-2F_n(k)\}^p\right].
\end{equation}
For $n=2m+1$,
\begin{equation}
