{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.240275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_978002015884a83d4521443fb427d31d1347167d854260aa09d725a6a6691c31","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi process of arXiv:2412.09471, 'On the moderate deviation principles in the sparse multi-type Erd\H{o}s R\'enyi random gra'] For all $n$ fixed, let $\{X^n_i\}_{i\ge 1}$ be a sequence of $i.i.d$ random vectors in $${\mathbb S}_{n}:=\{k:k_r\in\{1,\cdots,\lfloor\mu^n_r n\rfloor\},r\in{\mathcal S}\}$$ with  common law
\begin{equation}
    {\mathbb P}(X^{n}=k)=
    \frac{1}{Z_n}
    \frac{n^{|k|-1}p_n(k)\prod_{s\in{\mathcal S}}\left({\mu^n_s}\prod_{r\in{\mathcal S}}\left(1-\frac{\kappa(r,s)}{n}\right)^{\mu^n_rn-\frac{k_r}{2}}\right)^{k_s}}
    {\prod_{s\in{\mathcal S}}k_s!},
\end{equation}
where
\[
