{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.387045+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97ae097ac75d32a5e5c75877b323d7333e88ebdcb717fc469cd479967c53829f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:maincnvg of arXiv:2608.29657, 'Hypocoercivity of Tempered Bouncy Particle Samplers for Heavy-Tailed Targets'] ~
      Let Assumptions~(ass:wpi of the paper), (ass:sigmabounds of the paper), and~(ass:curvature of the paper) hold. Recall the constant $K_0$  in~(equation eq:defconstants of the paper) and the refresh rate $\lambda_{\mathrm r}>0$ in~(equation eq:TBP of the paper). Then, for all $f \in L^2(\mu_\sigma)$ with $\mu_\sigma(f) = 0$, the  inequality 
