        $ is invertible. By Lemma~(lemma:ev-V-jointly-repr of the paper) the functors $\ev_V$ are jointly conservative, so it will suffice to show that the Beck--Chevalley map is an equivalence after hitting it with $\ev_V$ for every representation $V$. But we have a commutative diagram of Beck--Chevalley maps
        \[
            \begin{tikzcd}
                \ev_V\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!'g'^*\arrow[r,"\textup{BC}_!"]\arrow[d,"\ev_V\textup{BC}_!"'] & \textbf{\textup{L}}f_!'\ev_Vg'^*\arrow[r,"\sim"] & \textbf{\textup{L}}f'_!g'^*\ev_V\arrow[d,"\textup{BC}_!"]\\
                \ev_Vg^*\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!\arrow[r,"\sim"'] & \ev_Vg^*\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!\arrow[r,"g^*\textup{BC}_!"'] & g^*\textbf{\textup{L}}f_!\ev_V
            \end{tikzcd} 
        \]
        in which the two horizontal Beck--Chevalley maps are equivalences as $\ev_V$ is a left adjoint, while the right-hand vertical map i (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.329124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_981840435c564e114b5bbfc99c6572f30a6dd1313237a2e4003b5651cffdde46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:cf_tempered of arXiv:2412.06374, 'Stable and tempered stable distributions and processes: an overview toward trajectory simu'] Let $(X_t)_{t\in \mathbb{R}}$ be a CTS Lévy process with Lévy triplet $\left(b_\nu, 0,\nu\right)$ where $\nu$ defined as in (equation eq:levy_measure_tempered_stable of the paper) and $b_\nu=\int_{|x|>1}x \nu(dx)$. For $t\in \mathbb{R}_+$, the characteristic function exponent can be expressed for $u\in \mathbb{R}$ as 
