{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.752186+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_981faff1a4f3a2bb19a4a2775b7b9082fe139331c914c68b884f230738f2f939","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition th:lin_FP of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $s\in [0,T)$, $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and let ${\boldsymbol\mu}:[s,T)\to \mathcal{M}_{+}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ (continuous, with ${\boldsymbol\mu}_{s} = \nu$) be such that
