{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.200725+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_983677664619108f2ad047589bec4cb03fc6e151df681ecaeccb80dba84412a2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] For the equation given by \eqref{eq NS},\eqref{eq xi} and any $B_0,\gamma,\varepsilon>0$, there exists $N\in\N^+$ such that if the sequence $\{b_j\}_{j\in\N^+}$ satisfies
