{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.031230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_985e14f9ee7bc5f6d3fd1e5045329b782f32744f7a68b8e0d97901a108ff45d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2609.00736, 'Modalities in non-classical variations of S4'] For all formula $\varphi$:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item  
            $\csf\vdash \neg\neg\neg\varphi\leftrightarrow \neg \varphi$;
        \item  
            $\csf\vdash \Box\Box\varphi \leftrightarrow \Box\varphi$;
        \item  
            $\csf\vdash \Diamond\Diamond \varphi \leftrightarrow\Diamond\varphi$;
        \item  
            $\csf\vdash \Box\Diamond\Box\Diamond \varphi \leftrightarrow \Box\Diamond\varphi$;
        \item  
            $\csf\vdash \Diamond\Box\Diamond\Box \varphi \leftrightarrow \Diamond\Box \varphi$;
        \item  
            $\csf\vdash \Box\neg \neg\Box\neg  \varphi \leftrightarrow \Box\neg \varphi$; and
        \item  
            $\csf\vdash \Box\neg\Box\neg\Box\neg\Box\neg \varphi \leftrightarrow \Box\neg\Box\neg\varphi$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.643426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_986080d22dab97173b2f70735dfa2c0eed5c829fcd966d230830f50a19332270","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm weak plus measure of arXiv:2608.18045, 'Supercritical sharpness for the random cluster representation of real-valued spin models'] Let $d\geq2$ and $(\eta_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence of boundary conditions satisfying $\eta_n(x)\ll e^{n}$ and $\eta_n(x) \gg n^{-(d-1)}$ for every $x\in \partial^{\textup{ext}}\Lambda_n$. Then, for every $\beta\in (\beta_c,\infty)\setminus\Xi$,
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{n\to\infty} \nu^{\eta_n}_{\Lambda_n,\beta} = \nu^+_{\beta}.    
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.389904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9865ae5f37a634fff0b46a50c4dd68754d9a66c484f5910af09fb4a0a4e7c207","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:tightness of arXiv:2606.11503, 'Percolation on hierarchical lattices'] Consider a family of random edge-rooted graphs $(G^{\lambda}, E^{\lambda})_{\lambda \in \Lambda}$ in $\mathcal{G}$, and let $\deg(E^\lambda)$ denote the sum of degrees of endpoints of $E^{\lambda}$. This family is tight if and only if
  \begin{equation}

    \deg(E^{\lambda}), \text{ for $\lambda \in \Lambda$},
  \end{equation}
  is tight. The same result also holds for any family of random edge-rooted graphs with marks in $\mathcal{A}$, $(G^{\lambda}, E^{\lambda}, \mathsf{m}^\lambda)_{\lambda \in \Lambda}$ in $\mathcal{G}_\mathcal{A}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.053248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98679b5c5be05a8f8dcb020e7b60fa886caa63b96939eb356a4f2d974bb3cb77","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:dimhofintersectionwithsublevelset of arXiv:2506.10448, 'Hitting probabilities and the Ekstr\"om--Persson conjecture'] Let $\mu\in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $t>0$ with $D_\mu(t) \neq \emptyset$. Then, almost surely, for every $\alpha>0$ with $t-F_\mu(t)<\frac 1\alpha \leq t$, we have that
\begin{equation}

\dimh (E_{\alpha}(\omega)\cap {D_\mu(t)})\geq \frac{1}{\alpha}+F_\mu(t)-t.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.146379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_986f42f403be912fc8c4a71f8533402dcab0f116bec1e528cee0f0721c524c31","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:dissipation_of_E of arXiv:2602.00988, 'Wealth exchange under ceiling and flooring constraints: a modified Bennati–Dragulescu–Yako'] Let ${\bf p}(t) = \{p_n(t)\}_{n\geq 0}$ be a classical solution to the system of nonlinear ODEs (equation eq:law_limit of the paper)-(equation eq:two-classes of the paper) with ${\bf p}(0) \in \mathcal{A}$. There exist fixed $k_1>0$ and $k_2>0$ such that for all $t \geq 0$ we have
\begin{equation}
\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} t} \widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{ab}[{\bf p}] \leq 0.
\end{equation}
Moreover, $\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d} t} \widetilde{\mathcal{H}}_{ab}[{\bf p}] = 0$ if and only if ${\bf p}$ coincides with ${\bf p}^*$ (equation eq:equi of the paper). Consequently, ${\bf p}(t) \xrightarrow{t\to \infty} {\bf p}^*$ strongly in $\ell^p$ for each $1 < p < \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.671649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_987597b643c88cca0784ab1af62d17f7d153cb617273e81e6cc7f8611cb89610","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (resolvent boundary condition) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[lemma]{lem:resolvent-bc}
The resolvent kernel $G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(x,y)$, viewed as a function
of its first argument at fixed $y \in (0,\infty)$, solves
$(\alpha-\mathcal{L})G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(\cdot,y)=\delta_y$ on $(0,\infty)$
in the speed-measure sense, with boundary condition
\begin{equation}
  \frac{dG^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(\cdot,y)}{ds}(0^+)
  = \frac{\alpha}{\mu}\,G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(0,y).
\end{equation}
By the symmetry $G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(x,y) = G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(y,x)$, the same condition holds in the second argument.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.368416+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9877d86e5357916bda236245d5e74d02006e34d0f3a90a8c6c2c511e44672314","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] The \textit{Brownian-snake} is the Markov process in $\mathcal{W}$, denoted by $(\omega_s,s\geq0)$, whose transition kernels $\mathcal{Q}_s$ are given by 
