{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:53:51.342233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9882d415c7cc1d81d8c1e4dd8521af7080e6f910c6e030c098f45fe55d314bc4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm_cons of arXiv:2605.05904, 'Schr\"odinger's problem with constraints'] Under Assumptions~(a:main of the paper) and (ass:f of the paper),  the optimizer of the constrained \sch problem (equation e:minentadpt of the paper) is $P({\hat\alpha})$, with $\hat\alpha_t=\sigma^2(t,X^2_t)\frac{\rho_y(t,X^2_t;X^1_1)}{\rho(t,X^2_t;X^1_1)}$, where $\rho:[0,1]\times E_\ell^2\to\bbR_+$ is defined as
