{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.330013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_988cd647b1ac09a6390c25a4c7f4b46e5d62d97a15021707dfeb15e736cc3d71","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma renormalization of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Let $f:\Omega\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a local function whose support is included in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0 -1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$. There exists a constant $C_{14}=C_{14}(\kappa ,\rho ,\mathcal{E} ,f)>0$ such that for any $t\in [0,T]$, and $\ell\ge \ell_0$ and any measurable function $v:[0,T]\longrightarrow\ell^2(\mathbb{Z})$, we have 
    \begin{equation}

        \mathbb{E}_{\rho ,\mathcal{E}}\left[\left(\int_0^t\sum_{x\in\mathbb{Z}}\tau_x\big\{ \mathbb{E}_{\ell }[f]-\mathbb{E}_{2\ell}[f]\big\} (s)v_s(x)\,\mathrm{d} s\right)^2\right] \le C_{14} \frac{\ell^\beta}{N^a}\int_0^t\| v_s\|^2\,\mathrm{d} s,
    \end{equation}
    where
    \begin{equation*}
        \beta = \begin{cases}
            2 & \mbox{ if }\nabla\psi_f(\rho ,\mathcal{E})\neq 0,\\
            1 & \mbox{ if } \nabla\psi_f(\rho ,\mathcal{E} )=0\mbox{ and }\mathrm{Hess}(\psi_f)(\rho ,\mathcal{E})\neq 0,\\
            0 & \mbox{ if } \nabla\psi_f(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0\mbox{ and }\mathrm{Hess}(\psi_f)(\rho ,\mathcal{E})=0.
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:25:44.959077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_988e94473e52d8cb19cdd3de682a3cfe6637fd819c52ffcddd78e591ee1e28de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2605.11264, 'Uniform sampling of multitype continuous-time Bienaym\'e-Galton-Watson trees'] Fix $i\in [d]$. For any $\bm{\ell}\in \z^d_+\setminus\{\bo 0\}$ with $\ell_i>0$ and $0< t<T$, we have
