{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.778365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98bc020f076ef070941a280baef5908804689c60a05151e0814698c756bab896","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Assume that $\rK$ is a separable infinite dimensional Hilbert space. A $\rK$-cylindrical Wiener process $W=(W(t): t \in [0,T])$ is a family of formal series
