{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.328216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9923f6c5e712b5eee1335dae46088d29f0992ad0f497c49e794588e708779c01","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2607.14674, 'On the entropy of the log-normal distribution'] The entropy $H[g_r]$ of the family of densities \eqref{eq:SC} is given as the power series
\begin{equation}
H[g_r]=H[g]+\alpha r -\sum_{k=1}^\infty \frac{\beta_k}{2k(2k-1)}r^{2k},\quad -1\le r\le 1,
