{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.499261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_995583e06abdf2535b0ef6197c95a5c3331a95fa2c1596b75933697430a4425f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2605.29608, '2605.29608'] Let $(Y_{k})_{k\in\mathbb{Z}^{+}}$ and $\mu_{N}$ be defined as in Theorem \ref{thm: transitionmatrix}. If the coupling constant $\hat{J}\in [0,+\infty)$, then for any real-valued function $f:\Omega\to\mathbb{R}$, we have
	\begin{align*}	
