{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.300667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9959315cd572bfd174066c82af5328f5e78545792c32d6731cdf0dc0d1a59e73","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:eternal_time_s of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Let $b$ be an eternal solution, and assume there exists $s \in \mathbb{R}$ so that $\pmb{\xi}^{b,s}$ contains at least two colors. Then, for all $x \in \mathbb{R}$,
    \[
