{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.474669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9966d1ad771c0f821f8f8b964fa79eb3a6114b064914ea50bda73091784a612d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:index-generating-formal of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[theorem]{thm:index-generating}
Fix \(s\in\mathbb R\), \(L>L_0\), and a continuous \(V\) bounded below.  Then
\begin{align}
 &\lim_{R\to\infty}\lim_{\delta\downarrow0}
 \lim_{\eta\downarrow0}\lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow0}
 \lim_{N\to\infty}
 \Phi_{N,L}^{G}(V,\varepsilon,f_{\eta,R,s,\delta})\notag\\
 &\qquad=\sup_u\{\theta_p(u)-V(u)+s\alpha_p(u)\}.

\end{align}
If \(V\in\mathcal V_m\) and the array \(J\) satisfies the hypotheses of either
(thm:bulk-universality of the paper) or (thm:weibull-bulk of the paper), the same
iterated limit holds with \(G\) replaced by \(J\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.407293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_996b10154ea145311a25c27a65bdcd5b3508f35fe998034379fb32221e47e4d5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Monotone coupling) of arXiv:2604.06532, 'Random permutations from $q$-Demazure products'] There exists a coupling such that for all $U \in \{0, 1, \dots, M-1\}$
and $V \in \{0, 1, \dots, X\}$:
\begin{equation}
  H^{refl}(V, U)
  \;\ge\; H^{dstep}(V, U)
  \qquad\text{and}\qquad
  H^{act}(V, U)
  \;\le\; H^{quad}(V, U),
\end{equation}
where $H^{quad}$ is the height function of the step-initial S6V on the quadrant.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.927867+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9975cc866677d9ffe028bc52cf40f86b1ecd3b2069e182e9c187d9ec30633493","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 of arXiv:2609.01020, '2609.01020'] Assume that the C.I. subvariety $Y=\{f_1=\cdots =f_d=0\} 
