{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.737465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_999dc0d33bca2b553f45771f357c7b56ceea7fd034737c52a836f454178a0e97","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:CL-gen-system of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The system (equation eq:Linear-Psi-3 of the paper) is compatible\footnote{That is, for any choice of initial data $\{\Psi(T^ku_0)\}_{k \in \mathbb{Z}}$ along a $T$-orbit, the value of $\Psi$ at any vertex reached by a finite composition of $S_i$-shifts is independent of the order of the composition.} if and only if for all $i, j\in \mathbb{N}$ and $u \in \mathcal V$,
