\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.829610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99ae14d0ed7e9716a29c90c3ee0ae8083c0e3c5071e87c1d1fc2fcc424647d08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop eq:OP_BT of arXiv:2609.01751, 'Orthogonal polynomials which are eigenfunctions of a partial differential operator'] For $\mu > - \frac12$, ${\boldsymbol{\kappa}} \in {\mathbb R}^{d_2}$ with $k_j > -1$, $1 \le j \le d_2$, define 
\begin{equation} 
 \bm Q_{\bm j, \bm k, m}^n(\bm x,\bm y) = \bm T_{\bm j, n-m}^{({\boldsymbol{\kappa}}, \alpha+2m)}(\bm y) (1-|\bm y|)^m 
      \bm B_{\bm k, m}^\mu \left(\frac{\bm x}{1-|\bm y| }\right),
\end{equation}
where $\alpha = 2 \mu + d_1-1$. Then
$\{\bm Q_{\bm j, \bm k, m}^n: |\bm k| = m, \, |\bm j| = n-m, \, \bm k \in {\mathbb N}_0^{d_1}, \, \bm j \in {\mathbb N}_0^{d_2}, 0\le m \le n\}$ 
is an orthogonal basis of ${\mathcal V}_n\big({\mathbb B}^{d_1}\!\! \rtimes\triangle^{d_2}, \bm W_{\mu, {\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}\big)$. 
Moreover, the norm square of $\bm Q_{\bm j, \bm k, m}^n$ is given by 
\begin{equation} 
   \bm h_{\bm j, \bm k, m}^{n; \mu,{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}}  

       = \frac{(2\mu+d_1)_{2m}} {(|{\boldsymbol{\kappa}}|+ 2\mu + d_1 + d_2)_{2m}}\bm h_{\bm k,m}^{\mu, {\mathbb B}}  
       \bm h_{\bm j,m}^{({\boldsymbol{\kappa}}, {\alpha}+2m), \triangle}. 
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.896869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99b24eef0ce816503314105bfbb4c6ade12252c23c3f21b71097662b818bb971","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm thm:OdeltaRWintro of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] Let $k\in \mathbb{N}$ and $\rho_\ell$ be a bounded sequence.
When $\alpha\in[0,1)$, the scaling bound in (equation eq:scalimRW of the paper) is a scaling limit with error
\begin{equation} 
\delta_{[\alpha\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^M=\mathrm{O}\left(\frac{\beta_\ell+1}{\ell}\right) =o(1),
\end{equation}
When $\alpha=1$, the scaling error in (equation eq:scalimRW of the paper) is 
\begin{equation} 
\delta_{[\ell-\beta_\ell,\ell]}^M
=\mathrm{O}\left( \frac{\ell}{\beta_\ell} \delta_{[0,\ell]}^M\right) +\mathrm{O}(1)\begin{cases}
    \frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell} & n\ge 3
    \\
    m_\ell \sqrt{\frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell}} 
    & n =2 
    \\
    m_\ell^2& n =1
\end{cases},
\end{equation}
as $\ell\to +\infty$, for all $\alpha\in [0,1]$, where
\begin{equation} 
m_\ell:=\sqrt{
    \min\left\{\max\left\{ \frac{\beta_\ell}{\ell}, \beta_\ell\rho_\ell\right\},1 \right\}.
    }
    \end{equation}
 In particular, the $\mathcal{C}^k$ Scaling Bound of Random Waves of type $\alpha=1$ in fixed range $[0,\rho]$, with $\rho=\rho_\ell$, is a scaling limit, that is,  $\delta^M_{I_\ell}=\mathrm{o}(1)$, under either of the following (sufficient) conditions:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item $n\ge 2$ and $\beta_\ell\to +\infty$;
    \item $n\ge 2$, $\frac 1{\beta_\ell}$ is bounded, and $\delta_{[0,\ell]}^M=\mathrm{o}(\ell^{-1})$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.895249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99b419f65bf037e1010e38af2329e40d85b5f6cff87d57ca387430e004535f05","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:convergence_need_to_explain of arXiv:2606.31155, 'The well-posedness of stochastic Korteweg--de Vries equations revisited'] Let $f(\omega,x)\in L_\omega^2L_x^2$ and $k(x,y)\in L_x^\infty L_y^2 $. Then, we have 
