{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.350552+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99be42e5d1175f01cd11bf2108edd59d5a04b96abccfae4854894210f62d0c1e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:scalar_DR_variance of arXiv:2609.02491, 'Generalised Random Parking for Trapeziums on a Strip'] Let $F:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ be locally bounded and continuous for all sufficiently large arguments. Suppose that, for some $C_0\in\mathbb{R}$ and all sufficiently large $x$,
