{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.369250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_99e845843b45d72d3c41022a4cc5f8a913fe1fbc34b85473be4b93aaa158219e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:buckling_D_norm of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $(S, T) \in [0,1]^2_\leq$ and ${\color{blue}f} \in \mathcal{D}_g^{2\gamma}([s,t])$.  Suppose that there exist constants $C_1, C_2$ such that for all $(s,t) \in [S,T]_{\leq}^2$ we have
