{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.087178+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a3b78967b815f9f3e7266905dbba3344e606c38f1c5ecdbfb0d9c8fc95c29e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:forward of arXiv:2606.12143, 'Continuous stochastic flows driven by white noise and their duals'] Fix $\alpha>0$. There exists a family of processes
    $$
    \mathcal S = \left\{\bigl(\mathcal S_{r,x}(a),\, x \ge r\bigr)\right\}_{(a,r) \in {\mathbb H}}
