{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.735007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ad2b1be14b3744cf3a7b590301297c00afcb74c53caa8b37abdc8f7efdf9fc2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 22 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] For all $x,y \in \mbR^d$, we have that 
