{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.635124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ae53b81247473495f1cf24575431c00e9652afa04b69f19174343ba39211c27","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:PBW of arXiv:2411.13707, 'High-degree cubature on Wiener space \\ through unshuffle expansions'] Given a Hall basis $H$, the set
