{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.786186+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b33d625d32c34019c325124f6b7a6bbd419715870909304da316c67e86a5017","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 of arXiv:2604.00598, 'Allowing for Imprecision in the Game-theoretic Characterisation of the Poisson Process'] For all natural numbers~\(k\in\nats\), time points~\(t_1, \dots, t_{k+1}\in\posreals\) such that \(t_1<\cdots<t_{k+1}\), bounded functions~\(g\in\bfns[k+1]\) and paths~\(\pth\in\countpaths\), and with \(\Delta\coloneqq t_{k+1}-t_k\),
\begin{equation*}
\oscuprev{g\gr{N_{t_1}, \dots, N_{t_{k+1}}}}[t_k]\gr{\pth}
= \osuprev{g\gr{\pth\gr{t_1}, \dots, \pth\gr{t_k}, \pth\gr{t_k}+N_{\Delta}}}.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.066570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b342efba736063dac1ce74ed9e401d34638441d3f8c50c7296279aa068b951d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 (Characterizing equation for the mgf of the stationary distribution) of arXiv:2606.00781, '2606.00781'] The moment generating function (mgf) $g:[0,1]\to[0,\infty)$ of the stationary distribution $\mu$ of $X$, defined via $g(x):=\sum_{n=0}^\infty \mu_nx^n/n!$ for all $x\in[0,1]$, satisfies for every $x\in[0,1]$ the
   equation
   \begin{equation} 
      2dxg'(x)+2\int_{(0,1]}\frac{g(x)-g(x(1-t))}{t}\,\Lambda({\rm d}t)\ =\
      dxg(x)+\int_{(0,1]}\frac{e^{xt}-1}{t}g\big(x(1-t)\big)\,\Lambda({\rm d}t)
   \end{equation}
   with $d:=\Lambda(\{0\})$. Conversely, if $g$ is the mgf of some distribution on $[0,1]$ and if $g$ satisfies
   the equation (\ref{inteqn}) for all $x\in[0,1]$, then $g$ is the mgf of the stationary distribution $\mu$ of $X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.985318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b37690bdc58bca79295e92e3bcd9451c216e19031d0310ddd474a0e4d4716d1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Collision-null diffuse basis) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] The family in \eqref{primitive:eq:spatial-replicas} satisfies:
