{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.356939+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b3d940952ad5097ce831f70a3a5cad05ad810a7e1a7821191c749a1b76008b4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:iteration_enhanced of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $R>0$, $M\geq 1$ and $\eta\in (0,1)$. Let $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ be such that (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper) holds.
