{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.646067+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b5a0194279db90dc2b34224272cd31cc3f92b2c44dc46992c64045cb6197fe3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ht-bdd tree of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $h_n$ be such that $4\leq h_n\ll\sqrt{n}$.
    Then, for any $4\leq m\leq h_n$, we have
    \begin{align*}
        H_{n,m}&=\frac{4^n}{m+1}\frac{\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)}{\left(1+\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)\right)^n}+O\left(\frac{4^n}{m^3}\frac{1}{\left(1+\tan^2\left(\frac{2\pi}{m+1}\right)\right)^n}\right)\\
        &=\big(1+o(1)\big)\frac{4^n}{m+1}\frac{\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)}{\left(1+\tan^2\left(\frac{\pi}{m+1}\right)\right)^n}
    \end{align*}
    where the $o(\cdot)$ and $O(\cdot)$ terms only depend on $h_n$, and are uniformly bounded over all such $m$.
    Moreover, the second asymptotic equality trivially holds when $m\in\{2,3\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.045706+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b5c72788dd850e7b8a453d3818ceae013d7b8a0f71e7c7694c427d10b9cccde","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Limiting point process of arXiv:2411.13972, 'The Stochastic Bessel operator at high temperatures'] There is a random variable $M_0$ valued in the Borel sets of $]0,\infty[$, such that, for all fixed $\mu_1 < \ldots < \mu_k$,
