{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.329931+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c016779688606b32ecd9fe1801cff6feb08a2729cdf5f94030cee5b16f3f3b8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1BE of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Consider a local function $f:\Omega\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ whose support is included in~$\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0-1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$. There exists a constant $C_{13}=C_{13}(\kappa ,\rho ,\mathcal{E} ,f)>0$ such that for any $t\in [0,T]$ and any measurable function $v:[0,T]\longrightarrow\ell^2(\mathbb{Z} )$, we have 
    \begin{equation}
