{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.712752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c020be19e06ccfaf2821e06652fb911c7211afe23001a0a5e1ae4ba9aad2939","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Lipschitz function of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] Given $(\mathcal{X},d)$ a metric space, a function ${f: \mathcal{X}\to \mathbb{R}}$ is called $L$-Lipschitz if 
