{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.295643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c82e6cc85c2940cf9dd5b09bf381db66a5adcd48d4669725ce734457df3c03d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary LM of arXiv:2605.10452, 'A secretary for Messrs. Luce and Mallows'] When the weights for the Luce distribution are given by $\theta_j=q^j$, for $q\in(0,\infty)$, one has
