{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.022393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c8314c0da77b347ee843b5cda238bf67619ac111fd72d04ea33196910f13611","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 (Stationary distribution) of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] Suppose that $\{U_t\}_{t\ge 0}$ is a solution to the free SDE \eqref{eq:fSDE}. A probability measure $\mu\in\mathcal P(\mathbb R)$ is called a \textit{stationary distribution} for the solution (or the equation) if, for every $t\ge0$, 
