{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.332903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c8bcb6bd64490220ca6d394a180e06066a64672f11e6561d1bb54322bf6604a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2511.05618, 'Coupling Invasion and First Passage Percolation'] For any $\epsilon >0$, $r\ge 0$, there exists an $R_0=R_0(\epsilon, r)$ such that for all $R\ge R_0$  
