{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.224550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c9a225c501654e042a741fddaaf3781382bbfa72d611fc3a7a72700ae63fe79","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cor of arXiv:2412.09471, 'On the moderate deviation principles in the sparse multi-type Erd\H{o}s R\'enyi random gra'] \hfill
\begin{itemize}
\item[-] When $\Sigma(\kappa,\mu)>1$, let $c$ be the solution to the characteristic function~(equation cha of the paper). 
\item[-] When $\Sigma(\kappa,\mu)<1$, set $c=\mu$. 
\end{itemize}
Then $h(k)$ is given by
\begin{equation}
    h(k)=\tau(k)\prod_{s\in{\mathcal S}}\frac{(e^{-(\kappa c)_s}c_s)^{k_s}}{k_s!}.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, the following properities hold for $\{h(k)\}$:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
    \item Total mass:
    \begin{equation}
