{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.363250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cb840ceb8eb506c7facdae7a1f4da6f093e9cb305fc5ba1e27640c9a766423c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:bound_controlled_flow of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] There exist constants $C=C(H_-,\| \sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^2})$ and $q=q(H_-)$  such that for all $s \in [0, 1]$, $x \in {\mathbb{R}}^d$,  we have 
