	Furthermore, if $H \in C_c^1(\mathbb{R})$, the role of $C$ is fulfilled by some constant $C(H)$ satisfying \eqref{Cinvshift}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.574772+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ce22f486a5e1a8e213939eb96971cca7bf1de4bf84e62e637413246f617ab19","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 52 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:rand_sc_eq}, let $B_1,B_2\in\C^{L\times L}$ be deterministic matrices with $\|B_1\|+\|B_2\|\lesssim1$. Uniformly for deterministic vectors $\bbx\in\C^L$,
        \begin{align}
                \sum_{a=1}^{L}\abs{(B_1GB_2)_{a\bbx}}^2 & \prec\frac{\vphi+\eta}{\eta}\|\bbx\|^2,\qquad \max_{1\leq a\leq L}\abs{(B_1GB_2)_{a\bbx}}\prec(1+\phi)\|\bbx\|, \nonumber \\
                \sum_{a=1}^{L}\abs{(B_1GB_2)_{a\bbx}}^4 & \prec(1+\phi)^2\frac{\vphi+\eta}{\eta}\|\bbx\|^4. \nonumber
