{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.499222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d08a511acad783b34c8d729013c377daa12780a6602f9b63bd4543ac64f2fa2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] Let \(N\geq1\).  If \(P\) is a polynomial of degree \(d\) and \(t\in\C\),
its polynomial heat flow at scale \(N\) is defined by
\begin{equation}
