{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.818401+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dee0367d141a3dc2fae79dd79b770ea563a8604400b6d0c4a50c450b359903c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:stable-suspended-chart of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] Uniformly in the prime tuple,
\begin{equation}
 |\mathcal P_h(\boldsymbol\ell)|\gg_t h^4.
\end{equation}
Every $A_t$ in (equation eq:iterated-prime-suspension of the paper) is a primitive
$(4+t)$-set with
