{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.934135+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9df86f21d92e9bf5c7d3c2bc0aaa9c89a52b4f50920179b26f7197c09f639457","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cor:almost_legendre of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $\Lambda$. Let $w_1,\dots,w_D$ be periodic edge weights satisfying (equation eq:gauge_change_loop of the paper) for contractible loops, and suppose that $s=\sum_{i=1}^D p_i e_i$, where $p_i = \frac{w_i}{w_1+\dots+w_D}$. Then the surface tension is minus the entropy of $\mu_{n,N,w}$, i.e.,
