{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:29:27.959441+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9dfe928b90ad4c29c1991e23c89a9b104f7cb7a557c4cec9edf31403b5ec0bce","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2608.24675, 'Towards Liouville Quantum Gravity on fractals'] Let $|\gamma|< \sqrt{d_H/C_0}$. For any $w\in\{1,2,3\}^n$, $n\geq 1$, the LQG measures $\nu^\gamma$ and $\nu_{w}^\gamma$ satisfy
