{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.852629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e504878a9b6db0dc741f7b7508a3b3d422baac05bbd16d72741edb88f58b37a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition e:QalphaY of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting and $Y=(N,\Lambda)$. The generator of  $Y$ is given by

