{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.542085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e7ec6a44bb11272382ad44089a939aad6c7e1e55572c34f97e7ae2fb8d2a3bc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:week_converence of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] Let~$(u_{s,j}^t)_{1\leq s\leq t\leq 2\ell N}$ be the interlacing particles system defined in Definition~(def:marked_interlacing of the paper), and let~$\tau $ and~$\sigma^2$ be defined in~(equation eq:turning_point of the paper) and~(equation eq:sigma_square of the paper). Then
\begin{equation}
\left(\frac{u_{s,j}^{t}-2N\tau }{2\sigma\sqrt{N}}\right)_{1\leq s\leq t}\to \left(\xi_{s,j}^t\right)_{1\leq s\leq t},
\end{equation}
in the sense of weak convergence as~$N\to \infty$, and~$(\xi_{s,j}^t)_{1\leq s\leq t}$ is the marked GUE-corners process with~$\theta$ given in~(equation eq:theta of the paper). That is, for any compactly supported continuous functions~$\varphi:\Lambda_{\{0,1\}}\to [0,1]$,
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to \infty}\mathbb{E}_{\operatorname{Int}}\left[\prod_v \left(1-\varphi\left(t_v,\frac{u_{s_v,j_v}^{t_v}-2 N\tau }{2\sigma \sqrt{N}},j_v\right)\right)\right]
=\mathbb{E}_{\operatorname{GUE}}^\theta\left[\prod_v (1-\varphi(t_v,\xi_{s_v,j_v}^{t_v},j_v))\right],
\end{equation}
where~$\mathbb{E}_{\operatorname{Int}}$ and~$\mathbb{E}_{\operatorname{GUE}}^\theta$ are expectations of~$\mathbb{P}_{\operatorname{Int}}$ and~$\mathbb{P}_{\operatorname{GUE}}^\theta$, respectively.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.231462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e81596ae3e93b6dc5e287a2bd47a87755f54b62840f40b490c9f88acfdb73e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Consider a family of $(N,k)$-periodic environments such that \eqref{eq:NonDegeneratedEnvironment} holds. For all $m_0>0$,  there exist constants $\theta_0,c,C>0$, depending only on $\mathfrak{a}$ and $m_0$, such that for all sites $v=(\np,m\np)$ with some $\theta\geq \theta_0$, $m=m(\np) \in [m_0,m_0^{-1}]$, and $\np=\np(\theta) \in \N$, which satisfy
 \begin{equation}
 \np \leq \theta^{-1}N^{3/2} , 
 \end{equation} and all $x \in [1,\theta^{2/3}]$, we get that for all $N$ large enough
\begin{equation}
\Pper\Big( \TF\big(\gper_{(0,0),v}\big) \geq x \np^{2/3} \Big) \leq C \exp(-c x) .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:21:45.350372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e8278ff643902d57054dd891bd4486ee56a8acadc46fd3d6e1fd4700b6d795d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 (Universality of persistence on Euclidean space \cite{univ_euclidean}) of arXiv:2607.27535, 'Universal topological statistics on \\ triangulated singular spaces'] Let $f: \RR^d \rightarrow \RR_{\ge 0}$ be a good density and let $\filt$ be either the Rips or \v Cech filtration. Then there exists a measure on $[1,\infty)$, denoted $\overline{\Pi}_{k,\filt, d}^\univstar$, such that the following holds independently of $f$:
