{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.714402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f23dd4b99e0dafc15180a41bc5001c56d8b9958978c1b169eb5d5ec5ef852c1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.18775, 'Limit Theorems for the Dynamical Foundation of the Fractional Brownian Motion and Related '] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space.  Let $\mathcal{X}$  be a separable metrizable topological space endowed with its Borel $\sigma$-field $\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{X})$. Let $\mathcal{G}\subset\mathcal{F}$ be a sub-$\sigma$-field. A sequence $(\xi_N)_{N\in\mathbb{N}}$ of $(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{X}))$-valued random elements is said to \emph{converge $\mathcal{G}$-mixing} to a (random element with) probability distribution $\nu$ on $\mathcal{X}$, if the conditional distributions $\mathcal{P}_{\xi_N|\mathcal{G}}$ converge weakly to $\nu$ as $N\to\infty$, i.e., if for every $f\in L^1(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})$ and every bounded continuous function $h$ on $\mathcal{X}$
		\begin{align*}
			\lim_{N\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[ f\mathbb{E}\left[h(\xi_N)|\mathcal{G}  \right] \right] =\mathbb{E}[f]\int_\mathcal{X} h d\nu.
