where $R\in \{R_{\sst I}, R_{\sst \Ical}\}$ and $H \in \{H_{\sst I}, H_{\sst \Ical}\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.358386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0254e82c2d91e95b9fcfed9f681d5b22c2fbb06a9c286a1e25fc6df002f2788","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 10 of arXiv:2506.18834, '\large\bf On the random-time and finite-time ruin probability for widely dependent claim s'] (1) Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{thm104} but without requiring condition (\ref{110}),
