{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:58:24.518185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a033c01dafe3638de962fbf40a29d4e8516cfb27b4e1134a5296eeac2f84cdf7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:pp.conv.star of arXiv:2601.12677, 'Stable and Fréchet limit theorem for subgraph functionals in the hyperbolic random geometr'] Assume $1/2<\alpha<k-1$; then, as $n\to\infty$, 
