{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.268275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a044504f6fff7f20fb30c1bd5602aa3bdc467dfb0eff853c16fc7b37437d2cf5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma S42L of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] Fix $p, \epsilon, \eta, M^{\mathsf{bot}}, M^{\mathsf{side}}, A^{\mathsf{sep}}, A^{\mathsf{gap}}\in (0, \infty)$, $\Delta^{\mathsf{gap}}  \in (0,1/2)$, $k \in \mathbb{N}$, $\sigma = \sqrt{p(1+p)}$. There exist $N_6 \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\delta > 0 $, depending on $p, \epsilon, \eta, M^{\mathsf{bot}}, M^{\mathsf{side}}, A^{\mathsf{sep}}, A^{\mathsf{gap}}, \Delta^{\mathsf{gap}}, k$, such that the following holds for all $n \geq N_6$. If we assume:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\vec{x}, \vec{y}\in \mathfrak{W}_k$ as in ((DefSig of the paper)), and $|x_i| \leq M^{\mathsf{side}} \cdot n^{1/2}$, $|y_i - pn| \leq M^{\mathsf{side}} \cdot n^{1/2}$ for $i \in \llbracket 1, k \rrbracket$;
\item $x_i - x_{i+1} \geq A^{\mathsf{sep}} \cdot n^{1/2}$ and $y_i - y_{i+1} \geq A^{\mathsf{sep}} \cdot n^{1/2}$ for $i \in \llbracket 1, k -1 \rrbracket$;
\item $g: \llbracket 0, n \rrbracket \rightarrow [-\infty, \infty)$ is such that $g(s) - ps\leq  M^{\mathsf{bot}} \cdot n^{1/2} $ for all $s \in \llbracket 0, n \rrbracket$;
\item $x_k \geq g(s) - ps + A^{\mathsf{gap}} \cdot n^{1/2} $ for all $s \in \llbracket 0, n\rrbracket$ with $s \leq \Delta^{\mathsf{gap}} \cdot n$;
\item $y_k -pn \geq g(s) - ps + A^{\mathsf{gap}} \cdot n^{1/2} $ for all $s \in \llbracket 0, n\rrbracket$ with $s \geq n - \Delta^{\mathsf{gap}} \cdot n$;
\item the set $\Omega_{\mathsf{Inter}}(0,n,\vec{x},\vec{y}, \infty, g)$ is non-empty;
\item for $Q_i \in \Omega(0,n, x,y)$, we set $\mathcal{Q}_i(t)= \sigma^{-1}n^{-1/2}(Q_i(tn) - ptn)$ for $t \in [0,1]$;
\end{itemize}
then the following inequality holds for each $i \in \llbracket 1, k \rrbracket$
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}_{\mathsf{Inter}, \operatorname{Geom}}^{0, n, \vec{x}, \vec{y}, \infty, g}\left( w(\mathcal{Q}_i, \delta) > \epsilon \right) < \eta.
\end{equation}
We recall that $w(f,\delta)$ is the modulus of continuity from ((S33E1 of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:06:55.288960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0473961ae74cd12c29c7d8da553abe7faf3136d9a9d00900941ba566786e4b0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:cLSI of arXiv:2602.17579, 'Non-equilibrium functional inequalities for finite Markov chains'] The \emph{log-Sobolev inequality (LSI)} is satisfied if there exists a constant $\alpha > 0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\forall \varphi\in \mathcal D_\pi(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}}): \ \ \mathscr{H}_\pi(\varphi)\leq  \frac{1}{\alpha} \mathscr{R}_\pi(\varphi,M).
\end{equation}
The supremum over all possible choices of $\alpha$ is called the \emph{log-Sobolev constant}. We denote it by
\begin{equation}
    \alpha_{\LSI}(M) \coloneqq \inf_{\substack{\varphi\in \mathcal D_\pi(\ensuremath{\mathbb{Z}})\\\varphi\neq \1}}\frac{\mathscr{R}_\pi(\varphi,M)}{\mathscr{H}_\pi(\varphi)}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.753739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a04a7709541a78e9e011ca6ff781d79330c9a0959c568574f2bcb0f9086c4297","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop PropISDEGL of arXiv:2605.06429, '\large \bf $\mathsf{GL}_N(\mathbb{C})$ BROWNIAN MOTION AND STOCHASTIC PDE ON ENTIRE FUNCTI'] For any $\gamma\ge \sum_{i=1}^\infty x_i$, whenever $(x_i)_{i\in \mathbb{N}}\in \mathbf{W}_{\infty;+}^\circ$, the projection of $\mathbf{X}_{GL}^\bullet$ on the $(\mathsf{x}_i(\bullet))_{i\in \mathbb{N}}$ solves the infinite system of SDE
\begin{equation*}
\mathsf{x}_i(t)= x_i+\int_0^t\mathsf{x}_i(s)\mathrm{d}\mathsf{w}_i(s) + \frac{\theta}{2}\int_0^t\mathsf{x}_i(s)\mathrm{d}s
 +\int_0^t\sum_{j=1,j\neq i}^{\infty}\frac{\mathsf{x}_i(s)\mathsf{x}_j(s)}{\mathsf{x}_i(s)-\mathsf{x}_j(s)}\mathrm{d}s, \  \forall t\ge 0 , \   i \in \mathbb{N},
 \end{equation*}
with independent standard Brownian motions $(\mathsf{w}_i)_{i\in \mathbb{N}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.790507+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a04c9c5f869bd45a1e60e3661da3167ec592e39f709f2631d2ae922a838b66db","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2609.00183, '2609.00183'] Let $u$ be a harmonic map to an $N$-dimensional conical DM-complex $Y_C$ with splitting $u=(V,v):B_{\sigma_j}(0) \to (\mathbb{R}^j \times Y_C^{N-j},d_G)$ satisfying $\Ord_{\phi,v}(0,R_0)\leq \Lambda$ and $\sup_{B_{\sigma_j}(0)}|\nabla u| \leq M$, then there exists $\eta_1>0$ and $\calA\geq 1$, depending only on $\Lambda$, $n$, $M$, and the constant in \cite[(29)--(33)]{dm}, such that for $\sigma\in (0,\eta_1]$ and $\eta\in (0,\eta_1]$, if for $x\in B_{R_0/64}(0)$ there exists a homogeneous Lipschitz map $h:B_{\sigma}(x)\to Y_C$ such that
