     \end{equation*}
     then $\alpha\leq \calA$, where $\alpha$ is the degree of $h$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.763830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05821f529ce72ebf53f1ad837e703c5a5d11543aff70aaf4ff1980ab290a127","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 (Well-posedness of RDEs) of arXiv:2512.04646, '\textbf{Canonical Rough Path over Tempered Fractional Brownian Motion: Existence, Construc'] Let $H > 1/4$, $\lambda > 0$,
