{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.363511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a08d99a82a59302a8b2f8aa2806a0f8e99d7377a685a62beb09bb340fec16faa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Prop:sta-ini of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $(\phi_{t}^{s,x})_{t\in[s,1]}$ be given by (equation eq:flow-def of the paper), let X be a solution to the SDE (equation eq:main of the paper). Then, for any $p \geq 1$ there exists a constant $C=C( H_-, p, C_{D,p}^X, C_{S,2p}^X, \|\sigma\|_{\mathcal{C}^2}) $, such that for all $(s,t) \in [0, 1]^2_{\leq}$ we have 
