{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.877890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0903b43f476d36ec50eb18b1f21a6c0de23c559cccdb7ebcd71c913cc72c28e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 17 (Barraquand) of arXiv:2607.17030, 'Stationary measures for log-gamma polymer on a strip and in half-space'] Fix $\alpha,u,v>0$ and $0=m_0<m_1<\dots<m_d=N$. Let $u>t_1>\dots>t_d>-\min\{\alpha,v\}$. Then we have the
