{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.308692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0cc38782b2feb9d5e0e23b8782444264f0117044a7666428fb5d1ad699f2d5a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 (Tropp, Chretien \& Darses) of arXiv:2606.24323, 'Conditioning of incoherent sub-dictionaries sampled from a coherent dictionary'] Let $\hat \P$ be a (discrete) probability measure on $\Delta$, $I$ the set-valued random variable with $I(\delta) = \{i:\delta_i=1\}$ and $\hol \in \R^{K\times K}$ a matrix with zero diagonal, then there exists a subset $T\subseteq [K]$, such that for all $\theta \in \R$
