{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.065506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0f667bba0d65146ebe9b96169192e720cf5ac92f2162fcaa2b2be27930085e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 27 of arXiv:2606.27078, 'Semimartingale Optimal Transport with Jumps: A General Framework and Equivalent Formulatio'] Assume $\mu_0=\delta_1$ and that $\mu_1\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ has finite first moments.  Set $L(t,\omega,b,c,F)=G(\omega)$, where $G:\Omega\to[0,+\infty)$ is lower semicontinuous. Let
