{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.588813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1153d0e1a3a46dd38f5e66a81726e8937c60c45ac71666cab63bb46ac5532c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 607 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p \geq 1$ and $\beta >0$,  there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $t\geq 0$ and $0\leq t_1<t_2\leq t$,
