{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.834909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a143c13755a5a82a4bea8f37c35ebdb9f328618306ff48988f50ab4259085fd4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp 2 of arXiv:2506.12755, '{\bf Stochastic intrinsic gradient flows on the Wasserstein space}\footnote{Supported in p'] Assume $(C_1)$. Let $\Lam$ be as in \eqref{eq:Lam}, $\gamma:\RR^d\times\scr P\to (0,\infty)$ be measurable such that $c^{-1}\leq\gamma(\cdot,\cdot)\leq c$
	for some constant $c\in(0,\infty)$ and $\Gamma$ be as in \eqref{eq:Gammadef}.


	(i) The bilinear form $(\EE^{\gamma,\Lam},C_b^1(\scr P_p))$, defined 
	\begin{equation*}\EE^{\gamma,\Lam}(u,v):=\int_{\scr P_p}\Gamma(u,v)(\mu)\LL(\d\mu),\qquad u,v\in C_b^1(\scr P_p),
	\end{equation*} 
	has a closed extension in $L^2(\scr P_p,\LL)$. Its minimal closed extension yields a quasi-regular, strongly local Dirichlet form $(\EE^{\gamma,\Lam},\D(\EE^{\gamma,\Lam}))$.
	In particular, there exists a non-terminating diffusion $(\Omega, \scr F,$ $(\mu_t)_{t\geq 0}, (\P^\mu)_{\mu\in \scr P_p})$ on $\scr P_p$ which is associated with $\EE^{\gamma,\Lam}$.

	(ii) There exist $\phi_{\mu,k}\in L^2(\RR^d\to\RR^d,\mu)$, $k=\N$, $\mu\in\scr P_p$, such that $D_{\phi_{\mu,k}}u:\scr P_p\to\RR$ is measurable for $u\in C_b^1(\scr P_p)$ and 
	\begin{equation*}
		\Gamma(u,v)(\mu)=\sum_{k=1}^\infty D_{\gamma_\mu\phi_{\mu,k}} u(\mu)D_{\phi_{\mu,k}}v(\mu)
	\end{equation*}
	for $\Lam$-a.e.~$\mu\in\scr P_p,$ $u,v\in C_b^1(\scr P_p)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.314015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1463be6dbeddb9f5964802e8a77420b211612bbbdcee5dbc311f80f7b1cb651","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:exp_est of arXiv:2606.00325, 'Ergodicity for a class of stochastic Hasegawa-Mima equations with dissipation'] Let $\phi$ be a solution of (equation eq:main of the paper) in the sense of (def-sol-H1 of the paper), then the following exponential bound holds
