same $x$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.850374+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1520c3b5f6bb0d9100f4929af8aa59b17ed3c7dd6461857399315f2c9927f47","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 29 of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] Let $A,~ B \in  \mathcal{M}_{n}(\mathbb{R})$  be symmetric and let $S \in  M_{n,m}$. Then

\begin{enumerate}
\item  if $A \geqm B$, then $S^\top AS \geqm  S^\top BS$;
\item  if $\rank S = m$, then $A \gm B$ implies $S^\top AS \gm  S^\top BS$
\item if $m = n$ and $S \in M_n$ is nonsingular, then $A \gm B $ if and only if $S^\top AS \gm  S^\top BS$;
									$A \geqm B $  if and only if $S^\top AS \geqm  S^\top BS$;
\item  $I_m \gm S^\top S$ (respectively, $I_n\gm SS^\top$) if and only if $S$ is a strict contraction; $I_m \geqm S^\top S$ (respectively, $I_n\geqm SS^\top$) if and only if $S$ is a  contraction;

										\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

