    In particular, $A_n-\widetilde{A_n}\to0$, as $n \to \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.087590+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1664461db97cc487eff005d57bffa39d4b220108eb40a868f01f800fbb51881","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 25 of arXiv:2607.13849, 'Rearranged Stochastic Heat Equation with an Entropy Gradient Structure'] For $T>0$ and $\delta >0$, let $(X_t, W_t)_{0 \le t \le T}$ be a weak limit in $\mathbb{D}([0,T], \mathcal{H}^{-1}_{\mathrm{Sym}}(\mathbb{S})\times L^2_{\mathrm{Sym}}(\mathbb{S})
    )$ of the family $\{(X_t^{(h)},W_t)_{0 \le t \le T}\}_{{h \in T/{\mathbb N}^*}}$ when $h\searrow 0$. Then, almost surely, the following equation holds in a weak sense:
\begin{align}
\mathrm{d}X_t(\mathbf{x}) = -\frac{1}{2}D_{\mathbf{x}}\Big(\frac{1}{D_{\mathbf{x}}X_t(\mathbf{x})}\Big)\mathrm{d}t + \Delta_{\mathbf{x}} X_t(\mathbf{x})\mathrm{d}t +\mathrm{d}\nu_t(\mathbf{x}) + \mathrm{d}W_t(\mathbf{x}), \quad \forall \mathbf{x}\in \mathbb{S}, \ t \in  [0,T], 
\end{align}
where $(\nu_t)_{0 \le t \le T}$ stands for a process with values in ${\mathcal H}^{-2}_{\rm Sym}({\mathbb S})$ that is non-decreasing in the sense that, for any function $\varphi \in {\mathcal H}_{\rm Sym}^2({\mathbb S})$, 
$(\langle \varphi,\nu_t\rangle)_{0 \le t \le T}$ is non-decreasing. Moreover, for all $t \in [0,T]$,
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{\epsilon \searrow 0}
\mathbb{E}\int_{0}^{t} \mathrm{e}^{\epsilon \Delta}  X_r\cdot\mathrm{d}{\nu}_r =0,
\quad 
\lim_{\epsilon \searrow 0}
\mathbb{E} \biggl[ \biggl\vert \int_{0}^{t} \int_{\mathbb S} \frac{ \mathrm{e}^{\epsilon \Delta} 
D_{\mathbf{x}} X_r({\mathbf x})}{D_{\mathbf{x}} X_r({\mathbf x})} \mathrm{d}{\mathbf x} - t
\biggr\vert \biggr]=0.
\end{equation*}

In addition, the process $(X_t)_{0 \le t \le T}$ has time-continuous trajectories with respect to the norm $\|\cdot\|_2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.856804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a173aca04a6ee6bc0051da898125b86499a5bd4a64a029bbf76b18c12c37faa2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:independence of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] Let $x\in (0,1)$. Then it holds that $\beta_x$ and $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}$ (as introduced in Definition (def:l_and_bb_pin of the paper)) are independent. Further, the integration formula
    \begin{align}
    	\mathbb{E}\left[ F(\beta) \psi (\beta_x) \right]
    	&= \int_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{E}\left[ F(\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}+y l^x)\right] \psi (y) \, \mathcal{N}(0,x(1-x))(dy) \nonumber\\
    	&= \int_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{E}\left[ F(\beta+(y-\beta_x) l^x)\right] \psi (y) \, \mathcal{N}(0,x(1-x))(dy)
