{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.325077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a18d1b964bb80e55f523a1912d2eeef3bf9f110b3d89e1c81983785c7cfa75f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:summed-cut-kernel of arXiv:2609.03532, 'Airy limit for the Jack process and topological expansion'] There are constants $C,c>0$ such that, uniformly in
$L\in\mathbb Z_{\geq0}$ and $d\in\mathbb Z_{\geq1}$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal K_L^\pm(d)
  \leq \frac{C}{(L+1)^{1/2}}
       \exp\!\left\{-\frac{c d^2}{L+d+1}\right\}.

\end{equation}
Expanding the two partition functions in each summand into paths, and let
$\mathcal K_{L,\geq R}^\pm(d)$ denote the restriction to pairs of raw
walks $(W^{\mathrm l},W^{\mathrm r})$ satisfying
\[
  \max\{\max W^{\mathrm l},\max W^{\mathrm r}\}\geq R.
\]
Then uniformly in $R\geq0$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal K_{L,\geq R}^\pm(d)
  \leq\frac{C}{(L+1)^{1/2}}
  \exp\!\left\{-c\left(
    \frac{d^2}{L+d+1}+\frac{R^2}{L+d+R+1}
  \right)\right\}.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.781007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1a0bc870339113c803157c0345e5bacd0038a3185f7a7782f8270639f8db889","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tailrl-harmonic-decomposition of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] The TailRL{} objective decomposes as
