{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.240814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1ab1225d5dcee6a3bdcfaaf75a6fade22a1930fd1afeaefa365b6b521ef5eef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cty12pn of arXiv:2507.02518, '{\bf Exponential Ergodicity in Relative Entropy and $L^2$-Wasserstein Distance for non-equ'] Assume {\bf (C)}.
There exist  $K_*,c,\tilde c,\lambda>0$, depending on $d$ and on the constants in {\bf (C)} except on $K_I$, such that, provided $K_I\leqslant K_*$  then, for all $N\geqslant 1$,  (equation Degthp of the paper) has a unique invariant probability measure $\bar{\mu}^N\in\mathscr P_2((\mathbb R^{2d})^N)$,
\begin{align}\mathbb W_2((P_t^N)^\ast\nu^N,\bar{\mu}^N)^2\leq c\text{\rm{e}}^{-2 \lambda t}\mathbb W_2(\nu^N,\bar{\mu}^N)^2+cNR_{d}(N),\ \ t\geq 0, \nu^N\in\mathscr P_2((\mathbb R^{2d})^N),
\end{align}
and

\begin{align} \mathrm{Ent}((P_t^N)^\ast\nu^N|\bar{\mu}^N)\leq \tilde c\text{\rm{e}}^{-\lambda t}\mathbb W_2(\nu^N,\bar{\mu}^N)^2+cNR_{d}(N),~ t\geq 1, \nu^N\in\mathscr P_2((\mathbb R^{2d})^N)
\end{align}
where
\begin{equation*}\begin{split}
R_{d}(N)=
