for $n$ large enough uniformly over
$N\in\mathbb{N}_0$, partitions $\{t_1,\dots, t_N\}$,  and $k=0, \dots, N$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:29.002582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1f2b4934c8cf612a7c33c09129f7713e395bc5119b10ff57525ddf0eb07fa83","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop gen supp of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] Define
