{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.298017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a319b3bc2614181f5b62380923d24b25611775797a880bf9117c08d8b4885263","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.23242, 'Correction to ``The stepping stone model in a random environment'' - limit theorems for th'] As $ n \to \infty $, for $ \mu $-almost every $ \omega \in \Omega $, $ (L_n(t), t \in [0,T]) $ converges in probability to $ ( \gamma L^0_t(X^1-X^2), t \in [0,T]) $ in the Skorokhod topology, where $ L^0_t(X^1-X^2) $ is the local time at zero of $ X^1-X^2 $ and $ \gamma $ is given by
