{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:51:33.324950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a319f7a3c08bbb62bbb4f06efe917e0b455000392b37f13a2f9accf10333bff9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop equiv-sp-compact-gen of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] The stable $\infty$-category ${\mathfrak S\kern-.5pt\mathfrak p}_G$ is compactly generated by the collection of suspension spectra $\Sigma^\infty G/H_+$ for all closed subgroups $H\subset G$. In particular, it is presentable.
