{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.408061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a32685ba1ec508d34a1b59257b39f9fa088976627a047a3142003a94e9f6d885","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop twistgroup of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] The group $G_m^{tw}$ is free on $Y = x_{2m+4}$, $H = x_2(x_{m+4}^{-1}x_{m+3})^m$. Killing the trivial-strand meridian gives the quotient
\begin{equation*}
	Q_m^{tw} = \langle a, b \mid w^ma = bw^m \rangle \ \ \ \ \ w = ba^{-1}b^{-1}a
\end{equation*}
In the conventions of [hosteshanahan], this is the fundamental group of the twist knot complement $K_{2m}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.778729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3349de9db68d67f64ff96fbab1df77a2fd4fcb1a11586939ffdbabf1ce8599e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:decode of arXiv:2608.01253, 'The pseudo-quantum representation of \\finite reversible Markov chains'] Let $Q$ be a finite irreducible reversible generator, with all objects defined from
