{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:18:54.363918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a376ac37ff3411d75eae180f579fc4fc4dfc6ebc137c5c67b4ffca9fb6a46c34","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] Given $A\in M_N(\mathbb C)$, define its adjoint matrix by $(A^*)_{ij}=\bar{A}_{ji}$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item $<Ax,y>=<x,A^*y>$, for any two vectors $x,y\in\mathbb C^N$.

\item $x\to Ux$ with $U\in M_N(\mathbb C)$ is an isometry precisely when $U^*=U^{-1}$.

\item $x\to Px$ with $P\in M_N(\mathbb C)$ is a projection precisely when $P^2=P^*=P$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.039429+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a377f46c77e0cd0560b0bb296c3d8f50ae857f373e8a78bb5bb17f4e5134a5eb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 (Existence of the limiting invariant measure) of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Let $(V,E,r_N)$ be a strongly connected weighted graph satisfying Assumption \ref{FRL}.
