{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.663992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3936a7d1437b4cc3f668f7dd8213e704ceec7d81b9958294ec20978e0ea6948","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm hop-count-asymptotics of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Assume that the edge weights satisfy Assumption~(ass:weight of the paper).
\begin{enumeratea}
\item  \textup{(Mesoscopic law of large numbers)}
Assume that $1 \ll \ell \ll n/\log n$. Let $H_n^{(\ell)}(0,\mathsf{u}_n)$ denote the number of edges in the a.s.\ unique geodesic realising $T_n^{(\ell)}(0,\mathsf{u}_n)$. Then, for fixed $\mathsf{u}\in(0,1/2)$, we have
\begin{align}
 \frac{\ell}{\mathsf{u}_n} H_n^{(\ell)}(0,\mathsf{u}_n) \stackrel{\pr}{\to} \frac{\beta_{\mathsf{c}}}{\theta}
 \text{ and }
 \frac{\ell}{\mathsf{u}_n} \E H_n^{(\ell)}(0,\mathsf{u}_n)
 \to \frac{\beta_{\mathsf{c}}}{\theta} \text{ as } n\to\infty,
\end{align}
where $\beta_{\mathsf{c}}$ is the constant defined in~(equation eq:beta_c of the paper).

\item  \textup{(Macroscopic law of large numbers)}
Assume that $\ell/n\to\gl\in(0,1/2)$. Let $U_n$ be chosen uniformly from $\mathds{T}_n\setminus\{0\}$ and let $H_n^{(\ell)}(0,U_n)$ be the number of edges in the geodesic from $0$ to $U_n$. Then
\begin{align}
 \frac{H_n^{(\ell)}(0,U_n)}{\log n}
 \stackrel{\pr}{\to}\frac1\theta ,
 \text{ and }
 \frac{\E H_n^{(\ell)}(0,U_n)}{\log n} \to \frac{1}{\theta} \text{ as } n\to\infty.
\end{align}
\end{enumeratea} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.979831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3979c5b151f1a7f69de080ad154f0f8f3de987bd51b749bb7220c0ea49238bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm hypergraphr of arXiv:2412.00610, 'Joint Poisson Convergence of Monochromatic Hyperedges in Multiplex Hypergraphs'] Fix an integer $r \geq 2$ and consider a sequence $\bm H_n = (H_n^{(1)}, H_n^{(2)})$ of 2-hypermultiplexes, where both $H_n^{(1)}$ and $H_n^{(2)}$ are $r$-uniform. Suppose the vertices of $\bm H_n$ are colored uniformly at random with $c_n$ colors, such that the following hold: 
\begin{align} 
\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \bE [ \bm T(\bm H_n) ] = \begin{pmatrix}
  \lambda_1 \\ 
  \lambda_2
  \end{pmatrix} \quad \text{ and } \quad \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \mathrm{Var}[ \bm T(\bm H_n) ] = \begin{pmatrix}
