{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.889534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a40414d4d6f8abc8e1c980c344b2d22141da94f0f8be082fda0902d72311413a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ultrahot of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] Assume $\beta = o(1)$. Then there exist universal constants $C, c > 0$ such that, for all $\epsilon \in (0,1)$,
