{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.354653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a415e37c055d14a20927e17cd3ee12b907571e2298245cd6d9c1852e8e6bb3cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.dpiconstant of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Suppose that $p > 4$, $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$ is any probability space, $t_0 \in [0,1)$, $X_0 \in L^p(\Omega)$, $\widebar\alpha \in L^{\infty}(\Omega)$ with $\|\widebar\alpha\|_2 \leq c_0$, and $h \in (0,1-t_0)$. Then
