{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.297691+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a45ef83694813cc7a234f89307aea57ee6d7d60a89809b0e1189f97d0cf5fe38","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:def_attention of arXiv:2609.03129, 'A Closed-Form Formula for Consistent Lipschitz Regression on Metric Spaces with Sparse Neu'] Let $\lambda>0$, and let $d_{\rm in},d_{{\rm key}},d_{\rm out},N\in \mathbb N$. 
Let
${\bf Q},{\bf K}\in \mathbb{R}^{d_{{\rm key}}\times d_{\rm in}}$
and
${\bf V}\in \mathbb{R}^{d_{\rm out}\times d_{\rm in}}$. 
We define the associated attention mechanism
$\operatorname{Attn}(\cdot|{\bf Q},{\bf K},{\bf V},\lambda):\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{\rm in}}\to \mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{\rm out}}
$
by
\begin{equation} 
    [\operatorname{Attn}(\mathbf{X}|{\bf Q},{\bf K},{\bf V},\lambda)]_n
    \ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}} 
    \sum_{m=1}^N
    \frac{e^{\lambda \langle {\bf Q}[\mathbf{X}]_n, {\bf K}[\mathbf{X}]_m\rangle/\sqrt{d_{{\rm key}}}}}{
    \sum_{l=1}^N e^{\lambda \langle {\bf Q}[\mathbf{X}]_n, {\bf K}[\mathbf{X}]_l \rangle/\sqrt{d_{{\rm key}}}}}
    {\bf V}[\mathbf{X}]_m, \qquad n=1,\dots,N.
\end{equation}
Here $[\mathbf{X}]_j \in \mathbb{R}^{d_{\rm in}}$ denotes the $j$th row of $\mathbf{X}$, interpreted as a column vector when multiplied by ${\bf Q},{\bf K},{\bf V}$.

A transformer network operates by iterating layers, each consisting of a row-wise activation–bias map followed by an attention mechanism.
Concretely, let $d,D,L\in\mathbb{N}$, and let $d_0,d_1,\dots,d_L, H_0,H_1,\dots,H_L\in\mathbb{N}$ such that $d_0=d$ and $d_L=D$.
For $j=0,1,\dots,L-2$ and $\mathtt{h}=1,\dots,H_j$, let $d^{(j)}_{{\rm key}, \mathtt{h}}, d^{(j)}_{{\rm value}, \mathtt{h}}\in\mathbb{N}$ such that $d_{j+1} = \sum_{{\mathtt{h}}=1}^{H_j} d^{(j)}_{{\rm value}, \mathtt{h}}$.
A $j$th \emph{transformer layer with Multi-head attention}, for $j=0,1,\dots,L-2$, is a map
$
\mathcal{T}_j:\mathbb{R}^{N\times d_j}\to \mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{j+1}}
$
that sends an input matrix $\mathbf{X}^{(j)}\in \mathbb{R}^{N\times d_j}$ to
$
\mathcal{T}_j(\mathbf{X}^{(j)})\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}  \mathbf{X}^{(j+1)}\in \mathbb{R}^{N\times d_{j+1}},
$
where 
\begin{alignat}{2} 
    \nonumber \mathbf{Z}^{(j)}
    &\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}} 
    \underbrace{
        \bigoplus_{\mathtt{h}=1}^{H_j}
            \operatorname{Attn}\big(
                \mathbf{X}^{(j)}
                |{\bf Q}_{\mathtt{h}}^{(j)},{\bf K}_{\mathtt{h}}^{(j)},{\bf V}_{\mathtt{h}}^{(j)},\lambda
            \big)
    }_{\text{Multi-head attention}} && \\
     [\mathbf{X}^{(j+1)}]_n
    &\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}}  

        \sigma\bullet
        \big(
            [\mathbf{Z}^{(j)}]_n + b^{(j)}
        \big),

    &&\qquad n=1,\dots,N.
\end{alignat}
Here $\bigoplus$ denotes concatenation along the second (column) dimension, $
{\bf Q}_{\mathtt{h}}^{(j)},{\bf K}_{\mathtt{h}}^{(j)}\in \mathbb{R}^{d_{{\rm key}, \mathtt{h}}^{(j)}\times d_j}$ and 
$
{\bf V}_{\mathtt{h}}^{(j)}\in \mathbb{R}^{d_{{\rm value}, \mathtt{h}}^{(j)}\times d_j}$, and $b^{(j)}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{j+1}}$.
Further, the addition in (equation eq:representation_transformer of the paper) is applied row-wise.
A \emph{transformer with Multi-head attention} with depth $L$, obtained by composing the layers $\mathcal{T}_0,\mathcal{T}_1,\dots,\mathcal{T}_{L-2}$, is a map $\mathcal{T}:\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}\to\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}$ sending an input matrix ${\bf X}^{(0)}\ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}} {\bf X}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times d}$ to $\mathcal{T}({\bf X}) \ensuremath{\stackrel{\mbox{\upshape\tiny def.}}{=}} {\bf A}^{(L-1)}{\bf X}^{(L-1)} + b^{(L-1)}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}$, for some ${\bf A}^{(L-1)}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times d_{L-1}}$ and $b^{(L-1)}\in\mathbb{R}^D$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.363218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a45f2d5bc3008b55840793465d19896b2e08b3396c5b5ffbea63d62b0aac1026","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 (Joint distribution of descents, valleys, and cycle type) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] For $t\in (0, 1)$, as a formal power series in $u$, one has
\begin{align}
&\frac{t}{1-t}+\sum_{n\ge1}u^n\sum_{\pi\in S_n}\frac{t^{\vl(\pi)+1}}{p^n(1-t)^{n+1}}(p+qt)^{\asc(\pi)-\vl(\pi)}
(q+pt)^{\des(\pi)-\vl(\pi)}X(\pi;\x)

