{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.640465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5e832b71df86a361028d7b2b5ee90c212b39d31b851d51b9d125fee0aa7008b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary BE2-cor of arXiv:2411.13788, '\bf Gradient bounds and Liouville property for a class of hypoelliptic diffusion via coupl'] Let $f\in C^1\left(\mathbb{R}^{m_0}\times\mathbb{R}^{m_1}\right)$ be a  globally Lipschitz function. Then for any $t\ge0$, $x^{(1)}\in \mathbb{R}^{m_0}, x^{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{m_1}$, we have
