{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.644992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a657a76be598f67777bd69d3dc1a5b17b6f4ed1fbfd86f1204242b7a390cdd64","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bridge_subg_tail of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $(B^{(n),x}_t;0\leq t \leq n)$ be a \textcolor{green!50!black}{uniform bridge} of length $n$ ending at $x$, and for fixed $C>0$, define the functional
