{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.358318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a65bcd60eee81ffde849d79b7d7cb361a27808e01f2704fc8b6ffe62c5d6bea0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_solution of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] An $\mathbb{F}$-adapted  stochastic process $(X_t)_{t \in [0, 1]}$ is called a solution of (equation eq:main of the paper) if the following are satisfied:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
