{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.185284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7053e273816286895b7c98bd660a84293a2269e7e904fcf5419d02548c9fb5d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:RandomWalkBound of arXiv:2511.10630, 'Cutoff for generalised Bernoulli--Laplace urn models'] Let $\alpha > 0$ be a constant and let $N \in \mathbb{N}$ with $N/2 \geqslant \alpha$. Let $(Z_t)_{t \geqslant 0}$ be a rate $1$ simple random walk on $[N]$ with a bias of $\alpha/N$ to the right with reflection, i.e., 
    \begin{equation*}
        \cP{Z_t = y}{Z_{t_{-}} = x} = \begin{cases}
            \frac{1}{2} + \frac{\alpha}{N} & \text{ if } y = x + 1 \text{ and } x < N \text{ or } x = y = N,  \\
            \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\alpha}{N} & \text{ if } y = x - 1 \text{ and } x > 1 \text{ or } x = y = 1, 
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation*}
    for all $x \in [N]$, for a jump at time $t$. For $x \in [N]$, let $\tau_{x}$ denote the first time when the walker $(Z_t)$ reaches site $x$. Then there exists some universal constants $c_0, \varepsilon_0 > 0$ such that for all $\varepsilon \in (0, \varepsilon_0)$,
    \begin{equation}
        \cP{\tau_N \leqslant \varepsilon N^2/\alpha}{Z_0 = 1} \leqslant \Exp{-c_0 \alpha \varepsilon^{-1}}
    \end{equation}
    for all $N$ sufficiently large.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.334170+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a707995996502302d23c013d779b220910ec991e479dcd22e7410fa7c234ebb0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a locally finite weighted graph satisfying the $CD\psi\left(n,-K\right)$ condition with $K\geq0$, where $\psi\in C^{1}\left(0,+\infty\right)$ is a concave function with $\psi^\prime \left(1\right)>0,\ H_{\psi}<\infty$ and $\limsup _{\lambda \downarrow 0}\frac{\eta_{\psi}(\lambda)}{\lambda^{2}}<\infty $. Then there exist positive constants $c,C$ depending only on $n,\psi,D_\mu,\mu_{\max}, w_{\min}$ such that for any $x\in V$ and any $r>0$,
