{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.080219+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a707ac9620581ad95a8e0e812e8b9ae301f41593758809e348b1d3bac40274f6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 of arXiv:2608.19832, 'Sharp Convex Concentration for Symmetric Random Tensors with Subgaussian Coordinates'] There are absolute constants $K_0,c,C>0$ such that the following holds.
