{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.337928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a71817b9f56b5038f8d61672f02cd37948623448cc38d1fddb79c5327d5c8099","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 2 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] The generator $L=L_0+L_1$ of the process $\eta_t$, determined by 
\eqref{eq:eta_t-pert-2}, is given by
\begin{align*} 
L_0 & = \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( \partial_{\eta(x)}^2 - \partial_{\eta(x)}\partial_{\eta(x-1)}
\big)  + \frac12 \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( V'(\eta(x+1)) -2V'(\eta(x))+ V'(\eta(x-1)) \big) \partial_{\eta(x)} \\
& = \frac12 \sum_{x\in \T_N} 
\Big( \big( \partial_{\eta(x)} - \partial_{\eta(x-1)} \big)^2
- \big( V'(\eta(x)) - V'(\eta(x-1)) \big)
