{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.292163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a72576b4d6ca869439d64c35f93d9b22698c4ed7d203f34a8f38655285e6b91f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:beta of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Fix a (small) $c_0>0$ and a (large) $L>0$. For $w_j=\pm\mathrm{i}\eta_j$ it holds that
