{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.430332+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a77451d81261c24f523352d5c3a534e4bbce087fe15941be82bc5ea826e8b2a6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:gaussian.multicausal.optimizer of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] For centered filtered Gaussian processes $\mathbb{X}^1 = \mathbb{G}^{L^1},\dots,\mathbb{X}^K = \mathbb{G}^{L^K}\in\mathcal{FG}(T,d)$, the following statements hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item The barycenter value is given by
\[
\inf_{\mathbb{Y}\in\mathrm{FP}_2}\sum_{k=1}^K \lambda_k\mathcal{AW}_2^2(\mathbb{X}^k,\mathbb{Y})=\sum_{t=1}^T\min_{\mathbf P_t\in\mathscr{P}_+(K,d)}\Phi_t(\mathbf P_t),
