{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.718938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a77bc0a2ea389815ad3e489804ced048500a9bdf6ec63a307fad39f21eef4b8d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:tail_inequality of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] For each $m\geqslant 2$, there exists a constant $\kappa_m$ such that if  $\pr{S,\mathcal{S}}$ is a measurable space, $\left(X_i\right)_{i\in\mathbb Z}$ is a strictly stationary sequence taking values in $S$,   $h\colon S^m\to \mathbb R$ is a canonical kernel, $a\geqslant 0$ and $N\geqslant m$, the following inequalities hold for each positive $R,t$: 
 \begin{multline}
 \mathbb P\pr{\abs{U_{m,N+a}\left(h\right)-U_{m,a}\left(h\right)}> t}
  \\ 
     \leqslant R^2\frac{\kappa_{m}}{t^2} N\left(N+a\right)^{2m-3}  \pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^{N+a }k
      \beta\left(k\right)}+\frac{\kappa_m}{t} \frac{\left(N+a\right)^{m-1}}{N^{m-3/2}} 
      \sup_{\bm{i}\in\operatorname{Inc}^m}\E{ 
      \abs{h\pr{X_{\bm{i}}}}\mathbf{1}_{\abs{h\pr{X_{\bm{i}}}}>R}
      },
 \end{multline}
 \begin{multline}
     \mathbb P\pr{\max_{m\leqslant n\leqslant N}\abs{U_{m,n}\left(h\right)   }>N^{m-1/2}t    } \\
     \leqslant     \frac{\kappa_{m}}{t^2} \left(\log N\right)^2\frac{R^2}N \pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^{N }k
      \beta\left(k\right)}+\frac{\kappa_m}{t} \sqrt{N} 
      \sup_{\bm{i}\in\operatorname{Inc}^m}\E{ 
      \abs{h\pr{X_{\bm{i}}}}\mathbf{1}_{\abs{h\pr{X_{\bm{i}}}}>R}
      }.
 \end{multline}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.782815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a77cf19d0a03745701cbf767548bd430e5f346f53de271815e0eb3e29b364f5f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 of arXiv:2609.03054, 'The classes of bivariate Schur and Herglotz matrix-valued rational functions: realizations'] Let $G\in \mathbb C^{m \times n}(s,p)$ be a rational matrix valued  function. Then the following conditions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[\rm (i)]
\item $G$ has no singularities in $\mathbb{GH}$ and the matrix $G(s,p)$ has norm less than or equal to one
for any $(s,p)\in \mathbb{GH}$;
\item $G$ admits a realization of the form 
    $$G(s,p)=  D+  \frac12 {C} \left(s I+ 2A -
    (s^2-4p) P(s I+ 2A)^{-1} P\right)^{-1}B. $$
    with 
    \begin{equation}
\matr{
A+A^*- C^*C  & C^*D+ B\\ D^* C+ B^*  & 
I - D^* D} \geq 0,
\end{equation}
   and $-I\le P \le I$.
   \end{enumerate}
Additionally, if $G\in {\mathbb R}^{m\times n}(s,p)$, then the matrices $A,B,C,D$ and $P$
can be chosen as real.","status":"unverified"}

