{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.862214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7eb6e21e6c9f7e87c5ecb053db0d999be8ce93d13549e4b79f896c6ecc5bddc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2605.21424, 'A dice game, a multinomial walk, and the inverted Dirichlet distribution'] Let $n_1\in (0,\infty)$  and let $0\leq K\leq N$ be real numbers.  Then the function \(\N_{\ge 1}\to \R\)
