{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.763147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8174e7080d23a3f02f9ae6a4a832b876ada3b5ed1ffb2fb32f9b20d54a15069","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Tempered fractional Brownian motion
\cite{MeerschaertSabzikar2013}) of arXiv:2512.04646, '\textbf{Canonical Rough Path over Tempered Fractional Brownian Motion: Existence, Construc'] For $H \in (0,1)$ and $\lambda > 0$, the \emph{tempered fractional
Brownian motion} (tfBm)
$B_{H,\lambda} = (B_{H,\lambda}(t))_{t \ge 0}$ is the centred
Gaussian process defined by
\begin{equation}

B_{H,\lambda}(t) = \frac{1}{\Gamma(H+\frac{1}{2})} \int_{\mathbb{R}}
\Bigl[ e^{-\lambda(t-s)_+}(t-s)_+^{H-\frac{1}{2}}
      - e^{-\lambda(-s)_+}(-s)_+^{H-\frac{1}{2}} \Bigr] \, dW(s),
\end{equation}
where $W$ is a standard two-sided Brownian motion and
$x_+ = \max(x,0)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.579219+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a81a4d67b9664d426f3442981897bdc62b38a3b84ae73e41c84851d6b0d614a1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Reduction; conditional on Hypothesis~\ref{hyp:red}) of arXiv:2608.15987, 'Threshold cascades of interacting diffusions on unimodular random trees: a conditional bra'] Under Hypothesis~\ref{hyp:red}, the failed cluster of the root converges in distribution (as a random rooted tree) to the family tree of the multitype Galton--Watson process on type set $D$ with mean matrix
\begin{equation}
M_{d,d'}=m_*\,q(d')\,p_{d,d'},\qquad d,d'\in D,
\end{equation}
where $p_{d,d'}$ is the transmission probability \eqref{eq:wald}. In particular the survival probability of the cascade is positive iff $\rho(M)>1$, and zero iff $\rho(M)\le1$, where $\rho(M)$ is the Perron root of the nonnegative matrix $M$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.270487+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a81aa477e04ead579f7c8e6f9fc34f32fec05322a8b094d5e6f1b3270beaada2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem setup2 of arXiv:2412.09535, 'Local limit theorem for joint subgraph counts'] Let $H\in \mathcal{H}$ be connected and let $\eps \leq \alpha \leq 1$ be real. We get $\abs{\sete[e^{if}]} = n^{-\omega_{\lambda,\ell,\eps}(1)}$ as long as
\begin{cond}
    \item  $n^{-\alpha+\eps} \leq \Delta_H^2 \leq 1.1\pi^2 (p(1-p))^{e(H)}$;
    \item  For any graph $H' \succ H$, we have $n^{v(H')} \Delta_{H'}^2 < n^{v(H)- \alpha - \eps}$.
\end{cond}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.066001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a81ad026572e95ea456fe0afcce4752b51a5871e971cbb838ce9982fb32cef09","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.27520, 'Critical curve of loop percolation on the $d$-regular tree'] The critical value $\alpha_c(\kappa)$ is positive if and only if $\kappa>\kappa_c$. Furthermore, for each $\kappa>\kappa_c$, 
$\alpha_c(\kappa)$ is the unique solution of $\alpha > 0$ to the equation \begin{equation}
\sum_{n \geq 0} \Big( \big(1-\tau_\kappa^{2(n+1)}\big)^{-\alpha} -1 \Big) (d-1)^n  = \frac{1}{d-2}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.388391+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8244f27652a4a2fdf54022099add5e46223edaa0d5c8308e3037e675da74df4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi $K$-fuzz structure of arXiv:2607.28817, 'Limiting spectral distribution for the adjacency matrix of the Watts--Strogatz random grap'] We need a few definitions to be able to formally introduce the full $K$-fuzz graph model, denoted $F(K,p)$. See Figure~(fig:fullkfuzz of the paper) for an illustration.
    \begin{itemize}
        \item \textbf{Full $K$-path.} A full $K$-path is the infinite rooted graph with vertex set $\mathbb{Z}$ in which each vertex is adjacent to its $K/2$ nearest neighbors on either side.\\
        \item \textbf{Reduced $K$-path.} A reduced $K$-path is a rooted full $K$-path from which one of the $K/2$ edges connecting the root to its rightmost neighbors chosen uniformly at random is removed.\\
        \item \textbf{Full $K$-fuzz and reduced $K$-fuzz.} A full $K$-fuzz is obtained by starting from a full $K$-path and, for each node, independently rewiring each of its rightmost edges with probability $p$. Each rewired edge becomes a shortcut to a new full $K$-fuzz, producing an independent recursive copy. In addition, each node receives $\poisson(\frac{pK}{2})$ incoming shortcuts, each connecting to the root of a reduced $K$-fuzz. The reduced $K$-fuzz is defined analogously but starts from a reduced $K$-path.
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.256249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8268847580d18f60144cf8ac99b6545d523dfb4cfbd83ea99429f22107ca584","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma spacetimeaverageagain of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix any {\small$\mathfrak{q}_{\n_{2}}$} in (equation eq:qnformI2 of the paper). We have the following (with notation to be explained afterwards):

\begin{align}
N\grad^{\mathbf{X}}_{\mathfrak{l}_{0}}[\mathscr{S}^{N}\star\mathfrak{q}_{\n_{2}}[\tau_{\cdot}\bphi_{\t}]\mathbf{Z}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}]_{\x}&=\sum_{\substack{{m}=0,\ldots,\mathrm{M}\\0<|\mathfrak{l}_{1}|,\ldots,|\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}|\leq\mathfrak{n}_{\mathbf{Av}}}}\tfrac{1}{|\mathfrak{l}_{1}|\ldots|\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}|}\mathrm{b}'_{N,{m},\mathfrak{l}_{1},\ldots,\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}}\grad^{\mathbf{X}}_{\mathfrak{l}_{1}}\ldots\grad^{\mathbf{X}}_{\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}}[\mathscr{S}^{N}\star(\mathbf{Av}^{\mathbf{T},\mathbf{X},\mathfrak{q}_{\n_{2}}}_{\t,\cdot}\cdot\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}\mathbf{S}^{N}_{\t,\cdot})]_{\x}\\
&+\sum_{\substack{{m}=0,\ldots,\mathrm{M}\\0<|\mathfrak{l}_{1}|,\ldots,|\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}|\leq\mathfrak{n}_{\mathbf{Av}}}}\tfrac{1}{|\mathfrak{l}_{1}|\ldots|\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}|}\mathrm{b}'_{N,{m},\mathfrak{l}_{1},\ldots,\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}}\grad^{\mathbf{T},\mathrm{av}}_{\mathfrak{t}_{\mathbf{Av}}}\grad^{\mathbf{X}}_{\mathfrak{l}_{1}}\ldots\grad^{\mathbf{X}}_{\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}}[\mathscr{S}^{N}\star(\mathbf{Av}^{\mathbf{T},\mathbf{X},\mathfrak{q}_{\n_{2}}}_{\t,\cdot}\cdot\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}\mathbf{S}^{N}_{\t,\cdot})]_{\x}\\
&+\mathrm{Err}_{2}[\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}\mathbf{S}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}]_{\x}.
\end{align}

\begin{itemize}
\item The parameter {\small$\mathrm{M}=\mathrm{O}(1)$} is a positive integer.
\item The {\small$\mathrm{b}'_{N,{m},\mathfrak{l}_{1},\ldots,\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}}$} are deterministic and {\small$\mathrm{O}(N)$}. Moreover, {\small$\mathrm{b}'_{N,{m},\mathfrak{l}_{1},\ldots,\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}}=0$} if {\small$\min\{|\mathfrak{l}_{1}|,\ldots,|\mathfrak{l}_{{m}}|\}\geq2$}.
\item The term {\small$\mathrm{Err}_{2}[\mathbf{R}^{N}\mathbf{S}^{N}]_{\t,\x}$} is a linear operator in {\small$\mathbf{S}^{N}$} evaluated at {\small$(\t,\x)$}, and it satisfies the deterministic estimate below as long as {\small$\mathrm{C}=\mathrm{O}(1)$} is sufficiently large:

\begin{align}
|\mathrm{Err}_{2}[\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}\mathbf{S}^{N}_{\t,\cdot}]_{\x}|\lesssim N^{-\frac32}\cdot N^{-1+\delta_{\mathbf{S}}}\sum_{|\w|\lesssim N^{1-\delta_{\mathbf{S}}}}\Big(1+\sum_{|\z|\lesssim1}|\bphi_{\t,\x+\w+\z}|^{\mathrm{C}}\Big)\cdot|\mathbf{R}^{N}_{\t,\x+\w}|\cdot|\mathbf{S}^{N}_{\t,\x+\w}|.
\end{align}

\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:20.952015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a82df6916d21c1e3bfd2eb773e6a248ea3f78452d862a3d1aaec1cc008fcb58a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.05234, 'Quantitative propagation of chaos and universality for asymmetric Langevin spin glass dyna'] For all $\bfJ \in \R^{N\times N}$, the measure $P_t(\bfJ)$ satisfies the covariance bound 
    \begin{align*}
        \|\sfE_\bfJ[X_tX^\top_t]\|_{\textup{op}}\leq C_{\textup{Var}}\exp\Big(2t\beta N^{-1/2}\|\bfJ\|_{\textup{op}}\Big),
    \end{align*}
    where
    \begin{align*}
        C_{\textup{Var}}:=(C_\textup{P}(0)+T) e^{2tC_{\textup{Lip}}}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.781106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a82e0f1cbded3429971e758fb01302f8e2c32733b74e97ec1f76aa108150e83c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2609.03054, 'The classes of bivariate Schur and Herglotz matrix-valued rational functions: realizations'] Let $F\in\mathbb C^{n\times n}(z_1,z_2)$ be a rational matrix valued function. Then the following conditions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[\rm (i)]
\item {$F$ has no poles in $\RHPtwo$},  $F(z_1,z_2)$ has nonnegative real part
$($i.e.\ $F(z_1,z_2)^*+F(z_1,z_2)\geq 0)$ for any $z_1,z_2\in\RHP$,
and $\lim_{t\to\infty} F(t,t)$ exists;
\item $F$ admits a realization of the form
\begin{equation} 
F(z_1,z_2)= D+ C(z_1P_1+z_2P_2+A)^{-1}B,
\end{equation}
where the block matrix $\matr{A&B\\C&D} \in\Cmats{(k+n)}{(k+n)}$ is such that
\begin{equation}
\matr{
A+A^*  & C^*- B \\ C- B^* & D^*+ D
} \geq 0,
\end{equation}
$P_1,P_2\in \sqmat{k}$ are positive semidefinite and $P_1+P_2=I_k$.
\end{enumerate}
Additionally, if $F\in\mathbb R^{n\times n}(z_1,z_2)$ then the matrices $A,B,C,D,P_1,P_2$ in {\rm (ii)} may be chosen as real matrices.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.459981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a82f2ed2d87464792bb05619d1d6f10197e748bd3520248fe8a26cb3c543194a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:weighted-minimal of arXiv:2609.02234, 'An $n(\log n)^{o(1)}$ bound for nested cycles without geometric crossings'] Let $K>0$. An $n$-vertex graph $G$ is \emph{$K$-minimal} if $e(G)>K\Phi(n)$ and every nonempty proper $W\subset V(G)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
  e(G[W])\le K\Phi(|W|).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.008809+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8332b186c098a6a3c34a3c7763d7d6ed6c50ef2d8bcfb12d6919ec9bce7f745","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 of arXiv:2609.02808, 'Minimizers of Laplace eigenvalues under a lower curvature bound'] Suppose $\varphi\colon[0,D]\to[0,\infty)$ is continuous, positive on $(0,D)$, and satisfies 
    \begin{equation}
\varphi\ \text{ is concave on }[0,D].
\end{equation}
     Then the eigenspectrum of the Sturm Liouville Problem~\eqref{eq:slp} is purely discrete and simple with \[
0=\mu_0(\varphi)<\mu_1(\varphi)<\mu_2(\varphi)<\cdots.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.653442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a83a2872c6acb9c3f69b3a62e92cdb0721bb8048f58cce7169923f2bd65d7fa6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.07184, 'Convergence of Stochastic Gradient Descent with mini-batching and infinite variance'] Let
  \Cref{assumption:function_H,
