{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.071312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8766364e8cc737be9deab52e601a4e965cf2ecd81b3f5c7a1aecca243fa9c1e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2606.21556, 'Mean field limit of non-exchangeable interacting diffusions on co-evolutionary networks'] Given any two fibered probability measures \(\mu,\bar{\mu} \in \mathcal{P}_{\nu}(\mathcal{X}\times [0,1])\), we define the following fibered distances between \(\mu\) and \(\bar{\mu}\): 
