{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.765610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8dc1f4e3d4717b32530a5d57cf9bbb7e991e2ae54c1256ca8cf820558d98616","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2605.14254, '2605.14254'] Let $T$ be a stopping time with compensator $A$. Then:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[(i)] $T$ is predictable if and only if $A$ is almost surely constant apart from a possible unit jump;
			\item[(ii)] $T$ is accessible if and only if $A$ is almost surely purely discontinuous;
