      \end{align*}
      where $C_{\alpha,B},\bar{\varepsilon}_{\a}$ are from Lemma \ref{l.042501}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.645533+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a943deed5e4d799aaff6254aa432360a9b5460dc49a298c3fd8370d20cae4f8d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:width_from_contour of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] For any tree $T$ of size $n$, if we let $C^{(T)}=(C^{(T)}_t:0\leq t \leq 2n-1)$ be its contour walk, $w(T)$ its width, then 
