{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:24:20.641071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a95cc142dcbb6615baa4875df9b19fac4e30e3d2a5438241edb958a764fa8409","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] The sequence of cumulants $k_1,k_2,k_3,k_4,\ldots$ is as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For $\mu=\delta_c$ the cumulants are $c,0,0,0,\ldots$

\item For $\mu=g_t$ the cumulants are $0,t,0,0,\ldots$

\item For $\mu=p_t$ the cumulants are $t,t,t,t,\ldots$

\item For $\mu=b_t^2$ the cumulants are $0,t,0,t,\ldots$
\end{enumerate}
Also, for the compound Poisson laws the cumulants are $k_n(p_\nu)=M_n(\nu)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.955468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a95fabd8447c62721528f34f65f92fd1f6c91820a5694fad55fd5e2b8c016913","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:bernstein_current of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Let $\bar W = W - \E^\mu[W]$ and
$\bar Q = Q - \E^\mu[Q]$.
Let $k^\ast_{\max}$ be the positive root of
$k(\|\bar W\|_{L^\infty(\mu)} + k\|\bar Q\|_{L^\infty(\mu)}) = \lambda_\mathrm{gap}$,
\begin{align}
k^\ast_{\max}
=
\begin{cases}
\dfrac{-\|\bar W\|_{L^\infty(\mu)} + \sqrt{\|\bar W\|_{L^\infty(\mu)}^2 + 4\lambda_\mathrm{gap}\|\bar Q\|_{L^\infty(\mu)}}}{2\|\bar Q\|_{L^\infty(\mu)}}
& \|\bar Q\|_{L^\infty(\mu)} > 0, 
\\[6pt]
\dfrac{\lambda_\mathrm{gap}}{\|\bar W\|_{L^\infty(\mu)}}
& \|\bar Q\|_{L^\infty(\mu)} = 0,
\end{cases}
\end{align}
and define
\begin{align}
c_{J,2} \equiv \frac{1}{k^\ast_{\max}},
\qquad
\tilde\sigma_{J,2}^2 \equiv 2\E^\mu[Q]
+ \frac{2}{\lambda_\mathrm{gap}}
  \left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_\mu(W)} + k^\ast_{\max}\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_\mu(Q)}\right)^2.
\end{align}
Then for all $k \in [0, k^\ast_{\max})$,
\begin{align}
\Lambda^J(k) - k\E^\mu[W]
\leq
\frac{\tilde\sigma_{J,2}^2 k^2}{2(1 - c_{J,2}k)}.

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.986150+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a961ad6cf6246fa50ca4d3500266fcf129b3e83c973759397dc213107d356e89","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition contrainte of arXiv:2412.00865, 'On the spectral problem and fractional diffusion limit for Fokker-Planck with(-out) drift '] Define $\  B(\lambda,\eta):= \eta^{-\frac{2}{3}} b(\lambda,\eta) $.  

\noindent 1. The expression of $B(\lambda,\eta)$ is given by
\begin{equation}
B(\lambda,\eta)= \eta^{-\frac{2}{3}}\langle N_{\lambda,\eta},\Phi\rangle = \int_{\mathbb{R}^d}(\lambda- \mathrm{i} \eta^{\frac{1}{3}} v)M_{\lambda,\eta}(v)M(v)\mathrm{d}v .
\end{equation}
2.  The $\eta$ order of $B(\lambda,\eta)$ in its expansion with respect to $\lambda$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\underset{\eta \rightarrow 0}{\mathop{\rm lim}} \ \frac{\partial B}{\partial \lambda}(0,\eta) = \int_{\mathbb{R}^d} M^2(v)\mathrm{d}v .
\end{equation}
3.  There exists $\tilde\eta_0, \tilde\lambda_0>0$ small enough, a function $\tilde{\lambda}: \{|\eta|\leqslant\tilde\eta_0\} \longrightarrow \{|\lambda|\leqslant\tilde\lambda_0\}$ such that,
for all $(\lambda,\eta)\in [0,\tilde\eta_0[\times\{|\lambda|<\tilde\lambda_0\}$,  $\lambda = \tilde{\lambda}(\eta)$ and the constraint is satisfied: $$B(\lambda,\eta)= B(\tilde{\lambda}(\eta),\eta)=0.$$
Consequently, $\mu(\eta) := \eta^{\frac{2}{3}} \tilde{\lambda} (\eta)$ is the eigenvalue associated to the eigenfunction $M_\eta: = M_{\tilde{\lambda}(\eta),\eta}$ for the operator $\mathcal{L}_\eta$, and the couple $\big(\mu(\eta),M_\eta \big)$ is solution to the spectral problem (equation M_mu,eta of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.585167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a963dd3c9669c978d51fb4647a2e35358748c05c62d112600e62afabe1db1b7e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm equivalent_cost of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$. The map \begin{align*}
    \iota:  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)\to  \mathsf{Cpl}_s( \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_0), \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_1)),  \mathsf{Q}\mapsto ( \mathsf{sq}\circ\mathrm{Pr}^{\Gamma}_0, \mathsf{sq}\circ\mathrm{Pr}^{\Gamma}_1)_{\#} \mathsf{Q}^0
\end{align*}
is a bijection. Furthermore, it holds that 
\begin{align}
    \int \sum_{(x,y)\in \bar\xi\cap \Lambda_1}\left\lvert(x^+-x)-(y^+-y)\right\rvert^p \mathsf{Q}(d\bar\xi)=\int \left\lvert \mathsf{s}_1- \mathsf{s}'_1\right\rvert^p\iota( \mathsf{Q})(d \mathsf{s},d \mathsf{s}').
\end{align}    
In particular
  \begin{align*}
        \mathscr W_p(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)=\mathscr W_{gap,p}( \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_0), \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_1)) 
    \end{align*}
    and there exists an $\mathscr W_p-$optimal $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.864361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a96d064d435f5d4dc1f741739f474c29d379494f8a7522a4b9aeb731e5efa50e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2605.21638, 'Markov renewal theory for transfer operators and point processes on the line'] Let $\mu_{n,\beta}^x, \Phi$ be defined as above.
