where $\kappa$ and $\lambda_H$ are given by \eqref{def:kappa} and  \eqref{def:lambda:H}, respectively.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.237499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a97ecb9d39b2a177732dbfaf471def91e71f9ce3cf8da645668e65702be77c19","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Newton-Leibniz of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] Let $f \colon [0, 1] \to \BR$ be a continuous and strictly increasing function. Then $f^\prime(x)$ exists for almost every $x \in [0,1]$ and
