{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.018245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9cd8a9b866ae5e3cd4fe2eba50551d67bed79259ae434c4a810ba14a9c29a0d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:massive_limit of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d \ge 1$. Suppose $D(x)$ has finite support $\mathcal{U}$.
Let $x \in {\mathbb R^d}$ be on the boundary of $\mathrm{Conv}(\mathcal{U})$.
Then as $z \to 0$, we have
\begin{equation}
\abs x_{z} = \mathrm{rad}(\mathcal{U}) + O(m_z^{-1}) .
\end{equation}
In particular, $\lim_{z\to 0} | \cdot |_z$ defines a norm on ${\mathbb R^d}$, with its unit ball being $\mathrm{Conv}(\mathcal{U}) / \mathrm{rad}(\mathcal{U})$.","status":"unverified"}

