{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.907789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9dbf12e8b6720c5a4ebdaa89687d4c75711143ced21f3bddd528daec8ca7b60","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:NSP:statement of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] A linear operator $\mathcal{A}: \R^{d_1 \times d_2} \to \R^{m}$ is said to satisfy 
