{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.664704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9dd53127b3481d8249f7d93e07f0178d96cd50ef003548a8004c44a4cfda2b8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.29495, 'Fast Mixing for Low-Temperature Potts Models via Poisson Trees'] Fix integer $q\geq 2$ and $\beta>0$. Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph and 
$\nu=\nu_{G;q,\beta}$ be the Edwards--Sokal distribution.  Let $\mu=\mu_{G;q,\beta}$ and $\pi=\pi_{G;q,\beta}$ be the Potts and RC distributions. 

Suppose that $\mu$ satisfies
entropy factorisation with constant $C_{\mathrm{spin}}$. 
Then, with $C_{\mathrm{joint}} \coloneqq O(q^3  \emm^{3\beta \Delta}C_{\mathrm{spin}})$, for every function $g\ge0$ on the joint spin-edge space $[q]^V\times \{0,1\}^E$,
\begin{equation}
\Ent_\nu(g) \leq C_{\mathrm{joint}}
        \bigg(
        \sum_{v\in V}
        \E_\nu\left[\Ent^{\circ}_v(g)\right]
        + \sum_{e\in E}
        \E_\nu\left[\Ent^{\circ}_e(g)\right]
        \bigg).
\end{equation}
As a corollary, $\pi$ satisfies
entropy factorisation with constant $C_{\mathrm{joint}}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.755555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9e57a12b8874deaeee51d978b5733b961bc5569a6bc3baaa66d02d3dfc3fc7e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 46 of arXiv:2609.03836, 'Koszul Orlik--Solomon Algebras from Non-supersolvable Arrangements'] \label[Prop]{prop:pc_complement}
