{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.033179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aaf0ac359955086ca57b17392b6685dc210e3a5f522131b4e86762e31949e6c4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nemytskii_lipschitz of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] Assume that $f$ is Lipschitz continuous and that $\rho\in L^1(U)$. Then the associated Nemytskii operator $F$ is a nonlinear, bounded, Lipschitz continuous operator on $H=L^2(U,\rho)$ with
\[\|F(u)\|\le \sqrt{1+\zeta}\operatorname{Lip}(f)\|u\|+\sqrt{1+C(\zeta)}|f(0)|\|\rho\|_{L^1(U)}^{1/2},\]
for any $\zeta>0$ and some $C(\zeta)>0$,
and we have that $\operatorname{Lip}(F)=\operatorname{Lip}(f)$. If $\zeta=1$, then $C(\zeta)=1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.369390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aaf238d6fddd4b8e46d279f0873d53a0bd3fa0d017e0e7d5763eb81dc8bb2200","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:interpolation of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] Let $p\in[1,\infty)$, $k,\ell\in\mathbb{N}$, $k$ even. Take a  linear map $T:\mathcal{C}^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)\mapsto L^p(\Omega)$ such there exist positive constants $\Gamma_{\ell}\leq\Gamma_{-k}$ so that the following holds: for any $f\in \mathcal{C}^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)$ the following bounds hold                       

    \begin{equs}
       \|Tf\|_{L^p(\Omega)} &\leq \Gamma_{\ell}\|\nabla^\ell f\|_{\infty},\\
        \|T(\nabla^k f)\|_{L^p(\Omega)} &\leq \Gamma_{-k}\|f\|_{\infty}.  
    \end{equs}
    Suppose furthermore that $Tf_n\to T f$ in $L^p(\Omega)$ whenever $f_n\to f$ uniformly on compacts.
    Then for any $\beta\in[-k,0)$ there exists a constant $C=C(d,\ell,k,\beta)$ such that for all $f\in \mathcal{C}^\infty(\mathbb{R}^d)$ one has
    \begin{equ}
          \|Tf\|_{L^p(\Omega)} \leq C \Gamma_{\ell}^{1-\theta}\Gamma_{-k}^{\theta}\|f\|_{\mathcal{C}^{{\beta}}},   
    \end{equ}
    where $\theta\in[0,1]$ is uniquely defined by $\beta=(1-\theta)\ell-\theta k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.375234+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aaf32fc587a1f1111c98af9eed9b11603c9b31d7f396aba14320d4bb54f03ae9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:gapprocess-tilt of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $k=2$. Then, for every $\beta\in \mathbb{R} $, the gap process $X\coloneqq R^1-R^2$ is a ${\rm CTRW}$ on $\mathbb{Z}$. Supposing that the gap process sits at $x \in \mathbb{Z}$, its evolution goes as follows:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item if $x\neq 0,\pm 1$,  it  jumps to $x\pm 1$ with rate $\cosh(\beta)$;
    \item if $x=0$, it jumps to $\pm 1$ with rate $\frac12\cosh(\beta)$;
    \item if $x=\pm 1$, it jumps to $\pm 2$ with rate $\cosh(\beta)$, to $0$ with rate $\frac12\cosh(\beta)$, and to $\mp 1$ with rate $1/4$.
\end{enumerate}
As a consequence, the counting measure $\pi$ on $\mathbb{Z}$ is reversible for $X$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.856957+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aaf4803680179385c7149e4a31d896ef60f67f27d329850b896d6552a97ae24a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Asymptotic flatness) of arXiv:2605.20700, 'The maximum of a strongly \\ correlated Gaussian process'] We say that $K$ is asymptotically flat if there exists a function $w : \R^+ \to \R$ such that $K(x,y) \sim w(|x-y|)$ as $|x-y| \to \infty$, and which satisfies the following:  for every $\eta > 0$ there exists a $\beta > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}

  \limsup_{v \to \infty}  \sup_{u \in [v^{-\beta} , 1] } \Big| \frac{ w( u v) }{ w(v) } - 1 \Big| \le \eta  .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.867152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aafa6a4c01fbe4ae385616edc99d4a669c516dda8e994845e31d255746c6937a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Rcont of arXiv:2411.06838, 'Generalized Wasserstein Barycenters'] Let $(\mu_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\subset \mathcal{P}_2(H)$ be a sequence converging to $\mu \in \mathcal{P}_2(H)$ with respect to the (weak) topology of $\mathcal{P}_2^w(H)$ and let $(\nu_n)_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\subset \mathcal{P}_2(H)$ be a sequence converging to $\nu \in \mathcal{P}_2(H)$ with respect to the (strong) topology of $\mathcal{P}_2(H)$. 
