{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.413947+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab12c9b50e6c8682bc395c98dda48ad50f65b917e4883bc04328cd45e73ff401","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 74 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Let $\mathcal A_\eps\subseteq \W_\N$ denote the set of configurations such that
\begin{itemize}
\item there are at most $C \N^{\frac{1}{2}}(\log\N)^2$ particles $\ell_i$ in $[\N(\mathfrak{a}+\eps),\N\mathfrak{b}]\cup \big(-\infty,-\frac{\N D}{2}\big]\cup\big[\frac{\N D}{2},+\infty\big)$;
\item the event studied in Lemma~\ref{Lemma_tail_bound_general} with $t =\N^{-\frac{1}{2}}\log\N$ does not hold, \textit{i.e.}
\[
\forall f \in \mathscr{H}_{\textnormal{Lip},\frac{1}{2}} \quad \exists h \in [H] \qquad \bigg|\int_{\amsmathbb{R}} f(x)\dd(\mu_{\N,h} - \mu_h)(x)\bigg| \leq \frac{\log\N}{\N^{\frac{1}{2}}}\cdot |\!|f|\!|_{\frac{1}{2}} + \frac{C}{\N}\cdot \big(|\!|f|\!|_{\textnormal{Lip}} + |\!|f|\!|_{\infty}\big).
\]
\end{itemize}
For $0<\eps_1<\eps_2$, let $\mathcal{E}\big[\begin{smallmatrix} K_1 & K_2 \\ \eps_1 & \eps_2 \end{smallmatrix}\big] \subseteq \W_\N$ be the set of configurations with exactly $K_1$ particles in $[\mathfrak{a}+\eps_1, \mathfrak{b}]$ and $K_2 \leq K_1$ particles in $[\mathfrak{a}+\eps_2,\mathfrak{b}]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.500435+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab1883a9bf713d87fc3b96cf4a6d4da10bbe0f3c799fd573556c6c404346e720","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:one-point-bds of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] For any $\alpha_0>0$, there exists a constant $c>0$, such that whenever the boundary parameter satisfies $\alpha\ge \alpha_0$ we have the following bounds. 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item (Upper tail) For all $n \in \mathbb{N}, \epsilon \in (0, n^{-1/3}]$ we have
$$
\mathbb{P}(X(1, 1; n, n) \ge \mu_\alpha(n) + \epsilon n) \le 2\exp\left(-c \epsilon^{3/2} n \left(1 \wedge \frac{\epsilon^{1/2}}{(1/2 - \alpha)\vee 0}\right) \right).
$$
    \item (Shallow lower tail when $\alpha < 1/2$) For all $n \in \mathbb{N}, \epsilon \in (0, 1]$ such that $\alpha \le 1/2 - n^{-1/3}$ and $\epsilon n \le \mu_\alpha(n) - 4n$, we have
\begin{align}

	\mathbb{P}\Big(X(1, 1; n, n) \le \mu_\alpha(n) - \epsilon n\Big) \le 2\exp\left(- \frac{c\epsilon^2 n}{1/2 - \alpha} \right).
\end{align}
\item (Full lower tail for $\alpha \ge 1/2$, deep lower tail for $\alpha < 1/2$) For all $n \in \mathbb{N}, \epsilon \in (0, 1]$ we have
\begin{align}

	\mathbb{P}\Big(X(1, 1; n, n) \le 4n - \epsilon n\Big) \le 2\exp\left(- c \epsilon^3 n^2\right).
\end{align}	
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

