{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.933840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab6b6086be7a58b303988f0aa08263913e283c1ec619a8b4582e0448a7bcf116","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mult_concentration of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Let $k_i$ denote the number of tiles on edges of type $e_i$, and let $\overline{k}_i = \mathbb{E}_{\mu_{n,N,w}}[k_i]$. There exists a constant $c=c(w)>0$ such that for any $\varepsilon>0$ and $N$ large enough given $n,\varepsilon$, 
