{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.757394+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab76c8f859ae4f80d493e4f1e5566cdbe4bac66886b153e19a0571200dd5263a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:massive-massless-continuous-correction of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] Fix a disk $U\Subset\mathbb R^2$ and $m_0>0$.  Write $\Delta_U$ for the
Dirichlet Laplacian on $U$ and set $L_0^U:=-(2\pi)^{-1}\Delta_U$.  Consider
a centered Gaussian field $Z_U$ with covariance operator
\begin{equation}
 \Cov(Z_U)=C_U^{(m_0)}
 :=(L_0^U)^{-1}-(L_0^U+m_0^2)^{-1}
 =m_0^2(L_0^U)^{-1}
   (L_0^U+m_0^2)^{-1}.

\end{equation}
Then $Z_U$ has a continuous version.  More precisely, for every $K\Subset U$
there is $C_{K,U,m_0}<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E|Z_U(z)-Z_U(z')|^2
 \le C_{K,U,m_0}r^2
 \left(1+\log\frac1r\right),
 \qquad
 z,z'\in K,\quad 0<r:=|z-z'|\le\frac12.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.955632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab7878b4be96b605d77ac6dc12ae0602a3c7e8700cabdeb92d6ebaa0bc6e5877","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.25501, 'An RDT based approach to large deviations of Wishart and Wigner matrices spectral edges'] (\cite{Gordon85,Slep62})
 Let $X_{i}$ and $Y_{i}$, $1\leq i\leq n$, be two centered Gaussian processes which satisfy the following inequalities for all choices of indices
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mE(X_{i}^2)=\mE(Y_{i}^2)$
\item $\mE(X_{i}X_{l})\leq \mE(Y_{i}Y_{l}), i\neq l$.
\end{enumerate}
 Then
\begin{equation*}
\mE(\min_{i} X_{i})\leq \mE(\min_i Y_{i}) \quad  \Longleftrightarrow \quad \mE(\max_{i} X_{i})\geq \mE(\max_i Y_{i}).
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.712875+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab79d2a8a4e173796e12ca39c655f710b9a744550ca5025a0babb0a7f53668ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition W_1 of arXiv:2411.04778, 'Coupling between Brownian motion and random walks on the infinite percolation cluster'] For every $\delta>0$ and $y\in \mathbb{Z}^d$, there exist finite positive constants $C$ and $s$ depending only on $d,\mathfrak{p},\delta$ and  a nonnegative $\omega$-measurable random variable $\mathcal{T}_\delta^{(1)}(y)$ satisfying
		\begin{equation}
			\forall T\geqslant 0, \qquad \mathbb{P}_{\mathfrak{p}}\left(\mathcal{T}^{(1)}_\delta (y)\geqslant T\right)\leqslant C \exp\left(-\frac{T^s}{C}\right),
		\end{equation}
