{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.356099+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abd431a7fb3b9ab79f9aeeff523c99ef8d99a8098d44d48da8cb9268e499b3dd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:adaptive of arXiv:2608.23638, 'Replicable Conformal Prediction'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1)$, $\rho\in(0,1]$, and a score law with density $f$ continuous and positive at $q=F^{-1}(1-\alpha)$; let $\hat f_n$ be any shared pilot with $\hat f_n\to_pf(q)$, $\hat f_n\ge f_0>0$, independent of both calibration samples, and run \textsc{ReCal}{} with $\beta_n=2B_n/(\hat f_n\rho)$, $\hat\kappa{=}1$. Then, with $Z$ standard normal,
