{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.567675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abf0e44d39bfcae5b4bf3c57959adce88f424cc6664e6e89ed4fa214dc545606","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $(X,d,\mu)$ be a Polish probability space. Suppose it admits a continuous isoperimetric function $I:(0,1)\to(0,\infty)$. Define
\begin{equation}

\Phi(v):=
\begin{cases}
    \int_{\frac{1}{2}}^v\frac{dr}{I(r)},
    & v\in(\frac{1}{2},1),
    \\
    0, & v=\frac{1}{2},
    \\
    -\int_{v}^\frac{1}{2}\frac{dr}{I(r)}, & v \in (0,\frac{1}{2}),
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
and set $a:=\inf \Phi((0,1))$ and $b:=\sup \Phi((0,1)),$ where $-\infty \leq a \leq 0 <b\leq \infty$. Define the distribution function $\Psi:\mathbb R\to[0,1]$ by
\begin{equation}

\Psi(t):=
\begin{cases}
    0, & t\leq a,\\
    \Phi^{-1}(t), & t\in(a,b),\\
    1, & t\geq b.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Then $\Psi$ is continuous and non-decreasing with $\Psi(0)=\frac{1}{2}$. For each $s\geq0$, define
$R_s^I:[0,1]\to[0,1]$ by
\begin{equation}

    R_s^I(0):=0,
    \qquad
    R_s^I(1):=1,
\quad \text{and }
    R_s^I(v):=\Psi\bigl(\Phi(v)+s\bigr),
    \qquad v\in(0,1).
\end{equation}
Then $R_s^I$ is an enlargement function for $(X,d,\mu)$ in the
sense of Definition~\ref{d:enlargement}. Conversely, if $(X,d,\mu)$ has $R_s^I$ of the above form as an enlargement function, then it satisfies isoperimetry with isoperimetric function $I$.

Moreover, if $A\subset X$ is a Borel set with $0<\mu(A)<1$ and, for some
$s>0$ such that $R_s^I(\mu(A))<1$, equality holds in
\eqref{eq:enlarge_ineq}, then
\begin{equation}

    \mu(A_t)=R_t^I(\mu(A)),
    \qquad 0\leq t\leq s.
\end{equation}
In particular, $\mu(A_0)=\mu(A)$ and $A$ is an extremal set for the
isoperimetric inequality \eqref{eq:extremal_iso}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.166429+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abf1abcc5a7739ea5766f86c116da2eb0333ca68a78c21b14951e3d2f34e18ed","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:0.1 of arXiv:2608.30848, '\huge \bf Limit Laws of the Iterated Logarithm Under Sub-linear Expectations'] The following are equivalent:
