{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.671389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_acb7858b6e9698d646793643943898452f4977e66f10c3f62f00d80f5c9324f5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:covariance of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] Let \( \mu \) be a measure on \( (X, \mathcal{C}(X)) \) such that \( X^* \subseteq L^2(\mu) \).
