{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.585989+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_accfff7427fc3d32032afb2a4e05f6d44ead889d711848045bb5679f24d75247","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop entropy_exp of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mu$ be a measure on $[0,\infty)^{n}$ such that $\int x_i\mu(dx)=\int x_1\mu(dx)$ for all $i=1,\dots,n$.
