{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.970878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad401e17a5f21cbdb04dc5f4c4ae052465f2ed79ec2966f18f2c9916e4bf0219","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:rmulmc_cvx of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Let $\hat{\boldsymbol{P}}$, $\hat{\boldsymbol{P}}{}'$ denote the kernels for~(eq:rm-ulmc of the paper) and~(eq:ULMC of the paper) respectively, and let $\boldsymbol{P}$ denote the kernel for~(eq:ULD of the paper) run for time $h$.
