{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.823271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_adfd6101e7d2db93265924c6d220fef4790803f84c50f79157d12eb471219947","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2604.10244, 'Ergodicity for regime-switching neutral stochastic functional differential equations with '] Let $p\geq 2$ and assumptions (\hyperlink{A0}{A0})-(\hyperlink{A3}{A3}),  (\hyperlink{H1}{H1}) and (\hyperlink{H2}{H2})  hold. Suppose further that $$\mathcal{A}:=-\left(p\operatorname{diag}\left(\alpha^{F}(1), \ldots, \alpha^{F}(m)\right)+Q^{F}\right) H_{m} $$ is a nonsingular $M$-matrix, where  $\alpha^F$ and $Q^F$ are defined by \eqref{eq:xinffu} and \eqref{eq:xinleng} respectively, and
		\begin{equation}
