{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.885782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae010f6587adcae1831e97a12ef2862f2467a744e0cebfa8b6c779a29d5d8797","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eqn:exponential mixing 2 of arXiv:2606.29352, 'Exponential Mixing for 2D Stochastic Damped Euler Equation Driven by Bounded Noise'] Let $\gamma>0$. There exists $\epsilon(\gamma)>0$ such that there exists a unique invariant measure $\mu^\epsilon$ on $E$ for Eq. ((eqn:Euler 2 of the paper)). Moreover, for any $0<\epsilon<\epsilon(\gamma)$, $x \in E$ and $\phi \in \text{Lip}_b(E)$,
