{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.872480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae19b73272b2dcfc286d834e878cddee9e4d73d2cde669436b76d077da06e88b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop transf_pant_to_alph of arXiv:2411.00629, '\Large Transformation of Stochastic Recursions and Critical Phenomena in the Analysis of t'] Suppose $\mathscr{X}(t)$ is a nonnegative binary-tree solution process of (equation markovsspantographeq of the paper), i.e.\ satisfying
