{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.557140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae1b0d11a39c6d34f622a155e1b4f60e1ad4d72840500cc22964bf77deaeba3e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Dn_limit of arXiv:2603.28936, 'Composition of random functions and word reconstruction'] Let $w$ be a word of exponent $d\geq 1$, i.e. $w=\pi^d$ for some primitive word $\pi$. For any $g\geq 1$ and any tuple $(z_0,\dots,z_{g-1})\in \mathbb{C}^g$ we have the convergence in distribution
