{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.146562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae2c6fc727c66795dd328fe5e470872e6ba1376a0dfc988532b1cf86502bba13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For every $\varepsilon > 0$, there exist constants $c, C > 0$ such that for any $n \ge 1$, any $v \in [n]$ and any $S\in \left[ 1,c (n/v)^{1-\varepsilon} \right]$, the upper tail satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        c\frac{1+\log S}{S^2} 
        \ \leq\ \mathbb{P} \big( \widehat{\sigma}_{2}(v) \geq S v \big) 
        \ \leq\ C\frac{ 1+\log S}{S^2}.
    \end{equation}
    The upper bound holds for all $S\ge  1$.

    Moreover, there exist constants $c', C', \delta > 0$ such that for any $n \ge 1$, any $v \in [n/4]$, and any $S\in[1,\delta\sqrt{v}]$, the lower tail satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{c'}{S^2} 
        \ \leq\  \mathbb{P}\Big(\widehat{\sigma}_2(v) \leq \frac{1}{S}v\Big) 
        \ \leq\ \frac{C'}{S^2}.
    \end{equation}
    The upper bound holds for all $S \geq 1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.835479+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae2fbc9bd983c3981ad7ac0a156266b7fd1be972559a7bfe3af994ed340875cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 ({\cite{Bou02}}) of arXiv:2609.01965, 'A logarithmic Bogomolov--Sommese vanishing theorem on compact K\"ahler manifolds'] Let $X$ be a compact K\"ahler manifold and $L$ a pseudo-effective line bundle over $X$. 
