{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.316848+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae425c699c516e5a1987dcd57793631512b2ba7f2dfea3c9e28a18e270974203","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:shadow3 of arXiv:2608.30973, 'Pseudo-Anosov flow and dynamics on guts'] Let \(l\) be a component of the frontier of \(\Theta(\widetilde{S})\) in \(P_{\varphi}\). Then,
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(l\) is a slice leaf of \(\mathcal{F}^{s/u}\). If it is a slice leaf \(l\) of \(\mathcal{F}^{s}\), then as a sequence of point \(\{p_{n}\}_{n\in \mathbb{N}}\) tends to a point in \(l\), the preimages \((\Theta|_{\widetilde{S}})^{-1}(p_{n})\) in \(\widetilde{S}\) escape in the positive direction.
Similar conclusion holds for unstable boundary slice leaves.
\item \(l\) is periodic, namely, there is an element \(g\in \pi_{1}(M)\) such that \(g\) fixes \(l\) and hence a unique point in \(l\).
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.421874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae460b55591b2132f5787f10c18d8185aa559359092b18553c875dd09904bd4f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2608.31145, 'Gauge-compatible tensors on statistical manifolds: splitting and submanifold geometry'] Let $M$ be a $\Theta$-CR submanifold of a $\Theta$-statistical
manifold.

\begin{enumerate}
\item For $X,Y\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta})$,
\begin{equation}
F_{\Theta}([X,Y])
=
h(X,\Theta Y)-h(Y,\Theta X).
\end{equation}

\item For $U,V\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta}^{\perp})$,
\begin{equation}
P_{\Theta}([U,V])
=
A_{\Theta U}V-A_{\Theta V}U.
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}

Consequently:

\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] if
\[
\ker(F_{\Theta}|_{TM})=D_{\Theta},
\]
then $D_{\Theta}$ is integrable if and only if
\begin{equation}
h(X,\Theta Y)=h(Y,\Theta X)
\end{equation}
for all $X,Y\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta})$;

\item[(b)] if
\[
\ker(P_{\Theta}|_{TM})=D_{\Theta}^{\perp},
\]
then $D_{\Theta}^{\perp}$ is integrable if and only if
\begin{equation}
A_{\Theta U}V=A_{\Theta V}U
\end{equation}
for all $U,V\in\Gamma(D_{\Theta}^{\perp})$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.232836+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae47101f92fd527a88f1a83314da80e46a31ca8ee346fc567dcec62e54479cac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorema 2 ({\Cref{criterion-decomp-log}}) of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(X\) be a smooth \(k\)-variety of dimension \(d\), and let \(D\)
be a simple normal crossings divisor on \(X\).  Then the following
conditions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item The pair \((X,D)\) is log HT-split.
\item There is an isomorphism
\begin{equation}
F_{*}\Omega_{X/k}^{\bullet}(\log D)
\simeq
\bigoplus_{i=0}^{d}
\Omega_{X/k}^i(\log D)[-i]
\end{equation}
in \(\mcalD_{\qcoh}(X)\).
\end{enumerate}
If \(X\) is projective, these equivalent conditions imply logarithmic
Akizuki--Nakano vanishing and the \(E_1\)-degeneration of the
logarithmic Hodge-to-de Rham spectral sequence (\Cref{vanishing}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:02:17.908297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae4a3226afa257dd25480ef279cbef11a2d277feccab79076f7b885c287e19e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:aniso_inj_holder of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] For every $\alpha\in (0,1)$, any element $T\in \mathcal{C}^{\alpha,\alpha-1}_{x,y}(I\times J)$ for every $\chi\in C^\infty_c(J)$, the product $T1_I\chi$ which is well--defined
