{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.782250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae7375a72633710e26c671f7c2c603c6588152d855f06025427bc2aeb4ebc3a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 (Total variation principle for Einstein--Euler flows) of arXiv:2608.31171, '\bf Finite-energy spacetimes with torus symmetry. \\ \Large Cauchy stability of Einstein--'] Under the conditions in \autoref{proposition-JJJ}, the following total variation bound holds for sufficiently regular solutions: 
