{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.256441+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae7557ac4f87e841fc21b7f55e3425ea54ef4a94260ba516d88237d17ab23068","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 49 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] For $\alpha\in (0,\alpha_n),\;\kappa\in (0,1],\;y\in F,\;y_n\in F_n$ and $f\in\BL^{\kappa}(M)$, we have that
\begin{equation*}
  \begin{aligned}
    |G^{\alpha}f(y)-G^{\alpha,n}f(y_n)|
  \lesssim&\g{c}{estres,n}\Bigl\{ \|f\|_{K_n}  (d(y,y_n)+d_{\mathrm{H}}(F,F_n))+\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(K_n)}d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu,\mu_n)\Bigr\}\\
  \leq&\g{c}{estres,n}\|f\|_{\BL^{\kappa}(K_n)}(d(y,y_n)+d_{\mathrm{H}}(F,F_n)+d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu,\mu_n)).
  \end{aligned}
\end{equation*}
Here, 
$\g{c}{estres,n}=\g{c}{estres,n}(\alpha,\delta_n)$ is defined by setting
\begin{align*}
