{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.606878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae9e44c6109d54ba1c46a323ff298492b766b03c717b4efac8fdbb7dd3ecdf50","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:est-on-Yn of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] Let $p\geqslant 1$ and $\epsilon>0$. Suppose that Assumption (ass:main1 of the paper) holds. Let $M$ be as (equation def:noise of the paper) and let  $Z^n=(X^n,V^n)$ satisfy (equation eq:SDE-EM of the paper). Then for $ Y^n:=Z^n-M$ there exists a constant $N=N(d,\beta,\|b\|_{{\mathbb C}_{\boldsymbol{a}}^\beta},\alpha,\epsilon,p)$ so that for any $(s,t)\in[0,1]_\leqslant^2$
