{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.786271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aee9ab3f7a171ea5800dc7d4eee16944618900f54d90d74d70fbc2588c0f301e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:log.concave of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists an absolute constant $C>0$ such that with $X_i^\infty$ i.i.d.\ random variables with law proportional to $e^{ - 2\beta |k|+\beta Hk}$ for $k\in \mathbb Z$ and $S_{N,H}^\infty = \sum_{i=1}^N X_i^\infty$, if $\mathbb E[S_{N,H}^\infty]=k\in\mathbb Z$ then
