{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.829926+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aeed290f6fee1b800643a31b458b7e39ae8c82f5994bda40a60477a5dbf6a67d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:antipode of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] For a weakly geometric path $X$ with reversal $\overleftarrow X$ and every word $w=(i_1\cdots i_k)$,
