{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.330655+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af0cb847c6660997603a6beec489e54e49c1c1c1150222243923afdc037d8bc0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:VDC_ball of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\mathbb{G}\cong\mathbb{R}^{m_1}\times\mathbb{R}^{m_2}$ be a Carnot group of step-2 and let $\|\cdot\|$ be any symmetric homogeneous quasinorm on $\mathbb{G}$ such that the unit ball at the identity
