{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.885419+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af164e51979feadffe8dcc22584e9599074b17c29fb6cc0e3823c796f6fc28d1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eqn:exponential mixing 1 of arXiv:2606.29352, 'Exponential Mixing for 2D Stochastic Damped Euler Equation Driven by Bounded Noise'] There exists $\bar\gamma>0$ such that, for every $\gamma\ge\bar\gamma$,
