{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.340812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af1b65457413599163ace2e927435a0db853f131137b4b20c9e8b79f8dc3407c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (Random regular graphs: averaged version) of arXiv:2604.20514, 'Macroscopic loops in the random loop model on sparse random graphs'] Fix \(d\ge 3\), \(u\in[0,1]\), and \(\theta>0\). Let \(G_n\) be the random \(d\)-regular graph on \(n\) vertices, and let \(p_{d,n}\) denote its law. Assume
