{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.214925+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_af1f58381287017cbbc5fcd6a66f5916ace328b0d1ef5ea72d6e6c985ba3db05","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.02626, 'Comparison principles and symmetry for subquadratic fractional $p$-Laplacian equations'] We call $u\in W_0^{s,p}(\Omega)$ a weak solution to (equation main of the paper) if $f(u)\in  W_0^{s, p}(\Omega)'$ and
