{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.649132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aff1bd8d2c43fb786b03614f9e4cd8d9d64e9ce3b30af968268ce6c4286a8e10","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.09419, 'Left-tail expansions for Schr\"oder branching processes with explicit convergence rates'] \lb{T1} Suppose that the probability generating function $P(z)$ is analytic in some neighborhood of $z=1$, and $E=P'(1)>1$. Then the unique solution of the Poincar\'e functional equation 
