{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.328424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0b7caa4e1384eb79e0d3dd17b70110c9654e476c9e4c23767a20cce7bf8460a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma equivensembles_bernoulli of arXiv:2606.01937, 'Stationary fluctuations for an exclusion process with mass and energy conservation'] Consider the Bernoulli product measure $\pi_\rho = \mathrm{Ber}(\rho )^{\otimes\mathbb{Z}}$ of parameter $\rho\in [0,1]$, and let $\xi$ be a random variable distributed according to $\pi_\rho$. Let $g:\{0,1\}^{\mathbb{Z}}\longrightarrow\mathbb{R}$ be a local function whose support is included in $\{0,\hdots ,\ell_0-1\}$ for some $\ell_0\ge 1$, and define the function $\varphi_g(\rho ) = \pi_\rho(g)$. Then, there exists a constant~$C_2=C_2(g)>0$ such that for any $\ell\ge\ell_0$, we have 
    \begin{equation*}
        \sup_{\xi\in\{0,1\}^{\mathbb{Z}}} \left| \pi_\rho [ g|\xi_0^\ell ] - \left(\varphi_g(\xi_0^\ell ) - \frac{1}{2\ell}\xi_0^\ell (1-\xi_0^\ell)\varphi_g''(\xi_0^\ell)\right)\right| \le \frac{C_2}{\ell^2}.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.500604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0b7ece3f3e4d96328284544a3396c9c4045449a8e69c2daaca09484efa844dd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 13 of arXiv:2608.05185, '\large\bf ON THE HEAT FLOW CONJECTURE FOR RANDOM MATRICES'] The eigenvalues of \(\mathbf{X}_{N,c}\) have joint density
\begin{equation}
 \frac{1}{\mathcal{Z}_{N,c}}
 \left|\Delta(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_N)\right|^2
 \prod_{j=1}^{N}\dd\gamma_{N;1,c,0}(\lambda_j).
\end{equation}
Here \(\mathcal{Z}_{N,c}>0\) is the normalising constant.
Relative to \(\gamma_{N;1,c,0}\), they form a determinantal point process
with correlation kernel
\begin{equation}
 K_{N,c}(z,w)
 =\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}
 \frac{h_{k,c,N}(z)\overline{h_{k,c,N}(w)}}{\kappa_{k,N}},
 \qquad
 \kappa_{k,N}=\frac{k!}{N^k}.
\end{equation}
As an integral operator on
\(\mathrm{L}^2(\gamma_{N;1,c,0})\), \(K_{N,c}\) is the orthogonal
projection onto
\[
 \mathscr{H}_{N,c}
 =\operatorname{span}\{h_{0,c,N},\ldots,h_{N-1,c,N}\}.
\]","status":"unverified"}

