{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.095801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0ec59596d4860b872da5163b6ab1b603fe93275c99e4128913d27b7254cb836","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi defi28 of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] A real valued  adapted right continuous process with left limits $(V_t)_{t\in [0,\tau]}$ is called a bounded mean oscillation $(\operatorname{BMO})$ if 
