{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.847417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1296c9e80b6f700a201d9ff46eece925821fc1c1e9f221966540952482b91c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2511.10535, 'Eigenvalues of Brownian Motions on $\mathrm{GL}(N,\mathbb{C})$'] Let $G$ be an $N\times N$ complex Ginibre or GUE matrix (having the distribution of $Z^N(1)$ or $X^N(1)$ in Definition \ref{def:GinibreBM}),
