{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.115968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b183177d465152a333264bf995701ba8b7a9e2642e74b42cab4272020d4c72a9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop-observable-singularity-continuum of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $(\nu_{\delta_{k}}^{\operatorname{oloop},h})_{k}$ be a convergent subsequence of $(\nu_{\delta}^{\operatorname{oloop},h})_{\delta}$ and denote by $\nu^{W}$ its limit. Then, there exists $c > 0$ such that for any $\iota > 0$,
