{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.644117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b18c824dba774cba8772ac7503a73709f20696ec3ca03867d335861d6efe64fb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:high lln of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $\mu=\mu_n$ be such that $c_n=\mu/n$ converges to some $c\in(0,\infty]$ and assume that $\delta_n$ admits a limit $\delta$ (possibly infinite).
