\end{align}
converges absolutely and uniformly for any compact subset of $\HH$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.062047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1a186de9309dd7ceff01cdd35c5566f62af00d25e5b2732ea9929ee0ce8bf5f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem MAIN0 of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Suppose that $\mathrm{\mathbf{A}}_p(b,\alpha,\varepsilon)$ is verified with $\overline{b}:=b-\alpha >0$ and $\delta_{h,r,k}=\gamma_r^\varepsilon$ in~(equation New6 of the paper).  Let also (equation na1a of the paper) hold with the
