{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.322055+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1e3298397f23b1bbff20c2b078d16397d47904c1707250b47615e04e1fc3310","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 39 (No extremal pair) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $\alpha > \sigma$, let $X \in \SE(\sigma^2,\alpha)$, and let $f \colon \R \to \R$ be convex and non-affine with $\E[f(\alpha \Lap)] < \infty$. Then $\E[f(X)]$ is finite and
