{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.300027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1e93fb166776d9e0bf07b3f466cd4067d2aef27b6cecc0177ef5d253ffcacec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:moment_bound of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ c, q, \rho \in (0,\infty) $, $ p \in [1,\infty) $, $ \beta \in (0,1) $ satisfy
\begin{align}\begin{split} 
  q + p \ln\beta \ge \rho
  ,
 \end{split}\end{align}
let $\mathcal V\subseteq {\mathbb R}^d$ be measurable, and let $(X,U)$ be $(c,q)$-regular on $\mathcal V$ in the sense of (def:regular of the paper). Consider for each $i\in\{1,\dots,d\}$ the stopping time
\bas{
\bar\tau=\inf\{n\in{\mathbb N}_0: \theta_n\not\in \mathcal V\}
\qquad\text{and}\qquad
\sigma^{(i)}=\inf\bigl\{n\in{\mathbb N}: v_n^{(i)}\ge c\bigr\}.
}
Then for every $ i \in \{ 1, \dots, d \} $, $ n \in {\mathbb N} $ one has
\bas{
