{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.703715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2062116a9363dcb5d6748559dc8df08ed220938d8dcaf068b0a33f03cf3bca9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm-main2 of arXiv:2608.30807, 'Isodiametric-type upper bounds for Steklov eigenvalues'] Let $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be a bounded Lipschitz domain. Then there exists a constant $C(n)>0$ such that for every $k\in \mathbb{N}$, we have
