{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.683038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b207817e3ddeca1d9d64a144aa9e79f62caaf68a62c8edd6a87c652497514ed2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main_thm of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Consider a family of local memory systems, indexed by $N$, with request processes satisfying Assumption (ass:renewal of the paper), and with intensities $\{\lambda_i^{(N)}\}_{i=1}^N$ satisfying Assumption (ass:weak_convergence of the paper). Then:
