We write $\widecheck{{\mcb{C}}}_{\mu}[{\boldsymbol{\tau}}]$ for the closure of $\widecheck{{\mcb{C}}}[{\boldsymbol{\tau}}]$ with respect to ${\vert\kern-0.25ex\vert\kern-0.25ex\vert  
    \vert\kern-0.25ex\vert\kern-0.25ex\vert}_{N,\mu}$, again dropping the scale $\mu$ from notation when it is clear from context.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:41:33.822511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2773532eac85041b62cd51b5be1dfbb607be517b83dbf25e4b721faf72f4615","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2604.10244, 'Ergodicity for regime-switching neutral stochastic functional differential equations with '] Suppose that assumptions of Lemma \ref{thm:opao1} hold. Then there exist constants $C$, $\lambda>0$  such that for any   $\xi$, $\eta \in  C_r$,  $i \in \mbb S $, and  $t\geq 0 $,
		\begin{equation}
