{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.587656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2c0f59abcd9b1357be94439a2f1aa7565a4e3b3a04a886314d32cf13ae1f61a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm-SES-IM of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let (Hypo-SES H E of the paper) hold. Suppose there exists a deterministic initial state $x_0 \in \mathbf H$ such that the following conditions are met:
