{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.904404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2fef53305edee4ac878fc9c77d545aa878d7df1b03a43785d00a069169e91d0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def block-marschak of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] Fix an arbitrary set $\Omega$, let $\cal G$ be the finitary sub-family of subsets of $\Omega$, and let $\cal F$ be the field generated by $\cal G$.  A stochastic choice rule $G \mapsto c_G(\cdot)$ satisfies the \textbf{Generalized Block-Marschak condition} if for every $H \in \cal G$, $\alpha \in H$, and $G \subseteq H\backslash\{\alpha\}$, the coefficient:
