{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.607784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b378c7fa8178e2324c4886a0054e27a7ba161e92e8555faeb88f5b9274630464","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:qua of arXiv:2412.05142, 'Strong convergence of the Euler scheme for singular kinetic SDEs driven by $\alpha$-stable'] For any $\beta\in(1-\frac{\alpha}{2},(\alpha-1)(1+\alpha))$ and any $0<\epsilon<\frac{1}{2}+\frac{(\beta-1)}{\alpha}$ there exists a constant $N=N(\alpha,\beta,d,\|b\|_{{\mathbb C}_{\boldsymbol{a}}^{\beta}},\epsilon)$ independent of $n$ so that for any $n\in{\mathbb N}$ and $k=0,1,\ldots,n$,  $(s,t)\in[\frac{k}{n},1]_\leqslant^2$ the following holds
     \begin{align}
