{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.360708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3974bb75bb68d6156dc32159252580d8d96a3accb3a4b00a1d07ebd7b95fa77","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:off-critical-decay of arXiv:2606.11503, 'Percolation on hierarchical lattices'] For any directed graph $G$ satisfying (e:hypothesis of the paper), we have
  \begin{enumerate}[\quad a)]
  \item 
    (Existence of correlation length and surface tension) The function $\xi: (0, p_\star) \to (0, \infty)$ given by
    \begin{equation}

      \xi(p) = - \lim_k \frac{\log f_k(p) }{\d_{1}(a_1, b_1)^k}
    \end{equation}
    is well-defined and non-decreasing.
    The non-increasing function $\eta: (p_\star, 1) \to (0, \infty)$,
    \begin{equation}

      \eta(p) = - \lim_k \frac{\log \big( 1- f_k(p) \big)}{\cut(G_{1})^k}
    \end{equation}
    is well-defined.
  \item 
    (Critical exponents for the correlation length and surface tension) There exist constants $\uc{c:corr_exp_1}, \uc{c:corr_exp_2} > 0$ such that
    \begin{equation}

      \uc{c:corr_exp_1} (p_\star - p)^{-\nu}
      \leq \xi(p)
      \leq \uc{c:corr_exp_2} (p_\star - p)^{-\nu},
      \text{ for $p \in (p_\star/2, p_\star)$}
    \end{equation}
    where $\nu = \log_\zeta \d_{1}(a_1, b_1)$.
    Moreover, there exist constants $\uc{c:surf_exp_1}, \uc{c:surf_exp_2} > 0$ such that
    \begin{equation}

      \uc{c:surf_exp_1} (p - p_\star)^{-\mu}
      \leq \eta(p)
      \leq \uc{c:surf_exp_2} (p - p_\star)^{-\mu},
      \text{ for $p \in (p_\star, 1 - (1-p_\star)/2)$}
    \end{equation}
    with $\mu = \log_\zeta \cut(G_{1})$.
  \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b39dab285075b791d637b19afd9c7f58bd2254b2c32b272062e58fdfe2ad8780","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given a locally-finite random point measure $\eta$ on~$\R$, a Branching Random Walk with step distribution~$\eta$ started at $x\in\R$ is a sequence
$\{\xi_k \}_{k \ge 0}$
of random locally-finite point measures on~$\R$ such that $\xi_0=\delta_x$ a.s.\ and, denoting
$\scrF_k:=\sigma(\xi_j\colon j\le k)$,
\begin{equation}

E\bigl(\texte^{-\langle\xi_{k+1},f\rangle}\,|\,\scrF_k\bigr) =\texte^{-\langle\xi_k,\tilde f\rangle}\quad\text{where}\quad\tilde f(h):=
- \log E \bigl(\texte^{-\langle \eta, f(h+\cdot) \rangle} \bigr)
