{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.724072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3bd4b673190ca200bdc46e6b71bd24e8a6df91e5a21a6e36802add2c2d1f443","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:interior_intersection_left of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $a_1 >0$, $p \in (0,1)$. Suppose $h$ is a GFF on $\delta\mathbf{D}$ with some bounded boundary values so that the angle $\theta_0$ flow line $\eta_0$ from $-i\delta$ to $i\delta$ and the angle $\theta_0$ flow line $\overline{\eta}_0$ from $i\delta$ to $-i\delta$ in the components of $\delta\mathbf{D} \setminus \eta_0$ to the right of $\eta_0$ (and reflected off $\eta_0$) are defined. Let $z_1 \in \partial B(0,\delta/2)$, $w_1 \in \partial B(0,3\delta/16)$. Let $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ be the angle $\theta_0$ flow line of $h$ starting from $z_1$ and stopped upon exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^R$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting from $w_1$, reflecting off $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(0,\delta/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^L$ be the angle $+\pi/2$ flow line starting from $w_1$ and stopped upon exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$. In case $\eta_{w_1}^R$ and $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ intersect, sample the internal metric in the regions bounded between them. 
Let $E^p$ be the event that the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item $\eta_{w_1}^R$ intersects the right side of $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ with an angle difference of $3\pi/2 - \theta_0 = 0$ (before reflecting off), and they do not intersect in any other way.
\item $\eta_{w_1}^L$ does not intersect $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$.
\item There exist $x',x,y,y' \in \eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0} \cap \eta_{w_1}^R$ such that $(x,y) \in \intptsapproxbubble{U_{x',y'}}{\epsilon}$ as in~(equation eq:intpts_bubble of the paper) and $U_{x',y'} \subseteq B(0,\delta^{1+a_1})$ and $\metapproxacres{\epsilon}{U_{x',y'}}{x}{y}{\Gamma} \geq \median{\epsilon}+\epsilon^{-a_0}\mathbf{a}_{\epsilon}$.
\item The following event has conditional probability at least $p$ given $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$, $\eta_{w_1}^R$, $\eta_{w_1}^L$, $X_\delta^{\theta_0}$, $X_\delta^{+\pi/2}$, and the values of $h$ on these sets:
\begin{itemize}
\item The flow line $\eta_0$ merges into $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ before entering $B(0,\delta/4)$.
\item The extension of $\eta_{w_1}^L$ does not intersect $\eta_0$ until it hits $\partial(\delta\mathbf{D})$.
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
Then $\mathbf{P}[E^p] = O(\delta^{{\alpha_{\mathrm{apr}}}})$ as $\delta \to 0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.785853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b3c13a1fb1c485cd55e3ceb239ead69da32e749781b78be4dd1dc5cde1bd7da6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2609.00087, 'Translational tiles without spectra\\ in finite abelian $p$-groups'] There exist explicit translational tiles without spectra in each of the
