{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.461802+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b4590a14681c27c5c2b059e8f3a71a87c23ca5c1972afb0991fd1713a13e17ac","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 8 of arXiv:2609.02561, 'NON-NEF LOCI IN MIXED CHARACTERISTIC'] A real valuation $v$ of $K(X)$ is a map $v:K(X)\rightarrow\R\cup\{\infty\}$ such that for every $f,g\in K(X)$, the following hold:
