\end{equation}
where the supremum over $\gamma$ of the right-hand side of (equation eq:sharp-bound of the paper) is attained at $\gamma=\sqrt{m/2}$. In particular, no choice of the friction coefficient produces a decay rate better than $O(\sqrt m)$, so that the scaling of Theorem~(thm:main of the paper) cannot be improved.","status":"unverified"}

