{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.188987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b56fd0e110513926f14c0d57ec019b11b6273fb744128e0a38fc949527226645","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2606.30938, 'Poissonian potential measures for refracted-reflected L\'evy processes'] Let $p,q \geq 0$ and $\lambda,\gamma> 0$. Then, for $x,b \in [0,a]$, we have that 
			\begin{align}
				\E_x \Bigl( \ee^{-q T_{a,U}^{+,\lambda} - p \int_0^{T_{a,U}^{+,\lambda}} 1_{\left\{U_s<b\right\}} \mathrm{d} s} \; \1_{\{T_{a,U}^{+,\lambda} < T_{b,U}^{-,\gamma}\}}\Bigr) &=  \frac{\overline{z}_b^{(q+\gamma_p, -\gamma_p)}(x)}{\varphi_{q+\lambda} \int^\infty_0 \ee^{-\varphi_{q+\lambda}y}\overline{z}_b^{(q+\gamma_p, -\gamma_p)}(y+a) \dd y},  

