{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.074327+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b586bad69957c0ade448a79a3513e38252101a296f38c393df8b82a3d04be5c5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo full_dist of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] Assume the same hypothesis as in (theo:excha of the paper). For any $b\in\{1,\cdots,k\}$, any partition $(J_0,\cdots,J_{b-1})$ of the set $\{0,\cdots,k-1\}$ with non-empty parts, any sequence $(a_0, \cdots,a_{b-1})$ in ${\cal C}^b$ such that the $a_0, \cdots,a_{b-1}$ are cyclically ordered around ${\cal C}$ (i.e.\ such that turning around the circle we get $a_0\preceq 0\preceq a_1\preceq \cdots \preceq a_{b-1}\preceq a_0 \preceq 0 \cdots$) and such that
