{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.381294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b592d37f3705a85ef422dba8f6dc0c286ba6faef4e75b395733ed99160e1dac3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:global_hajek of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] As in (equation eq:hatngdef of the paper), let us write
\begin{equation}
    \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G(x) = \mathsf{N}_G(x) - 2 \mathsf{e} p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} \mathsf{E}(x).
\end{equation}
Then, for all $\zeta \in (0,1)$, there is some $c > 0$ such that
