{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.346406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5a2d10196b9dd5a9f93c80b148463295527cb9a4267e202dbf5930199995709","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2607.15125, '2607.15125'] (Flajolet - Odlyzko \cite{flajolet1990singularity})  
Assume that, with the sole exception of the singularity $z=1$, $F(z)$ is analytic in the domain $\Delta(\epsilon,\theta) \coloneqq \{z : \abs{z} \le 1 + \epsilon,  \abs{\mathrm{Arg}(z-1)} \ge \theta \}$ where $\epsilon > 0$ and $\pi/2 <\theta < \pi$. Assume further that as $z$ tends to 1 in $\Delta$,
