{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.924793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5d0963f1770d1c234ccab1f174b0178aaeae4d4679bcc937b7e858312a0ab29","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:tight1 of arXiv:2412.02160, 'A functional central limit theorem for weighted occupancy processes of the Karlin model'] Assume $|a_{i+j}-a_i| \le Cj^\beta$ with $\beta\in[0,\alpha/2)$. 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item For all 
$p\in[1,\alpha/{2\beta})$,
 we have, for some constant $C$, 
\begin{equation}
{\mathbb E}\abs{\what W_n(t)-\what W_n(s)}^{2p} \le C \pp{\sigma_n^2|t-s|^{\alpha} + \sigma_n^{2p}|t-s|^{\alpha p}}, \mbox{ for all } 0\le s<t\le 1, n\in{\mathbb N}.
\end{equation}
\item For some constant $C>0$, almost surely, 
\begin{equation}
\abs{\what W_n(t)-\what W_n(s)}\le C (N(nt)-N(ns) + n(t-s)), \mbox{ for all } 0\le s\le t\le 1.
\end{equation} 
\end{enumerate}
As a consequence, if in addition 
\[
\beta\in\bigg[0,\frac{\alpha^2}2\bigg) \quad\mbox{ and }\quad p\in\pp{\frac1\alpha,\frac{\alpha}{2\beta}}, 
\]
the process $\sigma_n^{-1}\what W_n$ is tight in $D([0,1])$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.413767+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5d628b70e6e73e92e63b1d95bc1330ab19a1888f1421ef8eaefdf504f2fee64","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 17 of arXiv:2606.08115, '2606.08115'] Let $\{S_n\}$ be a random walk with increments $X_j$, $\ex X_j = 0$, $\ex X_j^2 = \sigma^2 \in (0, +\infty)$. Then for any $\alpha > 0$ there exists a parameter $C$ such that for every sufficiently large natural $n$ the inequality
