\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:43:45.397308+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5e8a1b9a45618b2561beae9a42eb5720ad209cd40ceb55133fd5271ebf8d705","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 46 ({\cite[Theorem~6.2) of arXiv:2609.04139, 'The conformally invariant metric on CLE$_4$ II:\\ existence of geodesics'] {zhan2019two}}]

Let $v_-, w_-, w_+, v_+ \in \BR$ with $v_- < w_- < w_+ < v_+$ be such that $0 \in [v_-, v_+]$. Let $(\eta_+,\eta_-)$ be a bichordal SLE$_4$ in $\BH$ with link pattern $\{\{w_+, v_+\}, \{w_-, v_-\}\}$. Then, there exists a universal constant $C \in (0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{equation*}
    \BP[\text{both } \eta_+ \text{ and } \eta_- \text{ exit } B_L(0)] \leq C L^{-4} G_1(w_-, w_+; v_-, v_+) \left(1 + C((v_+ - v_-) / L)^{5/6}\right)
\end{equation*}
for all $L > 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.529378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5ea7560569e2f4781c28804b23b2e6129f71d3e7a6b9c5dae80a2e70e3023cd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:uniform-profile-tail of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[definition]{def:uniform-profile-tail}
We say that the random field satisfies \(({\rm PT})_p\) if, for every
