{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.897335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b654bdc0d2c10d117108320f4d569a069a2fe8018b8fcbcb04a5fd864e129798","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm thm:drago of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] There exists real number $T_0>0$ such that the following holds for any $T\ge T_0$.
