{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.473979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7ba5adad4daf82cc1ff4f36dd1294ddd2973ad82d07ca0f38b957674bb077c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:sharp-nonlinear-constant of arXiv:2606.21006, 'Law of the Iterated Logarithm for Weighted Sums of Functionals of Long-Memory Gaussian Seq'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:functional-nonlinear-lil of the paper),
\[
    \limsup_{n\to\infty}
    \frac{|S_n|}
    {A_n(2\log\log n)^{m/2}}
    =
    \Lambda_m
    \qquad\text{\rm a.s.},
\]
where the deterministic constant is given by the variational formula
\[

    \Lambda_m
    =
    \sup_{\|\xi\|_{\mathfrak H_{\mathbb R}}\le1}
    \left|
        \big\langle Q_1,\xi^{\otimes m}
        \big\rangle_{\mathfrak H_{\mathbb R}^{\otimes m}}
    \right|.
\text{      Moreover, }
    0<L_{m,\alpha,d} 
    \le
    \Lambda_m
    \le
    \frac{1}{\sqrt{m!}},
\]
where
\[
    L_{m,\alpha,d}
    :=
    \left(\frac{2-\alpha}{2(1-\alpha)}\right)^{m/2}
    \frac{
        \displaystyle
        \sum_{k=0}^{m}
        \binom{m}{k}
        \mathrm B\!\left(
            1-d+(1-\alpha)k,\,
            1+(1-\alpha)(m-k)
        \right)
    }
    {
        \sqrt{m!\,I_{m,\alpha,d}}
    },
\]
and
\[
    I_{m,\alpha,d}
    =
    \frac{
        2\,\mathrm B(1-d,\,1-\alpha m)
    }
    {
        2-2d-\alpha m
    }.
\]
Here \(\mathrm B(\cdot,\cdot)\) denotes the beta function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.304132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7c08080668ce3d5891554e927692c418fa5676b8920da77a4923af43bf2c3f3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop procov of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] \begin{align}
     \lim_{i \rightarrow + \infty} i^{-(2\alpha+2)/(1-\alpha)} \mathbb{E}\Big( \big(\sum_{j\leq i} (\overline{Z}_{\rho_j}-\overline{Z}_{\eta_{j}})-\mathbb{E}(\overline{Z}_{\rho_j}-\overline{Z}_{\eta_{j}})  \big)^2\Big) 
