{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.043249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8162e9c226e9cb62030b5f3ec40236138bb1edbbb0e8609375091342d4732ce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 69 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] The function $G_{\cA}$ is Borel measurable,
