{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.460510+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b84d3324717d88939fe2de72f8a3630279b982c3f59edb74ab62a0c4eaea42e4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 14 (Comparison for the penalized equation) of arXiv:2607.28238, 'Well-posedness and large deviations for the obstacle problem of first-order stochastic con'] Let $1\leq n\leq m$, and let $u_n$ and $u_m$ be kinetic solutions of the corresponding penalized equations, with initial data $u_n^0$ and $u_m^0$, respectively.
Then, for almost every $t\in(0,T)$,
\begin{align*}
\E\bigl\|(u_n(t)-u_m(t))^+\bigr\|_{L^1(\mathbb T^N)}\leq\bigl\|(u_n^0-u_m^0)^+\bigr\|_{L^1(\mathbb T^N)}.
\end{align*}
If $u_n^0=u_m^0=u^0$, then we have $u_n\leq u_m$ a.s.
Consequently, the family $(u_n)_{n\geq1}$ is non-decreasing.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.863092+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b850fc27799613e7bf90dade4174f40e3c759d0d4bb0b48c56edf6d0b0571f6e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $\lambda>0$ and let $\varphi_\lambda(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\lambda}}e^{-\frac{x^2}{2\lambda}}$ be the density of a centered Gaussian with variance $\lambda$. 
        \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\forall x\in\mathbb{R},\;\forall \gamma\in(0,1],\; |x|\varphi_\lambda(x)\le (e\gamma)^{-\frac12} \lambda^{\frac{1-\gamma}{2}} \varphi_\lambda^{1-\gamma}(x)$,
            \item $\forall x,y \in \mathbb{R}\mbox{ with }|x-y|<\eps,\;\forall \gamma\in(0,1],\;\varphi_\lambda(y) \ge (2\pi\lambda)^{\frac\gamma2}\varphi_\lambda(x)^{1+\gamma} e^{-\frac{\eps^2}{\gamma \lambda}} $,
        \item $\forall x\in\mathbb{R},\;\forall \gamma>0,\; \varphi_\lambda^{1+\gamma}(x)\le {(2\pi\lambda)}^{-\frac\gamma2} \varphi_\lambda(x).$
        \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.074928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b85448df9f6fa6b9041c92baf28aa3c527c18d345ba2a37591aa0e15b7dcb661","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ODE-embedding of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Let $\mathcal{Y}^{(0)}:=d\mathcal{S}^{(0)}$ associated to $(S,(x^{(0)}_{e})_{e\in E(\mathbb{Z}^2)})$. Assume also that the collection of masses $(m_e)_{e\in \mathbb{Z}^2}$ vanishes outside the box $\Lambda$. Consider the differential system defined on corners of $ \Upsilon^{\times} \cap  \Lambda  $, whose initial condition is given by $\mathcal{Y}^{(0)}$ and whose dynamic is given for any $\frak{p} \in \Lambda $ by
		\begin{equation}
		\frac{d \mathcal{Y}^{(t)}(\frak{p})}{dt}= \frac{1}{2} \sum\limits_{z_k \in \Lambda}m_k \Bigg[ \mathcal{Y}^{(t)}(c^+_k) \langle \chi_{\frak{p}}\chi_{a^+_k} \rangle_{S(t)} -  \mathcal{Y}^{(t)}(a^+_k) \langle \chi_{\frak{p}}\chi_{c^+_k} \rangle_{S(t)} \Bigg].
	\end{equation}
Then 
\begin{enumerate}
	\item There exist $T_0(\Lambda)>0$ such that the ODE (equation eq:ODE-embedding of the paper) is well defined on $[0;T_0(\Lambda)] $.
	\item For any time $0\leq t \leq T_0(\Lambda) $, the fermion $\mathcal{Y}^{(t)}$ solution to (equation eq:ODE-embedding of the paper) constructs an s-embedding $\mathcal{S}^{(t)}$ of the Ising model $S(t)$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.136322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b85b2392d6040c8f56f2ab2378a2334d0d8d5ccc41d3d45282ad7816239cdf9e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn ofn of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] Assume that $\gamma:[0,T]\to R^d$ is a bounded variation path and $(0,0)=\gamma_0\neq\gamma_T$. We define the associated (with $\gamma$, $T$) normalization operator $\mathcal{A}=\mathcal{A}_{\gamma,T}$ by
$$
\mathcal{A}(\alpha)_t:=k^{-1}A\alpha_t,~\forall~t\in[0,S],
$$
where $\alpha:[0,S]\to R^d$ is a bounded variation path, the rotation $A$ and the scaling $k$ are given by  
\begin{equation}
A
=\left(
\begin{array}{cc}
\cos(\theta) & \sin(\theta) \\
-\sin(\theta) &\cos(\theta)\\
\end{array} 
\right)
=\frac{1}{|\gamma_T|}\left(
\begin{array}{cc}
 x_T & y_T \\
-y_T & x_T\\
\end{array} 
\right),\quad\quad k=|\gamma_T|.
\end{equation}
For any one-form $f(\cdot):=\left(
\begin{array}{c}
f_1  \\
f_2 \\
\end{array} 
\right)(\cdot)$, we define its adjoint operator $\mathcal{A}^*$ by 
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal{A}^*(f)(\cdot)=k^{-1} A^{-1}\left(
\begin{array}{l}
f_1  \\
f_2 \\
\end{array} 
\right)\left(k^{-1}A\cdot\right)
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.441451+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8617e1c1f18ad07ce2c903979560cefc7a7088c0dfe6dabd1b77c4a34bcaced","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro:tail_bound of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Under the assumption of Theorem (thm:main_thm of the paper), if $x>0$ and $x^2 t_N N^{-\frac{1}{3}}< c_0$ for some small absolute constant, then there exist constants $c, C>0$, such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}\Big(\|\frac{1}{2}X\|_{\mathrm{op}}>1+xN^{-\frac{2}{3}}\Big)\le C(1+ e^{C \tau x})e^{-c x^{\frac{3}{2}}}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.771699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b861852e0f3af008eef625ccac33ebe7ee805a527882ebb5d890a57bed77d7a9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 (\cite{Cerrai2001}) of arXiv:2512.05340, 'The rate of convergence of the critical mean-field $O(N)$ magnetization via multivariate n'] Let $V$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{assumption: assumptions on V}. For $u\in\RR^d$ and $t>0$, define
\begin{equation}
        I_{u}^{x}(t) := \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}t}\int_{0}^{t}\<\,\sU_{u}^x(s), \dbs \>.
\end{equation}
Then for any $\varphi \in C_{b}$, any $t>0$ and any $u,v,w\in\RR^d$ it holds that,
\begin{equation}
  D_{u}P_{t}\varphi(x) = \EE\left\< \grad\varphi(X_{t}^{x}),\,\sU_{u}^x(t)\right\>,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
  \begin{split}
  D^{2} P_{t}\varphi(x)[u,v] &= \EE\left(D P_{t/2}\varphi(X_{t/2}^{x})[\sU_{u}^x(t/2)]I_{v}^{x}(t/2)\right) \\
  &\quad +\frac{2}{t}\EE\int_{0}^{t/2}D P_{t-s}\varphi(X_{s}^{x})[\sU_{u,v}^x(s)]\, \ds,
  \end{split}
\end{equation}
and 
\begin{equation}
  D^{3} P_{t}\varphi(x)[u,v,w] = K_1^{x,t}(u,v,w) + K_2^{x,t}(u,v,w) + K_3^{x,t}(u,v,w) + K_4^{x,t}(u,v,w) + K_4^{x,t}(v,u,w)
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}
K_1^{x,t}(u,v,w)&:= \EE \,\left(D^{2} P_{t/2}\varphi(X_{t/2}^{x})[\,\sU_{u}^x(t/2),\sU_{v}^x(t/2)] I_{w}^{x}(t/2)\right) \\
K_2^{x,t}(u,v,w)&:= \EE \,\left(D P_{t/2}\varphi(X_{t/2}^{x})[\sU_{u,v}^x(t/2)]I_{w}^{x}(t/2)\right)\\ 
K_3^{x,t}(u,v,w)&:= \frac{2}{t}\EE\int_{0}^{t/2}D P_{t-s}\varphi(X_{s}^{x})[\,\sU_{u,v,w}^x(s)]\, \ds,\\
K_4^{x,t}(u,v,w)&:= \frac{2}{t}\EE\int_{0}^{t/2}D^{2} P_{t-s}\varphi(X_{s}^{x})[\sU_{u,v}^x(s), \,\sU_w^x(s)]\, \ds.
  \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:56.960843+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8659cc3acd1562b954123c04597e91c4f34332b43880453b02ed23c7deb054a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma E[weak-sl]_asymp of arXiv:2604.05921, 'Simplicity of random hypergraphs'] If $\forall e \in E: \delta_e^{\textnormal{tail}} = \delta^{\textnormal{tail}}\in O(1)$ and $\delta_e^{\textnormal{head}} = \delta^{\textnormal{head}}\in O(1)$ and 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathds{E}[(d_U^{\textnormal{out}})^{\delta^{\textnormal{tail}}}(d_U^{\textnormal{in}})^{\delta^{\textnormal{head}}}] \in o(n)$
    \item $\exists c>0 \textnormal{ s.t.}    \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \mathds{P}(d_U^{\textnormal{out}} \geq \delta^{\textnormal{tail}}), \mathds{P}(d_U^{\textnormal{in}} \geq \delta^{\textnormal{head}}) \geq c$
\end{enumerate}
then
\begin{align*}
    \mathds{E}[WS_n] &= \Big( \frac{\delta^{\textnormal{tail}} + \delta^{\textnormal{head}}-2}{2} + \frac{\delta^{\textnormal{head}} \mathds{E}[d_U^{\textnormal{out}}d_U^{\textnormal{in}}]}{\mathds{E}[d_U^{\textnormal{in}}]} \Big)(1+o(1)).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.363464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b865a510653794a93265a8de301c95eb9048fdbcb7f6a7ce55f0134453d83c05","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Consistency and rate for \textup{($iii$)}) of arXiv:2608.29465, 'Deciding When to Decide:\\Testing Operational Suboptimality Under Distributional Shift'] Suppose the assumptions of Lemma~\ref{lem:termI_consistency} hold, specifically the square-integrability of the envelope and Lipschitz modulus under $\mathbb{P}_1$. Let $\varepsilon_{m''}$ denote the uniform convergence rate of the empirical OCE risk over the evaluation sample. It holds that:
\begin{equation}

|\textup{($iii$)}|
\le
2\sup_{\theta\in\Theta}\sup_{z\in\mathcal Z}
\Big|
\rho^{\widehat{\mathbb P}_1''}\!\big(f(z;X,\theta)\big)
-
\rho^{\mathbb P_1}\!\big(f(z;X,\theta)\big)
