	\end{equation} where $(B_s)_{s \in [0,T]}$ is a Brownian motion starting from $\sqrt{t}$ with variance $\frac{1}{2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.017255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b8961dbb136fb2509383b3436d8d1ff033b7cd2a4ad33307cbe70e713ea03b41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:geom-intro of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d\ge 1$.
