{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.766721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b95b27e4563a1b3091aba98b40db6c3d563295c53b529c0fd463f1251e4eb474","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] There exists a unique line ensemble $\hsai = \{\hsai_{i}\}_{i \geq 1}$ on $[0, \infty)$, which satisfies the following properties. Firstly, the line ensemble is ordered, meaning that almost surely
\begin{equation}
\hsai_{1}(t) \geq \hsai_{2}(t) \geq \cdots \mbox{ for all } t \in [0,\infty).
\end{equation}
In addition, if $\mathsf{S} = \{s_1, \dots, s_m\} \subset (0,\infty)$, then the random measure
\begin{equation}
\hsmi(\omega, A) = \sum_{i \geq 1} \sum_{j = 1}^m {\bf 1}\{(s_j, \hsai_i(s_j,\omega) ) \in A\}
\end{equation}
is a Pfaffian point process on $\mathbb{R}^2$ with reference measure $\mu_{\mathsf{S}} \times \mathrm{Leb}$ as in Definition \ref{Def.Measures} and correlation kernel $\hski$, given by
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\hski(s,x; t,y) = \begin{bmatrix}
    \hski_{11}(s,x;t,y) & \hski_{12}(s,x;t,y)\\
    \hski_{21}(s,x;t,y) & \hski_{22}(s,x;t,y) 
\end{bmatrix} \\
&= \begin{bmatrix}
    \hsii_{11}(s,x;t,y) & \hsii_{12}(s,x;t,y) + \hsri_{12}(s,x;t,y) \\
    -\hsii_{12}(t,y;s,x) - \hsri_{12}(t,y;s,x) & \hsii_{22}(s,x;t,y) + \hsri_{22}(s,x;t,y) 
\end{bmatrix},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where the kernels $\hsii_{ij}, \hsri_{ij}$ are defined as follows. We have
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\hsii_{11}(s,x;t,y) = &\frac{1}{(2\pi \im)^2} \int_{\mathcal{C}_{1+s}^{\pi/3}}dz \int_{\mathcal{C}_{1+t}^{\pi/3}} dw \frac{(z + s - w - t)H(z,x;w,y)}{4(z + s + w + t)(z+s)(w+ t)}, \\
\hsii_{12}(s,x;t,y) = &\frac{1}{(2\pi \im)^2} \int_{\mathcal{C}_{1+s}^{\pi/3}}dz \int_{\mathcal{C}_{1+t}^{\pi/3}} dw \frac{(z + s - w + t) H(z,x;w,y)}{2(z+ s)(z + s + w -t)}, \\
\hsii_{22}(s,x;t,y) = &\frac{1}{(2\pi \im)^2} \int_{\mathcal{C}_{1+ s}^{\pi/3}}dz \int_{\mathcal{C}_{1+t}^{\pi/3}} dw \frac{(z - s - w + t)H(z,x;w,y)}{z - s + w - t},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
where we have set 
\begin{equation}
H(z,x;w,y) = e^{z^3/3 + w^3/3 - xz - y w},
\end{equation}
and the contours $\mathcal{C}_{z}^{\varphi}$ are as in Definition \ref{Def.S1Contours}. We also have that 
\begin{equation}
\hsri_{12}(s,x;t,y) = - \frac{{\bf 1}\{s < t\} }{\sqrt{4\pi (t-s)}} \cdot \exp \left(\frac{- (s-t)^4 + 6 (x+ y)(s-t)^2 + 3 (x-y)^2}{12 (s-t)} \right), 
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\hsri_{22}(s,x;t,y) = \frac{H(s,x;t,y) (y-t^2 -x + s^2) }{2\pi^{1/2} (t+s)^{3/2} } \cdot \exp \left(-\frac{(y - t^2 - x +s^2)^2}{4(t+s)}\right).
\end{split}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.122765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b95ce56a50a1a500c4f79d5940df67fa633063fcf51f1c80c4460f5aba13b9ca","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2602.00853, 'Mixing times for the stochastic $p$-Laplace equation'] Let $p\ge 2$. We say that $\{X_t\}_{t\in [0,T]}$ is a \emph{variational solution} to (equation eq:pLaplace of the paper) for initial data $x_0\in H$ if
