{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.821823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_badf25af71d5bf0e275e1ca9f63567d12bdffdacbc8f0e1cd3962104765cec30","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th: a priori branched0 of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] Assume that $\Upsilon_\tau$ is globally Lipschitz continuous for all $\tau\in{\mathcal T}^{\leq N}$. Then, for sufficiently small $\varepsilon:=T\wedge\mu$ and $Z$ any solution of (equation eq:davie of the paper), 
