{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.350121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baf82ba9e7ab7042eb7dfcb896371615bdf3f65ec0068af5f34f1303ed56c04a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:typewise_mean_error of arXiv:2609.02491, 'Generalised Random Parking for Trapeziums on a Strip'] There exists a finite constant $C>0$ such that, for all $x>(3a-b)/2$,
