{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:48:24.615250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb23888ea9b9526f18061851b103357b5c221f9efe33b3d4d9f8d3b644c963d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tv-ber-lb of arXiv:2601.04079, 'TV homogenization inequalities'] For $\textup{{\bf p}},\textup{{\bf q}}\in[0,1]^n$,
let $I=\left\{ i\in[n]:p_i\ge q_i \right\}$ and $J=[n]\setminus I$,
with
$\textup{{\bf p}}_I,\textup{{\bf p}}_J,\textup{{\bf q}}_I,\textup{{\bf q}}_J$ the corresponding subsequences of $\textup{{\bf p}},\textup{{\bf q}}$.
Then
\begin{eqnarray*}
\TV(\Ber(\textup{{\bf p}}),\Ber(\textup{{\bf q}}))
&\ge&
\max\paren{
\TV(\Ber(\textup{{\bf p}}_I),\Ber(\textup{{\bf q}}_I))
,
\TV(\Ber(\textup{{\bf p}}_J),\Ber(\textup{{\bf q}}_J))
}\\
&\ge&
\frac{1}{9}
\max(
\Phi(\textup{{\bf p}}_I,\textup{{\bf q}}_I)
,
\Phi(\textup{{\bf q}}_J,\textup{{\bf p}}_J)
).
\end{eqnarray*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.893675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb2538716ec5a847b618912fce5d8899f2fc85e69dc5e9d7002d2b2ebc1b95fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 of arXiv:2606.18877, 'Ergodic Properties of Non-Linear Density-Dependent Perturbations of the Ornstein--Uhlenbec'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:main}, assuming also that \(b_0>\kappa/2\), it holds that
    \[
