{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.342330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb36b70de98da22fc0f7772fd212d03855e98694128d83daee215969ca65c289","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] If $N$ is Poisson with mean $\mu>0$, then, for every fixed real $r\ge1$,
\begin{equation*}
 \frac{\E[N^r]}{\mu}\ll_r(1+\mu)^{r-1}.
