{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.741140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb6d41e95c4a92b5ffde81e326a7c7a7da7bb12d2f2f26cde76ca19711e76416","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:spectral_absorption of arXiv:2603.24803, 'Critical Spectral Invariants in Random Walks with Geometric Resetting'] For $k \ge 1$ and $z \in \{1,\dots,a-1\}$, the finite-time absorption 
probabilities admit the spectral decompositions
\begin{align}

u_{z,k} &= \sum_{\nu=1}^{a-1} A_\nu(z)\, \lambda_\nu^{\,k}, \\[6pt]

v_{z,k} &= \sum_{\nu=1}^{a-1} B_\nu(z)\, \lambda_\nu^{\,k},
\end{align}
where $v_{z,k} := \mathbb{P}_z(\tau_a = k, \tau_a < \tau_0)$ is the 
probability of success at time $k$, and the spectral coefficients are given by
\vspace{0.3cm}

{\small 
\begin{equation}

A_\nu(z) = \frac{2}{a} \left( \frac{q}{p} \right)^{z/2}
\sin\!\left( \frac{\pi \nu z}{a} \right)
\sin\!\left( \frac{\pi \nu}{a} \right)
\end{equation}
}

{\small
\begin{equation}

B_\nu(z) = \frac{2}{a} \left( \frac{p}{q} \right)^{(a-z)/2}
\sin\!\left( \frac{\pi \nu (a-z)}{a} \right)
\sin\!\left( \frac{\pi \nu}{a} \right)
\end{equation}
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.737638+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb6e7e1d80a15a07e44fd43c254b3e71eccc026669a55329554717985f8ff4ca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 37 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] For \(T>R\geq e\),
\begin{equation}
