{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:43:04.727236+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bb827b92abebb9dc6271b9d169d77e883eecd45bcc7c40294bcccb797da4c5dc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2605.17494, 'Generalized intersection exponents and local cut points for three-dimensional Brownian loo'] There exist constants $c_1,c_2$ such that the following. For every $0<\epsilon<\frac{1}{2}$, define
    $$V^-=((u+A_{\frac{1}{20}})\cup \mathcal{B}_{\frac{\epsilon}{2}}(u))\cap \mathcal{B}_e, V=((u+A)\cup \mathcal{B}_{\epsilon}(u))\cap \mathcal{B}_e.$$
