{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.992604+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbb9fb6f261db2eec4d46271544572d1a785b723770cadb6775be008ac9860c0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem3 of arXiv:2412.01070, 'A note on Lévy-driven McKean-Vlasov SDEs under monotonicity'] Assume that Assumptions $({\bf B}_0)$-$({\bf B}_{3})$  hold, and suppose further $X_0\in L^\beta(\Omega^1\to\mathbb R^d,\mathscr F^1_0,\mathbb{P}^1)$.
