{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.284068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bbc325212c38a759e496fdaaa2d59d8f03cde4f535411cab64963188306a3339","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem cor1-1 of arXiv:2411.01731, '$L^2$-Wasserstein contraction of modified Euler schemes for SDEs with high diffusivity and'] Assume that $({\bf A}_0)$, $ ({\bf A}_2)$,  $ ({\bf A}_3)$ and $ ({\bf A}_5)$ hold.
