{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:11:35.812202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc374ed6bff32d729c40cf84bdca842c905aa57ac764a5dc1fbdaf6f52ef40d8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:2.1.1 of arXiv:2607.18505, 'A Vector Space Approach to Heavy Tailed Analysis'] We say an arbitrary random variable $X$ is trivially normalized by a given normalizing function $b$ provided that for all $x>0$
