    We say that the $\kappa$-MLFE{} with potentials $(U, W)$ is \emph{well-posed} if for all $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ there is a linear growth solution to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, \infty)$ with initial condition $\lambda$ that is unique among the class of linear growth solutions.","status":"unverified"}

