{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.743892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bc72fa2a812cbab7dabdac6b362c2d2414690e760f19a18ae30a0976875de5c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 53 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] We fix $\alpha \ino (1, 2]$ and we assume that $\mu$ satisfies (\ref{hypostaintro}). Recall from (\ref{aennedef}) the definition of $(a_n)_{n\in \bbN^*}$. 
