    if $a = b$.
    The constant $C$ is independent $a,b$, and $\varepsilon$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.359852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd256a12f9bdf7d07755ba956dbd52eda57a5d00a014cdab54ebcbe886c754f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mainthm of arXiv:2605.16244, 'Analysis of a twisted Bose--Einstein Markov chain with applications to sampling Catalan st'] Fix $n \geq 2$. 
Let $K_{\mathrm{PF}}$ be the transition kernel of the Burnside process on $\mathrm{PF}_n$ and let $\pi_{\mathrm{PF}}$ be its stationary distribution. 
Then $\lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}} = \lambda_2(K_{\mathrm{PF}}) = \frac{n}{2(n+1)}$, and for all $t\ge1$, 
\begin{equation}
 \max\left\{
  \frac{n}{n+2}\lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}}^t,\,
  1-\frac{t+\log 3}{\log n}
 \right\}
 \le d_{K_{\mathrm{PF}}}(t)
 \le n\sqrt{\frac{n+1}{2}} \lambda_{2,\mathrm{PF}}^{t/2}.

\end{equation}
Consequently, for every fixed $0<\varepsilon<1$,
\[
 t_{\mathrm{mix},K_{\mathrm{PF}}}(\varepsilon)=\Theta_\varepsilon(\log n).
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.635461+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd3496f9a97fb78fb8aa6974123d335cf7635aea64567b0fd5ef7df4100452fe","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem maintheorem_with_simplices of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $f\colon \mathbb N^s \to \mathbb C$ satisfy (mainassumption of the paper) and be real and non-negative or satisfy (upperboundassp of the paper) as well. Assume that the polytope $\cal P$ is bounded, that $\cal F$ is not contained in any coordinate hyperplane, and that $\vec \ell$ is of convergent type for $\cal F$. 
    Dissect the polytope $\cal P$ into simplices and let $S_1,\ldots, S_h$ be those simplices that have exactly $d+1$ vertices in the maximal face $\cal F$, where $d = \dim \cal F$. Let the constants $C_{S_j}$ be as in (lem:simplex_computation of the paper) and $\cal F_{S_j} = \cal F \cap S_j$ for $1\leq j\leq h$.

