{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.420442+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be66195d23ec779dba618bd17c2ffadd312255bd8af9ad8cb35913eb015918bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj:conjectural_limit_of_full_barcode_kernel of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] The following limit exists for all $t,s\in \mathbb{Z}$:
