	\begin{equation}
	    c\int_0^\infty \mathrm{QT}(W_1,W_2,W_3;\ell,\ell)\, d\ell.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.326649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bec62d18a89a9c4f4b9d0462755fda432e84329553f9072dd1f436436b1738f6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:localized_SMR of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $\nu>0$ and let $Q=I\times B$ be a parabolic cylinder of side length $\varrho\in (0,1/2]$. Suppose that $(\zeta_n)_n : I\times \Omega\times B \to \ell^2$ is progressively measurable, and that there exist $M>0$ and $\nu_0\in (0,\nu)$ such that 
