{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.634473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf55e7a71607ef62dd970ce73b56562850b25a9c622ca81d92e5438266a8bc4b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 15 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] A classical spin model satisfies Pfaffian relations on $W \subset V$ if and only if for every non-planar pair $(A,B)$, 
