{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.033279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bfa79862e666fcec8ddd616ff596016a99db1517ba8b96434b3c9aa0d0b2b4eb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Fixed-time regularity of functionals of the decoupled flow) of arXiv:2605.03057, 'Uniform-in-time quantitative fluctuations of large scale interacting particle systems'] Let Assumption \ref{ass:flow-smothness} hold. Let $ \varphi \in C_b^7\left( \R^d \right) $.
For $ t \ge 0 $, $ x \in \R^d $, and $ \mu \in \Ptwo $, let $ X_t^{x,\mu} $ be the decoupled flow
