{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.465777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c14944f7f9d248aaa33b9a4ea91138bb7a02c61f98be0b6a00fff60808e60a0c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3G of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Fix small constants $\epsilon,\tau>0$. For any deterministic matrices $\|A_1\|+\|A_2\| \lesssim 1$ and vectors $\|{\bm x}\|, \|{\bm y}\| \lesssim 1$, the following holds
	\begin{equation}

		\Big| \big\langle {\bm x}, \big( G^{z_1}(\mathrm{i} \eta_1)A_1G^{z_2}(\mathrm{i} \eta_2)A_2G^{z_1}(\mathrm{i} \eta_1)-M_{121}^{A_1,A_2}\big) {\bm y} \big \rangle \Big|\prec \frac{1}{\eta_*\gamma}.
	\end{equation}
	uniformly for any $ |z_i|\leq 1+\tau$ and $\min_{i=1}^2 \{|\eta_i| \rho_i \} \geq n^{-1+\epsilon}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.083899+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c14bd911b6425c49a3b219d9e3d62e40650cbbfb5c1f48b448f182d8ad6a9685","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem i=0 of arXiv:2412.08334, 'Maker-Breaker on Galton-Watson trees'] Consider $\xi$ with $p_0=0$, where as before $p_k=\mathbb{P}(\xi=k)$, for $k\in\mathbb{N}_0$, is the distribution's pmf and $g$ its pgf. Then the probability $p$ of Breaker winning on a GW-tree arising from offspring distribution $\xi$, when the nodes carry no further information is a solution to
	\begin{equation}
		x^2=g(x).
	\end{equation}
    It is equal to $0$ if $p_1=0$, to $1$ if $\mu\leq 2,\ p_1>0$ and to the (unique) solution in $(0,1)$ in all non-trivial cases ($\mu>2,\ p_1>0$). When Maker begins, the probability of Breaker winning becomes $\bar{p}=g(p)=p^2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.343885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c14d337c30a1483913145d0ca68991b0f16e5b8c47d39066ae1de34549ffd466","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def weighted stable nodal family of arXiv:2609.04023, 'Characterizing Contractions and Weighted Blowdowns'] \begin{enumerate}
    \item Define input data to be a tuple $(g,\mathscr{A}):=(g,a_1,\dots,a_n)$ consisting of an integer $g\ge 0$ and the {\em weight data} $(a_1,\dots,a_n)\in \mathbb{Q}^n$ satisfying $0<a_j\leq 1$ for $j=1,\ldots,n$ and $2g-2+a_1+a_2+\dots +a_n>0$.
    \item A family of nodal curves with marked points $(C,s_1,\ldots,s_n)\xrightarrow{\pi}B$ is stable of type $(g,\mathscr{A})$ if
    \begin{itemize}
        \item the sections $s_1,\ldots,s_n$ lie in the smooth locus of $\pi$,
        \item for any $\{i_1,\dots, i_r\}\subseteq [n]$ such that $\bigcap_{j=1}^{r}s_{i_j}(B)\neq\emptyset$, we have $a_{i_1}+\dots +a_{i_r}\leq 1$ and,
        \item $K_{\pi}+a_1s_1+a_2s_2+\dots +a_ns_n$ is $\pi$-ample.
    \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.353475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1595e46cc99ff0ce360d3ef1d7c610d97e78b5d3f607967a9f79fd22cfc1472","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L5 of arXiv:2608.22945, 'A Momentum-Based Variance-Reduced Algorithm for Federated Multiobjective Optimization'] Suppose that Assumptions (A1 of the paper) and (A3 of the paper) hold. If $\max\{1152e^2(1-\beta)^2 \left(\eta KL\right)^2, 1152e^2(1-\beta)^2 \left(\eta \gamma KL^2\right)^2\} \leq \beta^{2}$, then the following inequality holds:
