{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.565796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c18bf2bf0a5ce61f7faa5af12ab265cf0f905e6f411f5ca64375e3f37817dc40","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro.velocity-resolvent-L2 of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] There exists $C<\infty$ such that, for $\mathbb{Q}$-a.e.\ $\omega$ and every $(m,h,\rho)$ in the admissible regime~(equation eq.admissible of the paper), the homogenization error~$U_m$ defined by~(equation def.Um of the paper) satisfies
