{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.742091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c18df9769ae12b79292f7cb8360d61eb82d1cdfd701b4f8e8df2bce4c63e29b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Minsker of arXiv:2411.07878, 'Bernstein-type and Bennett-type inequalities for unbounded matrix martingales'] Let $\mathbf{X}_1, \dots, \mathbf{X}_n \in \mathbb{H}(d)$ be a sequence of martingale differences such that $\max_{i} \norm{\mathbf{X}_i} \le K$ almost surely for some $K > 0$. Denote $\boldsymbol{\Sigma} \coloneqq \sum^n_{i=1}  \E\left[\mathbf{X}^2_i \middle| \mathscr{F}_{i-1}\right].$ Then for any $t \ge \frac{1}{6}(K + \sqrt{K^2 + 36\sigma^2})$,
