{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.056230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1d017033372ddcab37678e70f72d7c2e8707f940cb3c0209cdf44e65dc294d1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] For every $a\in\R^\sS$ and $b\in \R^\D$, we have
\begin{gather}
    a^\Vec\cdot b = D a \cdot b^\summ, 
    \\
    (a^\Vec)^\avg=a. 
\end{gather}
For every $b\in\R^\D$, we have
\begin{align}
    \nabla_d \xi^\Vec(b) = \nabla_s\xi(b^\summ),\quad\forall d \in \sfM_s\quad\text{and thus}\qquad \nabla\xi^\Vec(b) = \Ll(\nabla\xi(b^\summ)\Rr)^\Vec.
\end{align}
For every $b,b'\in\R^\D$, we have
\begin{align}
    b'\cdot \nabla\xi^\Vec(b) = D b'^\summ\cdot \nabla \xi(b^\summ)\qquad\text{and thus}\qquad \theta^\Vec(b)= D \theta (b^\summ).
\end{align}
For every $t\in\R_+$, $p, q \in  \mcl Q_\infty^\sS$ and $\up,\uq\in \mcl Q_\infty^\D$ satisfying $p=\up^\summ$ and $q^\Vec= \uq$, we have
\begin{align}
    \psi^\Vec\Ll(\uq + t\nabla\xi^\Vec(\up)\Rr) = \D \psi\Ll(q+t\nabla\xi(p)\Rr)\quad\text{and thus}\quad \sP^\Vec_{t,\uq}(\up) = \D\sP_{t,q}(p).
\end{align}
Moreover, 
\begin{align}
    \text{if}\quad  \up= \partial_{\uq}\psi^\Vec\Ll(\uq + t\nabla\xi^\Vec(\up)\Rr),\qquad\text{then}\quad p = \partial_q \psi(q+t\nabla\xi(p)).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:49:15.475747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1d5f01e0e4206824e382e15b36f9f0b2ce85d5a56108cd73ac713375d647855","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma equiv-quotient of arXiv:2608.28504, 'Global $\bm\infty$-categories and global Thom spectra'] Let $\alpha\colon G\to G'$ be a homomorphism of compact Lie groups, and let $H$ be any other compact Lie groups. Then $\alpha_!\colon\cat{$\bm{(H\times G)}$-Top}\to \cat{$\bm{(H\times G')}$-Top}$ sends $\mathcal G_{H,G}$-weak equivalences between Hausdorff $(H\times G)$-spaces with free $\ker(\alpha)$-action to $\mathcal G_{H,G'}$-weak equivalences.
    \begin{proof}
        Consider $G'$ as a $(H\times G\times G')$-space with $G'$ acting via left multiplication, $H$ acting trivially, and with $g\in G$ acting via right multiplication by $\alpha(g)^{-1}$. Then $\alpha_!$ factors as
        \[
            \cat{$\bm{(H\times G)}$-Top}\xrightarrow{\;G'\times{-}\;}\cat{$\bm{(H\times G\times G')}$-Top}\xrightarrow{\;(-)/G\;}\cat{$\bm{(H\times G')}$-Top}.
        \]
        It is clear that the first functor preserves Hausdorffness and sends $\mathcal G_{H,G}$-weak equivalences to $\mathcal G_{H,G'\times G}$-weak equivalences. Moreover, if $X$ is $\ker(\alpha)$-free, then $G'\times X$ is $G$-free, as every point of $G'$ has $G$-isotropy $\ker(\alpha)$. It therefore suffices to show that the second functor sends $\mathcal G_{H,G\times G'}$-weak equivalences between $G$-free Hausdorff spaces to $\mathcal G_{H,G'}$-weak equivalences.

        If $X$ is any $G$-free space, $K\subset H$ is any closed subgroup, and $\varphi\colon K\to G'$ is any homomorphism, then [schwede2018global]*{Proposition~B.17} shows that the tautological map
        \begin{equation}
            \begin{aligned}
                \smash{\coprod_{\alpha\colon K\to G}X^{(\alpha,\varphi)}/C(\im\alpha)}&\longrightarrow (X/G)^\varphi\\
                [x]&\longmapsto[x]
            \end{aligned}
        \end{equation}
        is a homeomorphism, where the coproduct runs over $G$-conjugacy classes of continuous group homomorphisms $K\to G$, and $C(\im\alpha)$ denotes the centralizer of the image of $\alpha$ in $G$. Thus, if $f\colon X\to Y$ is a $\mathcal G_{H,G}$-weak equivalence of $G$-free Hausdorff spaces, then $(f/G)^\varphi$ splits as a coproduct of the maps $f^{(\alpha,\varphi)}/C(\im\alpha)$. By assumption, each $f^{(\alpha,\varphi)}$ is a non-equivariant weak equivalence. As $C(\im\alpha)\subset G$ acts freely on $X$ and $Y$, Lemma~(lemma:quotient-we of the paper) therefore shows that also the quotient $f^{(\alpha,\varphi)}/C(\im\alpha)$ is a weak homotopy equivalence.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.844209+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1d732c714881b9825ca9c257aae088640eab586836d028a8c6318e1c4529c14","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:rhoelli of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] For any binary tree $\rho\in{\mathcal T}_b$ and for $\ell\in\{1,\ldots, m_L(\rho)+1\}$, we define
