{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.307992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c1ff0e6b118bd56056e072c3fcc0a8e05b29e155e69e5c514a74e1f1f36c5993","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ran_det of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] For any $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}$, $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$, $1 \le \ell \le k - 1$, $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$, $\mathbf{T} > 0$ and $\delta > 0$, we have
