{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.359467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c271f1741f94d2d0a84b829ff64536340ad530038e30633fec64b601c34dee2b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] The process $(\widetilde{B}^{s,1}_t)_{t \in [s, 1]}$ has negatively correlated increments. Moreover, for any $S \in [s, 1]$, and any partition $D= \{t_i\}_{i=1}^n$ of $[s, S]$, the $n\times n$ matrix $(Q^D_{ij})_{i,j=1}^n$ with entries 
