{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:48:43.550800+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2971f2f4b6a8ed0058d7733bb7a54dec8396d7df9c05be7f53dcf79e8c4c63d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.07239, 'Unified framework for asymptotically uniform iterative construction of generalised random '] Consider the iterative oriented graph process on $V$, $\d$, $\d'$, and $X$. Let $x_{\max}$ be the maximum out- or in-degree in $(V,X)$, and let
		\begin{align}
			d_{\max}&:=\max\{d_1,\ldots,d_n,d_1',\ldots,d_{n}'\},
			\\\Delta&:=d_{\max}(d_{\max}+x_{\max}).
		\end{align}
		Consider the asymptotics as $m\to\infty$, and assume that $\Delta=O(m^{\sfrac12}/(\log m)^2)$. Then the probability of rejection is $O(\Delta/m)$. In particular, for $m$ large enough, there exists an oriented graph with out- and in-degree sequences $\d$ and $\d'$ and with no arcs from $X$. Furthermore, any such graph is sampled with probability $(1+O(\mathscr{E}))\mathscr{P}$, where $\mathscr{E}:=\mathscr{E}(m,\Delta)$ and $$\mathscr{P}:=\exp(\lambda_{\d,\d'}+\tfrac12\lambda_{\d,\d'}^2+\tfrac12\lambda_{\d}\lambda_{\d'}+\mu_{\d,\d'}^{X})\frac1{m!}\prod_{i=1}^{n}d_i!d_i'!,$$ which is asymptotically uniform. The total number of such graphs is thus $(1+O(\mathscr{E}))\mathscr{P}^{-1}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.601456+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2971faf89523392ec6d9eefd0c2a1a877a82bf2a6f48f9eb80ad1efc20cd114","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 49 of arXiv:2608.12947, 'Branch-stationary max-stable fields on rooted trees'] For the representer \(Z^{Q,\pi}\),
