{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.789276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2997b9e40c7bcd91def57a98171ab10d74a732c93adc51a4597ff15e44fc34c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 57 (H\"older spaces of regularity $\alpha\in(0,1)$) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For $0 < \alpha < 1$, the space $\cC^\alpha(\Lambda)$ consists in all functions 
