{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.305418+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c34f1a433eb546f464580ec78d658eccf7ac9479c655461275d6489f78292841","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lln_lp of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Suppose that $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}$ and $q_{k} > 0$ for some $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$. Then for any $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$ and $p \ge 1$, we have 
