{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.775047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c38e69769a43c35bd5738bd63e5169fb26e4e7b7607225eaf1ebab15f12b1419","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: fantastic_vertex of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] We say $v \in \mathbb{T}^d_m$ is $\mathbf{fantastic}$ if the planted particle $w_0^o$ visits at least $\phi(s)$ number of vertices in $B_v$, where
