{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.458955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4ffcde406cd8d123d20bddf838d1c65d06fb51467a043e8d4d5c552d4f330af","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma HOProb of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Suppose $h_1, h_2\in \mathbb{R}^+$ and $t_1, t_2\in \mathbb{R}$ such that $t_2\leq t_1$, for $h_1<h_2$ and $t_2\leq t_1-t^*$, for $h_1>h_2$, where $t^*$ is defined in ((eq:tstar of the paper)). Under the two-point Palm probability measure $\mathbb{P}^{(t_1, h_1), (t_2,h_2)}_{{\mathcal H }}$, the probability of the event $A^{(k)}_{2,1}$,  for $k=1,2$, is 

