For each $i\in \{1,2,3\}$, every non-empty fiber of $P_i$ is path-connected.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.706325+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5787a43b0b4cf766eae54b610856ec5eee9f2f5ac220e81047eff3f43f1fbf6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lA1Delta of arXiv:2504.07255, 'A Tail-Respecting Splitting Numerical Scheme\\ for L\'evy-Driven SDEs With Superlinear Dri'] Let $r\in[2,\infty)$. Then, for any $\gamma\in [0,1]$
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
\sup_{t\in[t_k,t_{k+1})}\mathbf{E}^{(N)}_{t_1,\dots,t_N}\Big[\|\Delta_t^n\|^r\Big|\mathcal{F}_{t_k}\Big]
\leq_C \|\Delta_{t_k}^n\|^r
&+h_n^{r\gamma +1}(1+\|X_{t_k}^{(n)}\|^{r\gamma\chi+r}) +h_n^{r\gamma }(1 + \|X^n_{t_k}\|^{r\gamma\chi+r})\\
&+h_n  (U_{t_k}^n)^r
+ h_n^{r\gamma+1} (U_{t_k}^n)^{r\gamma\chi}  + h_n
\end{aligned}\end{equation}
for $n$ large enough uniformly over
$N\in\mathbb{N}_0$, partitions $\{t_1,\dots, t_N\}$, and $k=0, \dots, N$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.110164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c5792f4d582550cf88ff853440715cd12f49f86c27676833de4c8d7841dfe661","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma heat of arXiv:2411.15881, 'Stable Approximation for Call Function Via Stein's method'] Let the random variable $Y\sim S_\alpha(1,\delta)$ and denote the density function of $Y$ by $p_{1,\delta}$. Then for any $y\in(-\infty,\infty)$, we have
