{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.309146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c681bb84d4d6fdfb898851ed9192da813d39852be70a77f086f2c0c874bc0dfb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 96 of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Let $k \in \mathbb N$ and $1\leq i\neq j \leq k$. Consider a decreasing function $F:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ of exponential decay at infinity. We define the functional $V^{ij}(F;\bullet):(I^k)^{\mathbb Z_{\ge 0}} \to I^{\mathbb Z_{\ge 0}}$ by 
