{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.077717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c765b01fb3a3428c29230e0334267995e539a6c178db7685c4c438ab8b23a31a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo formule of arXiv:2507.00737, 'Dispersion models on a circle: universal properties and asymptotic results'] For all bounded and Lebesgue measurable function $g:[0,1]\to \mathbb{R}^+$,
	\begin{equation}\langle g, M_{\lambda}({\sf e}) \rangle  = \int_{ \lambda}^{+\infty} \sum_{k\geq 0} g( {\ell_t(k)})\, {\ell_t(k)} \,   \mathrm{d} t, ~~~\textrm{ a.s.}     \end{equation}

	In particular, for $f = {\sf Id}/2$, we have: 
	\begin{eqnarray}\langle f, M_{\lambda}({\sf e}) \rangle 
	&=&\int_{0}^1 {\sf e}_\lambda(s)-\underbar{{\sf e}}_\lambda(s)\, \mathrm{d} x
	= \frac12\int_{ \lambda}^{+\infty} \sum_{k=1}^{+\infty}  {\ell_t(k)}^{2} \mathrm{d} t.       \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.776042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c76a1d10400b003205338e26a947738c973ef3b9bc069e75a8634a8cca20410e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2603.25452, 'New approach to optimal control of delayed stochastic Volterra integral equations'] \textbf{(Representation Theorem for advanced BSVIEs)}\\
	Assume that the generator $\phi: [0, T]^2\times\mathbb{R}\times\mathbb{R}\to \mathbb{R}$ such that $\phi(.,s.,.)$ is $(\mathcal{F}_s)_{s\geq 0}$-adapted. Suppose that there is the couple of process $(p(t), q(t, .))$ solution of  the backward stochastic Volterra integral equation (BSVIE) 
\begin{eqnarray*}
	p(t) = \Phi(t) + \int_t^T \phi(t, s, p(s+\delta), q(t, s))ds 
		- \int_t^T q(t, s)dB(s), \quad t \in [0, T].	
\end{eqnarray*}  
Then, for all $0\leq t<s\leq T$, we have 
\begin{eqnarray}
q(t, s) = \mathbb{E}\left[ D_s p(t) \mid \mathcal{F}_s \right].
\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.729669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c76a734d319a0d060bfefccb30eab5d495b93ea93b96af2af3e055f76840afcf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] For a probability measure $\varrho$ on $\hat{U} (N)$, a \textbf{Schur generating function} $S_{\varrho}^{U (N)}$ is a symmetric Laurent
  power series in $(u_1, \ldots, u_N)$ given by
  \[ S_{\varrho}^{U (N)} (u_1, \ldots, u_N) := \sum_{\lambda \in \hat{U}
     (N)} \varrho (\lambda) \frac{\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\chi}}^{\lambda} (u_1,
     \ldots, u_N)}{\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\chi}}^{\lambda} (1^N)} . \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:32:34.792139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7797d04535444931b0f7276c9210964209d886fbaa80c92ee109071c524905d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:usefuldecomp of arXiv:2411.08295, 'Improving the convergence of Markov chains via permutations and projections'] Let $l,m,n \in \mathbb{N}\cup \{0\}$ with $l > n \geq 0$ and $m \geq 1$. Let $P \in \mathcal{L}(\pi)$ and $Q_i \in \mathcal{I}(\pi) \cap \mathcal{L}$ for $i \in \llbracket 0,m-1 \rrbracket$ be a sequence of isometric involution transition matrices. Define $R_n$ as in (equation eq:Rndef of the paper). 
	\begin{itemize}
		\item For $E \in \mathcal{E}$, we have
		\begin{align*}
			D^\pi_{KL}(R_n \| E) 
			&= \sum_{j=n}^{l-1} D^\pi_{KL}(R_j \| R_{j+1}) + D^\pi_{KL}(R_{l} \| E).
		\end{align*}

		\item For $E \in \mathcal{E}$, we have
		\begin{align*}
			\left\lVertR_n - E\right\rVert_F^2 
			&= \sum_{j=n}^{l-1} \norm{R_j - R_{j+1}}_F^2 + \norm{R_{l} - E}_F^2.
		\end{align*}

		\item  We have
		\begin{align*}
			R_\infty(Q_0,\ldots,Q_{m-1},P) = R_\infty(Q_0,\ldots,Q_{m-1},R_l).
		\end{align*}

		\item(Projection is trace-preserving)
		\begin{align*}
			\mathrm{Tr}(R_n) = \mathrm{Tr}(P).
		\end{align*}
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.096877+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c77a2aea819d1e9549830d6249335826005f91371ea17228783397bb41c53392","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Maldiff of arXiv:2412.08497, 'Time discretization of Quadratic Forward-Backward SDEs with singular drift'] Let Assumptions of Proposition (ClassYM of the paper) be in force. Then the couple process $ (Y,Z)$ solution to (equation 2.2 of the paper) is Malliavin differentiable and the derivative process $(D_u Y_t,D_u Z_t)$ solves the affine BSDE for all $0\leq u \leq t \leq T.$
				\begin{align}
