{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.820877+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7834ecb3d16f13ecd450aa1c88cf394fad26637f1f1a799d11964cb1f3658bf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defstar def:accessibility of arXiv:2605.06488, 'Continuous-state branching processes with L\'evy-Khintchine drift-interaction: Laplace dua'] \
\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Accessibility.} The boundary $\Delta\in \{0,\infty\}$ is said to be accessible if $$\forall x\in (0,\infty), \ \mathbb{P}_x(\exists t\geq 0: X_t=\Delta)>0.$$ 
\item \textbf{Absorption.} The boundary $\Delta\in \{0,\infty\}$ is absorbing if $$\mathbb{P}_{\Delta}(\exists t\geq 0: X_t\neq \Delta)=0.$$ 
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.248334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c785463d40ee1a2549e2f7269665b8ad5f5fe6ba59fbeb383960a2f9b3fdd323","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma aprioricompact of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix {\small$\mathrm{L}>0$}. If {\small$\zeta,\zeta_{\mathrm{large}}=\mathrm{O}(1)$} are large enough, then with probability $1-\mathrm{o}(1)$, we have

