{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:06:18.040197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c79af58c3532e503efd19ada537aa03f43b4baddb3465b17537bc6c6f8f3b4b3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 (Resolvent invariance of spectral directions) of arXiv:2608.15805, 'Spectral duality structures and the Fisher--Rao geometry of reset distributions'] Assume the active eigenvalues $\{\lambda_k : P_k\xi\neq 0\}$ are
pairwise distinct. Then
