    for $i,j \in \{ \bullet, \circ\}$ with $(i,j) \neq (\circ, \circ)$. Then, there exists a constant $C=C(\gamma_\bullet, \tilde{\gamma}_\bullet, \gamma_\circ, \tilde{\gamma}_\circ, p)$, such that 
    \begin{equs}
        \| [G^i-\bar{G}^i]_{\mathcal{C}^{\gamma_i}} \|_{L_p} \leq N K_i, \qquad \| [\mathbb{G}^{ij}-\bar{\mathbb{G}}^{ij}]_{\mathcal{C}^{\gamma_i+\gamma_j}_2} \|_{L_p/2} \leq  N ( K_{ij}+K_iK_j). 
    \end{equs} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.931688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c801b9023717d422fc69a010b236488b0f84914028c0126f24987bf991360ed7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 (Persistent supercritical misalignment) of arXiv:2608.20638, 'Provable Edge-of-Stability for Adam on a One-Dimensional Quadratic'] Suppose that $0<\beta_1<1$ and $w_{\max}>2$.  For every $v_0>0$ satisfying
$w_0=c\eta/(\sqrt{v_0}+\varepsilon)>2$, there exist $x_0\ne0$ and
$m_0\in\R$ such that
\begin{equation}
    x_t(m_t+cx_t)<0
    \qquad\text{for every }t\ge0.

\end{equation}
Along this trajectory,
\begin{equation}
    w_t\ge w_0,
    \qquad
    \abs{x_t}\le(w_0-1)^{-t}\abs{x_0},
    \qquad t\ge0.

\end{equation}
In particular, $(x_t,m_t,v_t)\to(0,0,0)$ and $w_t\to w_{\max}$,
although the trajectory remains uniformly supercritical for all time. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.290621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8028e6d82f4de4a295cb5e8813c8815181ea59751216a8a971a22d5c2a1b2d0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Let $q\in\N$, and let $F:\ccC_T^d\to \R^q$
    be a continuous non-anticipative functional. Assume that there exists a constant
    $C>0$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \|F(t,x)\|
        \leq C \biggl(1+\sup_{s\in[0,t]}\|x(s)\|\biggr), \quad (t,x)\in\ccC_T^d .
    \end{equation*}
    Then there exist continuous non-anticipative functionals
    \begin{equation*}
        F^n:\ccC_T^d\to\R^q,\quad n\in\N,
    \end{equation*}
    such that the following properties hold.

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $F^n\to F$ locally uniformly on $\ccC_T^d$.

        \item For each $n\in\N$, $F^n$ is Lipschitz continuous with respect
              to the metric $d_{\ccC_T}$.

        \item There exists a constant $C'>0$, independent of $n$, such that
              \begin{equation*}
                  \|F^n(t,x)\|
                  \leq C'\biggl(1+\sup_{s\in[0,t]}\|x(s)\|\biggr),
                  \quad (t,x)\in\ccC_T^d,\ n\in\N .
              \end{equation*}
    \end{enumerate}

    In particular, for each $n\in\N$ and each fixed $t\in[0,T]$, there
    exists a constant $L_n>0$ such that
    \begin{equation*}
        \|F^n(t,x)-F^n(t,y)\|
        \leq L_n \sup_{s\in[0,t]}\|x(s)-y(s)\|,
        \quad x,y\in C([0,t],\R^d).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.745285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c80c2fae9c00177c1bbd387d386df0e369c0b64e170ba12bca573f0ddafe6574","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Laplace upper bound) of arXiv:2511.14757, 'A weak convergence approach to the large deviations of the dynamic Schr\"odinger problem'] Suppose Assumptions \ref{ass:b-sigma-local-properties}-\ref{ass:log-gradient-convergence} hold. Then, for any bounded, continuous $F$,
