{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.811474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c80f0840a7df29341feca19216bd46d1a1726dfd531b444f793101c001574a64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma prop_cons_of_energy of arXiv:2603.26307, '\LARGE The incompressible Navier--Stokes--Fourier system with thermal noise'] Let Assumption (Ass:noise of the paper) hold, $(\Omega,\mathfrak{A},\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space equipped with a filtration $\mathscr{F}$ satisfying the usual conditions and $3$-dimensional standard $\mathscr{F}$-Brownian motions $(W_n)_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^3}$ and $3\times 3$-matrix valued $\mathscr{F}$-Brownian motions $(B_n)_{n\in \mathbb{Z}^3}$ with covariance structure (equation Eq_noise_matrix_covariation of the paper) be independent. Then, any local strong solution $(U,\Psi)$ to (equation Eq_new_var of the paper), defined up to a stopping time $\tau>0$, satisfies 
	\begin{equation}
		\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}   |U_t|^2 + |\Psi_t |^2\,\mathrm{d} x \,=\, 	\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}   |U_0|^2 + |\Psi_0 |^2\,\mathrm{d} x,
	\end{equation}
	for all $t\in [0,\tau)$, $\mathbb{P}$-almost surely. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.963061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c81176b746a1b7bed1ac8c010df0e2adf0a71fa1536799b3e9a048cb2d6513e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] Let $T<\infty$. For every $t\in[0,T]$ the map $x\mapsto V_T(t,x)$ is $\llip{(0,1)}$. Specifically, for the optimal stopping time $\tau^* :=\tau^*_T(t,x)$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \partial_x V_T(t,x)=\mathbb{E}\left[g'(X^x_{\tau^*})\partial_x X^x_{\tau^*}\right],
    \end{equation}
    for almost every $x\in(0,1)$. In particular, for $x,y\in[a,b]\subset(0,1)$,
    \begin{equation}
        |V_T(t,x)-V_T(t,y)|\leq K_\text{space}|x-y|,
    \end{equation}
    where $K_\text{space}:=\|g'\|_\infty$ under Assumption \ref{asmp:bounded:g'}, and there exists an interval $[A,B]\subset(0,1)$ independent of $t$ and $T$ such that $K_\text{space}:=\|g'\|_{L^\infty([a,b]\cup[A,B])}<\infty$ if Assumption \ref{asmp:bounded:c} holds.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.570648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c81469cc40358f344576ce5e9a692ffa646ccedc7445d75b9acc6f7b3c4ca9f5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.14443, 'SEMICLASSICAL LIMIT OF POLYAKOV-LIOUVILLE MEASURE and Q-Curvature Uniformization ON EVEN-D'] The \emph{white noise truncation} $h_{\ell}$ of the augmented field $h$ is defined by the centered Gaussian field
	\begin{align}
		h_{\ell}(x) := & \int_{M\setminus B_{1/\ell}(x)}{ g}(x,y)d W(y), \quad x \in M.
	\end{align}	
	The correlation function is given by 
	\begin{align}
		k_{\ell}(x,y):=\E[h_{\ell}(x)h_{\ell}(y)]=\int_{M\setminus(B_{1/\ell}(x)\cup B_{1/\ell}(y))}{ g}(x,z) { g}(y,z)\,d\vol(z)\ge0.
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.845718+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c815f30149e0817f87bdb0673ad59d07661fc2f204a0af80091a2828fe5adc7a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2609.03847, 'A counterexample to McKean's conjecture for the Landau-Coulomb equation'] The functional $\delta_{f_R}$ for $f_R$ defined in~\eqref{def:fR}  has the expansion
	\begin{equation}
		\delta_{f_R}(v)	=\lp \delta_{R,1} +\delta_{R,2} +\delta_{R,3} +  \delta_{R,4}\rp (v/R)  
		+	\mc E_R^\delta(v) \qquad \text{for all $ v \in \Omega_R^{\rm out}$},
	\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}
		\delta_{R,1}	=\frac{2}{R|\cdot|},
		\qquad	\delta_{R,2}	=\frac{8}{R^3|\cdot|}\beta,
		\qquad	\delta_{R,3} 	=\frac{8}{R^5|\cdot|}\beta^2, \qquad \delta_{R,4} = R^{-K-3}\delta_G ,
\end{align}
and $\beta (y) \coloneq |y|^{-4} -1$.

For every $N\geq0$, there exist constants $c,C_N>0$ such that, for all sufficiently large $R$,
	\begin{equation}
		\int_{\Omega_R^{\rm out}}	g_R(v)\langle v \rangle^N
		\lp	|\mathcal E_R^\delta(v)|	+	|\mathcal E_R^\delta(v)|^2 \rp \d v
		\leq
		C_N \exp \lp -cR^{\frac45} \rp.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.120923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c821e722029b42fc452c3f4a6ec8e639dc016e5e1349581e253376e3de3e207b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LargeDevBalls of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] The following holds:
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
        \item Let $\zeta \in \{y\in \mathbb{R}^d: \Phi(y)> 0\}$ and $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ be such that $B(\zeta, \epsilon)\subset \{y\in \mathbb{R}^d: \Phi(y)\geq \epsilon\}$, then
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{E}_0\Bigg[\sum_{v\in \mathcal{N}_t}\mathds{1}_{\{X_v(t)\in tB(\zeta,\epsilon)\}}\Bigg] \to 0 \ \ \mathrm{ as } \ \ t\to +\infty.
    \end{equation}
        \item Let $\zeta \in \mathrm{int}(\{y\in \mathbb{R}^d: \Phi(y)\leq 0\})$ and $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ be such that $B(\zeta, \epsilon)\subset \{y\in \mathbb{R}^d: \Phi(y)\leq \epsilon\}$, then
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbf{E}_0\Bigg[\sum_{v\in \mathcal{N}_t}\mathds{1}_{\{X_v(t)\in tB(\zeta,\epsilon)\}}\Bigg] \to + \infty \ \ \mathrm{ as } \ \ t\to +\infty.
    \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.762794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c826e7a86d36db4d3ebf7985947e2f903e131842f092ad737916f73ed7bb468d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t1.1 of arXiv:2411.19255, 'Moderate, large and super large deviations principles for Poisson process with uniform cat'] Let the scaling $\varphi(T)$ satisfies the condition ((15.11.2024-1 of the paper)). 
