    The above inequalities also works for~$R_k(s)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.568637+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c83963ab8e873346bafdda9ecd3dce601cb8d59f178ee41d6e1daad88635de1e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.girsanov-lambda of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] There exists $C=C(d,\Lambda)<\infty$ such that, for every environment
		$\omega$, every $\lambda,\lambda'\in(0,1]$, every $t>0$, and every
		nonnegative, possibly $\omega$-dependent, path functional $F$ measurable
		with respect to $\sigma(X(s):0\le s\le t)$,
		\begin{equation}
			E_0^{\lambda',\omega}[F]\le \exp\bigl(C(\lambda'-\lambda)^2 t/2\bigr) \bigl(E_0^{\lambda,\omega}[F^2]\bigr)^{1/2}\, .
		\end{equation}
		If in addition $|\lambda-\lambda'|^2 t\le 1$, then for every
		square-integrable, possibly $\omega$-dependent, path functional $G$
		measurable with respect to $\sigma(X(s):0\le s\le t)$,
		\begin{equation}
			\bigl|E_0^{\lambda',\omega}[G]-E_0^{\lambda,\omega}[G]\bigr|\le C|\lambda-\lambda'|\sqrt t \bigl(E_0^{\lambda,\omega}[G^2]\bigr)^{1/2}\, .
		\end{equation}
		The same estimates hold with the expectations $\widehat E_0^{\lambda,\omega}$ whenever $F$ and $G$ depend only on the diffusion path. For every integer $q\ge1$, the second estimate also holds for $\mathbb{R}^q$-valued $G$, with a constant depending additionally on $q$ and with $|G|^2$ in place of $G^2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.050860+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c83c0b1c0153814fefe0f785f4d0864e6e99cd5fc2b058aa194925702b03451c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Fix $h\in Z\hat C(\Delta_T^3;B_\alpha)$ and set $h^\tau:=\Theta_\tau h$. A compatible frozen increment family over $h$ is a family $r=(r^\tau)_{\tau\in[0,T]}$
such that
\begin{enumerate}
\item for every $\tau\in[0,T]$, $r^\tau\in C(\Delta_\tau^2;B_\alpha)$;

\item the map $ \mathfrak D_T^3\to B_\alpha, \, (\tau,t,s)\mapsto r^\tau_{ts}$ is continuous;

\item for every $\tau\in[0,T]$, $\delta r^\tau = h^\tau$;

\item for all $0\le s\le t\le \tau'\le \tau\le T$, $r^\tau_{ts}=S_{\tau-\tau'}r^{\tau'}_{ts}$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.360627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c83d7dc8517aa86ee3af360dbcb3a201648afb51b6db8aa30d08f612a508d771","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:entropy:symmetry of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Suppose $\nu \in \mathcal{M}_{2, d}$ is absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure. Let $\psi_\nu^n$ be defined as in (equation eq:entropy:2reconstruction of the paper). Then $\psi_\nu^n$ is a 2-MRF on $(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{V_n}$, and can be formulated equivalently in the following ways:
\begin{equation}
       \psi_\nu^n\big(\mathbf{x}^{(n)}\big) =
\begin{dcases}
    \nu(x_{-1}, x_{0}, x_{1}) \prod_{v =1} ^{n-1} \nu(x_{v+1} | x_v, x_{v-1})\nu(x_{-v-1}|x_{-v}, x_{-v+1}) , & \\
    \nu(x_{n-2}, x_{n-1}, x_{n}) \prod_{v = -n}^{n-3} \nu(x_v|x_{v+1}, x_{v+2}),  & \\
    \nu(x_{-n}, x_{-n+1}, x_{-n+2}) \prod_{v = -n+3}^{n} \nu(x_{v}|x_{v-1}, x_{v-2}). &
\end{dcases}

\end{equation}
Moreover, we have
        \begin{equation}
