{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:44.251558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c9f44fed03ea9ccafebfe44ca2682758256cf166fb58d794da06bdfb63a888ce","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 of arXiv:2604.15226, '\bfseries Nonlinear Schrödinger equations with spatial white noise potential on full space'] Let $\mu,\alpha\in\R$ and $p,q\in[1,\infty)$. The weighted Besov space $\CB_{p,q,\mu}^\alpha$ is the set of distribution $u\in\CS'(\R^d)$ such that
