{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.595916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca8d55a3456df5523acd34daa5a3afc9d3be5bfab23be0d9c672f071fd6503ba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (A localized comparator for a conjugate prior) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] \label[lemma]{lem:coordinate-comparator}
Let $\Pi$ be a distribution with $\Pi_\kappa(\d\theta)\propto \exp(\kappa A'(0)\theta-\kappa A(\theta))\ind_{[-B,B]}\d\theta$ with  $\kappa\ge1$. Assume \eqref{eq:A-regularity}. For $|\theta^\star|<B$ and $n\in\bN$, there exists a probability measure $\rho$ on $[-B,B]$ such that
    \begin{align}
    \KL(\rho\|\Pi)
    &\le C\left\{1+\log\left(1+\frac n\kappa\right)+\kappa(\theta^\star)^2\right\},
    \\
    \int D_A(\theta,\theta^\star)\rho(\d\theta)
    &\le\frac C{\kappa+n},
