for some absolute constant $C>0$, where
$D_A(\theta,\theta'):=A(\theta)-A(\theta')-A'(\theta')(\theta-\theta')$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.526785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca904cca2253ffe9c9a434922e248c65c5ec528c1cfa83530c566bc22649fe99","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pr:expansion_init of arXiv:2506.07158, 'The diffusivity of supercritical Bernoulli percolation is infinitely differentiable'] For every $m \in \mathbb{N}_+$, the mapping $\mathfrak{p} \mapsto {\overbracket[1pt][-1pt]{\mathbf{a}}}_m(\mathfrak{p})$ is polynomial, and its $k$-th derivative ${\overbracket[1pt][-1pt]{\mathbf{a}}}^{(k)}_m$ has an explicit expression
