{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.383859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca9b128f1accd395bb9db488dca4a4d0d9c59ba97383ee1db737edd48534f73b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cov of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] For any distinct $e, e' \in \binom{[n]}{2}$, we have
\begin{equation}
	\mleft| \operatorname{Cov}[X(e), X(e')] \mright| \lesssim \frac{1}{n}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, if $e$ and $e'$ do not share a vertex, then the right-hand side
above can be improved to $\frac{1}{n^2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.879163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ca9b2880369b601ed8e159946f59464d34a86c89e08dd9083873ea0456575819","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2609.02478, 'Improved Weyl bounds on short intervals'] Let $k\ge3$ be fixed and let $\varepsilon>0$.  Suppose that
