{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.501614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbe4c415fbe28a4efffb3ff7fb3b5d0265c37df6f1387ab8377baa27f0c44591","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:diagonal-free-spike of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:diagonal-free-spike}
Consider the diagonal-free ordered model
\[
 h_{N,\mathrm{df}}^J(x)=N^{-1/2}
 \sum_{\substack{I\in[N]^p:\ i_1,\ldots,i_p\ \mathrm{distinct}}}J_Ix_I,
 \qquad x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1),
\]
with i.i.d. centered \(K\)-sub-Gaussian entries having common law
\(\mu\).  There is \(M=M(p,K)\) such that, for all sufficiently large
\(a\) and every \(\eta>0\),
\begin{align}
 &\liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \mathbb E\operatorname{Crt}_{N,\max}^{J,\mathrm{df}}
 \left([ap^{-p/2}-M,(a+\eta)p^{-p/2}+M]\right)\notag\\
 &\hspace{45mm}\ge-\overline I_\mu(a,\eta).
\end{align}
Here \(\operatorname{Crt}_{N,\max}^{J,\mathrm{df}}\) denotes the local-maximum count for \(h_{N,\mathrm{df}}^J\).  Thus the localized one-spike lower-bound mechanism does not rely on repeated tensor indices; this corollary does not compare its exponent with Gaussian diagonal-free complexity.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.197647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbec5aa2b3dda60be0f4ce6571324e3e77a46de399de9cf5cdc663c7193cbad3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 43 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Consider events ${F}_i$, ${F}'_i$ (for each $i \in \{\iota(p),\ldots,\tau(p)-2\}$), ${F}_{\tau(p)-1}$, ${F}'_{\tau(p)-1}$ and ${F}^{(\p)}$ of the form above. Suppose that there exists $\gamma>0$ such that for each $i \in [\iota(p),\tau(p)-2]$, the conditional estimate 
        \begin{equation}

            \E\big[|E^\p_{\for}(G,G')|-|E_{\for}^p(G_i,G_i')| \,\big\vert\, \mathbf a_i, \mathbf{a}'_i\big] \leq \gamma 
        \end{equation}
        holds on the event ${F}_i\cap{F}'_i$.
        Then
        \begin{equation} 
            \E[e^{t E^\p_{\for}(G,G')}\cdot 1_{{F}^{(\p)}}] \leq 1+2e^t\gamma
        \end{equation}
        for any $N$ sufficiently large, $t>0$ and $e^t\gamma<\frac{1}{10}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.873008+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbec9526cc055537c5205e1835b5a54d0a4ad33e6f8b32d0f4bba61a2b9b1495","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:quasicont-conseq of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let  $(X,d,\mu, \mathcal{E}_p, \mathcal{F}_p, \Gamma_p)$ be a regular $p$-Dirichlet space.
		If $f\in \mathcal{F}_p$ is quasicontinuous and let $A\subset X$ be Borel measurable, then the following hold: 
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item If $\cCap(A)=0$, then $\Gamma_p\langle f\rangle(A)=0$.
			\item If $g \in \Lip(\mathbb{R})$ with $g(0)=0$, then $g \circ f \in \mathcal{F}_p$ and 
			\[
			\Gamma_p\langle g\circ f\rangle  \le( \Lip_a[g] \circ f)^p \cdot \Gamma_p\langle f\rangle.
			\]
			\item If $g\in \Lip(\mathbb{R}^n)$ with $g(0)=0$, and $f=(f_1,\dots, f_n)$ with $f_i\in \mathcal{F}_p$ and $f_i$ are quasicontinuous, then
			\begin{equation} 
				\Gamma_p\langle g\circ f\rangle  \le \left(1 \vee n^{(p-2)/2}\right) (\Lip_a[g] \circ f)^p\cdot \sum_{i=1}^n \Gamma_p\langle f_i\rangle.
			\end{equation}
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.314397+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbef953e03e0a0115f561b85d65b257f2230c0e9389700ee43da9fc659d579c1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma tricky of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] Let $E,F\subseteq \mathbb R^3$ be non-empty Borel sets. Let $\mu$ be a finite measure on $F$, and $\nu(y,\cdot)$ be a finite measure on $E$ for each $y\in F$. 
    Suppose $p(x,y)$, $s(y)$ and $r(z)$ are non-negative bounded Borel functions on $E\times F,\,F,\,E$, respectively, such that the following equality holds for all $x\in E$,
    \begin{equation}
        r(x)=\int _F p(x,y)\left (\int _E r(z)\nu(y,dz)\right )\mu(dy)+\int _F p(x,y)s(y)\mu(dy).
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, suppose there exists a constant $0\le a <1$ such that for all $x\in E$,
    \begin{equation}
        \int_F p(x,y)\nu(y,E)\mu(dy)\leq a,
    \end{equation}
    then for all $x\in E$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \int p(x,y)s(y)\mu(dy)\geq \dfrac{1-a}{1+(K(p)-1)a}r(x).
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.737045+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cbf037cb20048e0c65616168485d22ea3211951630ac0645525867f035ccd5d7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:4arm_good_fl of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $p \in (0,1)$. Let~$h$ be a GFF on~$\mathbf{D}$ with boundary values so that its flow line $\eta$ is an ${\rm SLE}_{\kappa}${} from $-i$ to $i$. Let $X^0_{0,1},X^0_{0,\epsilon}$ be as defined in~(equation eq:fl_annulus of the paper). Let $I_\epsilon$ be the event that there exist two strands $\eta_{w_1;\mathrm{in}}$, $\eta_{w_3;\mathrm{in}}$ of $X^0_{0,1}$ and a strand $\eta_{w_2;\mathrm{out}}$ of $X^0_{0,\epsilon}$ so that the following hold.
