{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:14:46.372490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cccabc390a41229e1890e3c88a069c0bfd6f0090cb92f641651e72af3d9870b6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.10415, 'Continuous random variables'] We denote by $P(k)$ the set of partitions of $\{1,\ldots,k\}$, with these partitions $\pi\in P(k)$ being most conveniently being drawn as diagrams,
