{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.069013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd977f6d5c9723962724e835626351a94e92a4786c7bb0a2d73acc3b9495cbe3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:N-occ-1 of arXiv:2509.06273, 'Normalized Matching Property for Competing Urn Models'] Let $e = e_m$ be an edge of $G$, 
and suppose that $e$ is incident to $v_{d-1}$ and $v_d$. 
Then, for any  $S \subseteq X$, 
\[
\aM_{G,d}^{\occ}(S) \;=\;
\begin{cases}
	\aM_{G-e,d}^{\occ}(S) \;+\; \aM_{G/e,d-1}^{\occ}(S), 
	& \text{if $\deg_G(v_{d-1}) \geq 2$ and $\deg_G(v_d) \geq 2$}, \\[6pt]
