{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.370421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdd4f9efcb07c0b0b4e60eabab82951a593fd3c1d57f90ab91266152498c7572","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def: HeightOffset of arXiv:2411.13465, 'Height-offset variables and pinning at infinity for gradient Gibbs measures on trees'] A function $H: \Omega \rightarrow \mathbb{R} \cup \{\pm \infty\}$ is called a \underline{height-offset variable} for a gradient Gibbs measure $\nu$ iff it fulfills the following properties:
