{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.827316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce1740a4b2ad1a48e077ae6ac0f8fbcc357ee4a200e69980bd1eb27e3a4f80e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:conditional-collision-phase of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] Fix $k\geq3$.  There is a unique number
