{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.353371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce4a03e5b6b9d05e012b98f98834c2440be3f147bbab7b6e991ba3e69c531109","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 34 of arXiv:2511.07350, 'Decoupling of clusters in independent sets in a percolated hypercube'] {\cite[Theorem 3.6]{ross}}

Let $X_1, \dotsc, X_n$ be random variables with $\E[X_i^4] < \infty$,
$\E[X_i] = 0$, $\sigma^2 = \Var(\sum_{i=1}^n X_i)$, and define $\widetilde{W} = \sum_{i=1}^n X_i / \sigma$. 
Let the collection $(X_i, \dotsc, X_i)$ have dependency neighborhoods $N_i$,
$i=1,\dotsc,n$, with $D \coloneqq \max_{1 \leq i \leq n} |N_i|$.
Then
\begin{align}

    \mathrm{d_{Was}}(\tilde{W}, W) \lesssim
     \fr{D^2}{\sigma^3} \sum_{i=1}^n \E|X_i|^3
        + \fr{D^{3/2}}{\sigma^2} 
        \sqrt{\sum_{i=1}^n \E[X_i^4]},
\end{align}
where $W$ is a standard normal random variable and $\mathrm{d_{Was}}$ is the $1$-Wasserstein distance. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.055281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce4a10f3ea99459e7acb7bf8933cf12e0db44aa63d6ff1ab9104b5a6f15c37ca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:sharp-v-estimate of arXiv:2608.30904, 'Entire monotone solutions of the anisotropic Allen--Cahn equation in dimension 5'] There exist $\beta\in(0,1)$ and $C<\infty$ such that
\begin{equation}
|v_{\varepsilon,f}(x)|
+\varepsilon|Dv_{\varepsilon,f}(x)|
\le
C\varepsilon^2\rho(x)^{-2}
