{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.109632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceaa8b2066aea4fc3be35a3cf0b2a71b1b2d4620ec6a62c9520c8ee6252b22e4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition px of arXiv:2411.15881, 'Stable Approximation for Call Function Via Stein's method'] If $X$ has a distribution function of the form
\begin{equation}
F_{X}(x)=\big(1-\frac{A+B(x)}{|x|^{\alpha}}(1+\delta)\big){\bf 1}_{[0,\infty)}(x)+\frac{A+B(x)}{|x|^{\alpha}}(1-\delta){\bf 1}_{(-\infty,0)}(x)\big),
\end{equation}
where $\alpha\in(1,2)$, $A>0$, $\delta\in[-1,1]$ and  $B: \mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}$ is a bounded function vanishing at $\pm\infty$, then we say that $X$ is in the domain $\mathcal{R}_\alpha$ of normal attraction of a stable law of exponent $\alpha$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.768591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceae296adfb7995fb2748029fc9c548e5909940ca33fc501879a00712fa0fd99","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ConstructionvLinfty of arXiv:2609.01464, 'Removability of non-isolated singularities for Einstein metrics and RCD spaces'] Let $n\geqslant 2$, $(M^n,g)$ be a closed $L^\infty$-Riemannian manifold, and suppose that $S\subset M$ is closed with codimension greater than 2. Let $c$ be as in (def:Codimension of the paper) and fix $0<a<n-c-2$. Assume that $g$ is smooth on $M\setminus S$.

     Let $\Omega\Subset M$ be a smooth connected open subset, with $\overline{\Omega}\neq M$, such that $S\Subset \Omega$. Then there is a function $v:\Omega\setminus S\to (0,\infty)$ such that the following hold:
     \begin{enumerate}
         \item $v$ is harmonic on $\Omega\setminus S$ and $v\in L^1(\Omega)$;
         \item For every $\widetilde\Omega$ with $S\Subset \widetilde\Omega\Subset\Omega$ there exists $C>0$ and $\varepsilon>0$ such that:
         \begin{equation}
        v(x)\geqslant C\mathrm{d}(x,S)^{-a}, \qquad \text{for every $x\in \widetilde\Omega\setminus S$ with $\mathrm{d}(x,S)<\varepsilon$.}
         \end{equation}
     \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.245164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceb19af06d6dd2d03514dea5621f5d6e3687bd04c157d5a1360c6e37c88f64d8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 66 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix $M\in \N$ and let $T>0$. Assume that for all $i\in \lbr M\rbr$, we have some $\hfix^{\per,(i)}_0 \in \UCp$. Consider the random function $(y,t) \mapsto \hfixpa(\mathfrak{h}^{\per,(i)}_0;y,t)$, where for all $y\in \mathbb{T}$, all $t \in [0,T]$, and all initial data $\mathfrak{h}^{\per,(i)}_0$,
    \begin{equation}
         \hfixpa\big(\hfix^{\per,(i)}_0;y,t\big) :=  \sup_{x\in \mathbb{T}} \big(\hfix^{\per,(i)}_0(x) + \Lpa(x,0;y,t)\big). 
    \end{equation} Here, $\Lpa$ is a wrapped patched directed landscape from Definition~\ref{def:PatchedDLExt}. 
    We refer to  $(y,t) \mapsto \hfixpa(\mathfrak{h}^{\per}_0;y,t)$ as a \textbf{patched KPZ fixed point} of scale $n$ and with periodic initial data $\hfixp_0$.","status":"unverified"}

