{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.574971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cefb9a0ddbe5121fe99936f5a5244fdfe33c23ea231d478c57d790ba17339fe1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition propo-stab- of arXiv:2605.15742, 'Turbulent stretching of FENE dumbbell polymer model via special stochastic scaling and sin'] (Stability and uniqueness)
      Let $f_1$ and $f_2$ be two solutions to  (equation fom-limit-1 of the paper) with initial data $f_0^1\in H_0$ and $f_0^2\in H_0$ respectively. Then, we have
      \begin{align*}
          \Vert f_1(t)-f_2(t)\Vert_{H_0}^2+2\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{T}^2}\int_D\bigl(\widetilde{\mathbf{M}}_0 (\dfrac{1}{\beta}+\dfrac{k_T}{2}\vert r\vert^2)\vert \nabla_r(\dfrac{f_1-f_2}{\widetilde{\mathbf{M}}_0})\vert^2 drdxds \leq   \Vert f_0^1-f_0^2\Vert_{H_0}^2.
      \end{align*}
      In particular, the solution to (equation fom-limit-1 of the paper) is unique. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

