{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.031840+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ceffee8ab340fb2751355f374560bc06697e29975719e9a45d2a7cdb32dd86ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Global smoothing by convolutions) of arXiv:2606.07290, 'Boundary behaviour of the Volterra square-root process'] Let $T > 0$, $K \in C^{\infty}((0,T])$ and assume that there exists $\rho \in (0,1)$ such that for every integer $m\ge 0$ there exists a constant $C_m > 0$ with the property
\begin{align}
|K^{(m)}(t)| \le C_m\, t^{\rho-1-m}, \qquad t \in (0,T].
\end{align} 
Let $\eta \in [0,1)$ such that $\eta+\rho \notin \mathbb{N}$ and $m \ge 0$. Then for each function $f \in C^{m, \eta}([0,T])$ satisfying $f(0) = f'(0) = \dots = f^{(m)}(0) = 0$, the convolution $\mathcal{K}f$ has the Hölder regularity
