    \end{equation}
    ie. the number of edges with one endpoint in $X$ and the other endpoint within $X \cup \Fix \sigma$ is bounded by $\left( \frac{1}{2 \alpha -1} + \eta \right) |X|$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.761923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf7a9cbbd76c6af1a36e3473c42afc83c4c0d5a8a9f936fcf669a8c88f4f998b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2512.04544, 'On the diameter of random uniform hypergraphs in dense regime'] Let  $\epsilon_k$ be as defined in \eqref{eqn:epsilonk}. For $1 \leq k \leq d-1$, define
