{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.033035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cfe65fad8d5f04a5b186d6d808de354c02807d912f73a823fe79a6b9ab071f24","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2605.03057, 'Uniform-in-time quantitative fluctuations of large scale interacting particle systems'] Let $F\in\mathbb{D}^{2,4}$ be centered with $\E[F^2]=\sigma^2>0$ and
let $Z_\sigma\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^2)$. Then,
