{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.318251+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0067decba04501d09d782bb328a31d948e8895fc00f92673d533fa8a7d7d092","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 (Exact deletion dynamics) of arXiv:2608.30261, 'Estimating Population-Risk Curves Along Nonconvex Gradient Flows from the Training Sample'] \label[proposition]{prop:exact-deletion}
Fix $i\in[n]$, $\lambda\in\Lambda$, and $T'\in[0,T]$, and suppose both
flows exist on $[0,T']$.  Suppose $F_{P_{-i},\lambda}$ is twice continuously
differentiable on the line segments joining $\theta_t^\lambda$ to
$\theta_{-i,t}^\lambda$ for every $t\in[0,T']$.  Then, for $0\leq t\leq T'$,
\begin{equation}
 \dot\Delta_{i,t}^\lambda
 =-\overline B_{i,t}^\lambda\Delta_{i,t}^\lambda
   +\frac{c_{i,t}^\lambda}{n-1},
 \qquad \Delta_{i,0}^\lambda=0,
\end{equation}
where the secant operator $\overline B_{i,t}^\lambda:\Theta\to\Theta$ is
\begin{equation}
 \overline B_{i,t}^\lambda
 =\int_0^1
   \nabla^2F_{P_{-i},\lambda}
      (\theta_t^\lambda+u\Delta_{i,t}^\lambda)\,\dd u.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

