{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.017838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d047292eb4c1dbfd61300fa1227bc51da922cf30d38da7744dd42e6177c7bf0c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2608.26288, 'Muon with Finite Newton--Schulz: The Smoothing Benefit in Nonsmooth Nonconvex Optimization'] Suppose~\cref{ass:general-spectral-link} holds and let $(C_t)_{t\geq1}$ be a positive sequence.
For any $t\geq1$, the action~\cref{eq:general-spectral-action} is the FTRL update
\begin{equation}
  X_t^h
  =-D\nabla\widetilde\Phi_{h,C_t}(M_{t-1})
  \in\argmin_{\lVert X\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leq D}
  \left\{
    \inpr*{\sum_{s=1}^{t-1}\beta^{-s}G_s,X}
    +\frac{R_{h,C_t}(X)}{(1-\beta)\beta^{t-1}}
  \right\},

\end{equation}
where the regularizer $R_{h,C}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
  R_{h,C}(X)
  \coloneqq D\widetilde\Phi_{h,C}^*(X/D)
  =DC\sum_{i=1}^r
  \phi_h^*\left(\frac{\sigma_i(X)}{D}\right).

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.714000+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d047d19a7ad48576774e4dba7e19b92ea9b9501db98c585967f07891dfa215ba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:1103.7 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Fix $u \geq 0$ and, for each $n \geq 1$, some deterministic subset $\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n \subseteq \mathbb{Z}^2$. In addition, let us set
	\begin{equation}
		{\rm W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n}_n(u) = {\rm W}_n(u) \cap \widetilde{{\rm D}}_n
		\quad ; \qquad 
		{\mathbf W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n}_n(u) := \big\{ z \in \mathbb{X}_{n-r_n} :\: {\rm W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n} \cap {\rm Q}(z;n-r_n) \neq \emptyset\} \,.
	\end{equation}
	Then,
	\begin{equation}
		\lim_{\delta \downarrow 0} \limsup_{n \to \infty}
		\mathbb{P} \bigg( \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}|{\mathbf W}^{\widetilde{{\rm D}}_n}_n(u)| > \delta^{-1} \sqrt{|{\rm D}_n^\circ \cap \widetilde{{\rm D}}_n|/|{\rm D}_n|} \bigg) = 0 \,.
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.319687+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d04941ea4eda0c7478197b647fb02aa92679917019b3bf78e09242a2e70019c7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:one_step_improvement_intro of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] There exists $\gamma_0>0$, a spatial scale $\eta\in (0,1/4]$ and a frequency $L_0\geq 1$ such that for every $N\geq L_0$, it holds that
\begin{align}

\Big({\mathbf E}\Big\|v^N-\fint_{\eta B} v^N\Big\|_{\underline{L}^2(\eta Q)}^r \Big)^{1/r}
&
\leq \eta^{\gamma_0}\Big({\mathbf E}\Big\|v^N-\fint_{B} v^N\Big\|_{\underline{L}^2( Q)}^r \Big)^{1/r}\\ 
\nonumber
&+ \mathscr{C}_Q[\pi^N,(\widetilde{\pi}^N_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha},F,G],
\end{align}
where the last term collects the contributions of pressures and forcing at the scale $Q$ (see Subsection (ss:role_pressure_intro of the paper) for details on the former). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.068262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d04bf4c6bd63900a747bab0ae51926fd339773282cd63cb61d9e8b59a0bbe7cc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2606.00945, 'Ising model and percolation: from hexagonal lattice to 3-12 lattice'] For a general polygon $(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N})$, the pure partition functions for multiple $\SLE_{\kappa}$ are defined as 
\begin{align*}
    \LZ_{\alpha}^{(\kappa)}(\Omega;y_1,\ldots,y_{2N}):=\prod_{i=1}^{2N}|\varphi'(y_i)|^h\times \LZ_{\alpha}^{(\kappa)}(\varphi(y_1),\ldots,\varphi(y_{2N})), \qquad\text{for }\alpha\in\LP_N, 
\end{align*}
where $\varphi:\Omega\to \HH$ is a conformal mapping such that $\varphi(y_1)<\cdots<\varphi(y_{2N})$. By M\"obius covariance~\eqref{eqn::COV}, this definition is independent of the choice of $\varphi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.727134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0544753dfdf145272e6fcddbb3405883216f3d696307617231a1cf25271d7bd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Push-TASEP-WF of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The product-graph wave functions satisfy the
