{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.620198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d05a8f0eb56c3050c178b2362e224333b5539e4ef7747dc44a7248ee6cb211d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2511.00764, 'Further Developments on Stochastic Dominance for Convex\\ Combinations of Infinite-Mean Ra'] {\rm \citep{ALO24, CHSZ25}}\ \ Let $\bm X=(X_1, \ldots, X_n)$ be a vector of iid random variables with a common distribution function $F$.
