{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.023868+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d08085550fcc29f3342840b41ce791f4cc604757d00b230b91012361483f4415","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2606.06489, 'The Missing Central Limit Theorems for Local Functionals of Berry's Random Wave Model'] As $R\to\infty$, the \emph{defect} or \emph{signed volume} of Berry's model,
    \begin{equation*}
    D(R)=|\set{x\in B_R: u_1(x)>0}|-|\set{x\in B_R: u_1(x)<0}|,
    \quad R>0,    
    \end{equation*}
    satisfies $\var D(R)\sim C R^d$, $C>0$, and $\frac{D(R)}{\sqrt{\var D(R)}}$ converges in 1-Wasserstein distance to a standard Gaussian random variable as $\R\to\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.254654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d083f58f7eecb46c9ace4bb308be0103b56312d4c68c791d9405c589cc488090","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 22 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] For $\calX_n=(X_n,d^{X_n},\mu_{X_n}),\;\calX=(X,d^X,\mu_X)\in\frK(\tau)$,
the following conditions are equivalent to each other.
\begin{itemize}
  \item [$\mathrm{(i)}$]There exist a compact metric space $(M,d^M)$ and isometric embeddings $f_n:X_n\to M,\;f:X\to M$
  such that $f_n(X_n)\to f(X)$ in the Hausdorff topology, and $\mu_{X_n}\circ f_n^{-1}\to \mu_{X}\circ f^{-1}$ weakly.  
  \item [$\mathrm{(ii)}$]$d^{\tau,\BL^{\kappa}}_{\frK}(\calX_n,\calX)\to 0$
\end{itemize}
In particular, $d_{\frK}^{\tau,\BL^{\kappa}}$ induces the compact Gromov-Hausdorff-Prokhorov topology.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.635571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d084c7b49a9c6aff1556c62c41f2fbc6256a9266acf5af1dc9c5ebba0901c716","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] Let $S \subset V$ be such that $|S| \leq 3$. Suppose any vertex $v \in S \setminus \Vis$ is only adjacent to vertices which are separated from $W$ by $S$. 
	Then, there is a classical spin model $ \widetilde{\vp}$ on the reduced graph $ \widetilde{G} = ( \widetilde{V}, \widetilde{E}) := R(G,S)$ and scaling factors $r_u > 0$ for each $u \in S$ such that
	\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
		\item the reference measure on all spins in $S \setminus \Vis$ becomes the Ising measure $\l\propto \delta_{1} + \delta_{-1}$,
			and remains the same on all other spins in $ \widetilde{V}$.
		\item  the boundary correlation functions satisfy
		\begin{equation}
			\langle \vp({A}) \rangle = \Big( \prod_{u \in A}  r_u \Big) \langle \widetilde{\vp}(A) \rangle_{ \widetilde{G}}
            \end{equation}
            for all $A \subset W$. 
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.159918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d085be0e90412270761da074cc73ae4320ee103fba0fe22e191c728f644a4030","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 (Composition and differences) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Let $I\Subset\R$ be compact and $F\in C^{m+1}(I)$.
If $f$ takes values in $I$, $f\in L^\infty$, and
$\nabla f\in H^{m-1}$, then
\begin{equation}
 \norm{\nabla F(f)}_{H^{m-1}}
 \le C_{F,I,m}\left(1+\norm{\nabla f}_{H^{m-1}}^m\right).

\end{equation}
If $f_1,f_2$ take values in $I$, $f_1-f_2\in H^m$, and their relative
coefficient norms are bounded by $R$, then
\begin{equation}
 \norm{F(f_1)-F(f_2)}_{H^m}
 \le C_{F,I,m,R}\norm{f_1-f_2}_{H^m}.

\end{equation}
For a function $f\in H^m$ and a normalization $F(0)=0$, this also gives
\begin{equation}
 \norm{F(f)}_{H^m}
 \le C_{F,\norm f_\infty,m}
 (1+\norm f_{H^m}^{m-1})\norm f_{H^m}.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.457588+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d091f70a6f18a6efc9854ce8d23ec8a42f1af5e474b73fb622b9a9a358655df5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:2G_edge of arXiv:2411.16572, 'Optimal decay of eigenvector overlap for non-Hermitian random matrices'] Fix small constants $\epsilon, \tau>0$ with $0<\tau<\epsilon/10$. Then, for any deterministic matrices $\|A_i\| \lesssim 1$, the following local law  
\begin{equation}
	\Big|\langle \big(\mathrm{Im}\, G^{z_1}(\mathrm{i} \eta_1) A_1 \mathrm{Im}\, G^{z_2}(\mathrm{i} \eta_2)-\widehat M_{12}^{A_1}\big)A_2\rangle\Big|\prec
	\frac{1}{\sqrt{n\ell}}\frac{\rho_{1}\rho_{2}}{\widehat{\gamma}},
\end{equation}
holds uniformly for any $z_i \in {\mathbb C}$ and $\eta_i \in {\mathbb R }~(i=1,2)$ such that $|z_i|\le 1+n^{-1/2+\tau}$ and $\ell =\min_{i=1,2}\rho_i|\eta_i| \geq n^{-1+\epsilon}$,
with $\widehat \gamma$ given by ((parameter2 of the paper)), and the deterministic matrix $\widehat{M}_{12}^A=\widehat{M}_{12}^A(\mathrm{i}\eta_1,z_1,\mathrm{i} \eta_2,z_2)$ defined in ((Im_M_def of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.664061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d095fad30a95590205ee89f7be31400afbb08c974e75df78adca142ba9ec9092","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem monotonie of arXiv:2506.01746, '\bf Optimal Bregman quantization: existence and uniqueness of optimal quantizers revisited'] $(a)$ For every $\xi\!\in U$, $v\!\in S(0,1)$, the mapping $(t^-_{\xi,v}, t^+_{\xi,v}) \owns t \mapsto \phi_{_F}(\xi, \xi+t v)$ is decreasing on $(t^-_{\xi,v},0]$ and increasing on $[0,t^+_{\xi,v})$.

\noindent $(b)$  For every $\bar x \!\in \widehat \partial\, U$, $\xi\!\in U$, $\phi_{_F}(\xi, \bar x):= \displaystyle \liminf_{x\to\bar x, \,x\in U} \phi_{_F}(\xi,x) >0$. 

In particular, when $U$ is unbounded (so that $\infty\!\in \hat \partial U$)
\begin{equation}
\forall\, \xi\!\in U,\quad \liminf_{|x|\to \infty, \,x\in U}\phi_{_F}(\xi,x)>0.
\end{equation}

\noindent $(c) $ When $d=1$,  Claim $(b)$ is also true for the boundary $\bar \partial\, U$ of $U$ in $\bar \mathbb{R}= [-\infty, +\infty]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.156126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d09a533ca47e561a8eada1b92b37dc419b84e642e1c1debc288fb4eb3e0ca59e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.22534, 'Entropy power inequalities in compact groups'] Let $G$ be a connected compact abelian group, let $\mu$ be its 
Haar probability measure and $Y$ be a random variable on $G$ with 
density $f_Y$. Let $S$ be a set of positive Haar measure 
and $g_S = \frac{1}{\mu(S)}\mathbb{I}_S$ be the density of a uniform 
random variable $U_S$ on $S$. For $t>0$, also define
    \begin{equation*} 
    g^t(y) = \frac{t+f_Y(y)}{1+t}, \quad y \in G.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, for all $t > 0 $
\begin{equation*} 
    \chi^2(f_Y \ast g_S \| g^t  \ast g_S) \leq \eta_S\frac{t+\|f_Y\|_{\infty}}{t}\chi^2(f_Y\|g^t),
\end{equation*}
where
$$\eta_S = \left(\frac{\sin(\pi \mu(S))}{\pi \mu(S)}\right)^2.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:36.727293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d09f309ce0f7abfd4b5684ebb2f108239932a884e5b569d49ac01a20ad45dac6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2511.14379, 'Stability of storage processes with general release rates'] Assume $\textbf{(C1)-(C3)}$ (or $\textbf{(\={C}1)-(\={C}2)}$ and  $\textbf{(C3)}$ in the case when $\bar\upnu(0)<\infty$).  Let  $p\ge1$ and $\beta:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ 
	be such that
	\begin{itemize}
		\item [(i)] $\displaystyle \int_{[0,\infty)}u\vee u^p\upnu(\D y)<\infty$;
		\item[(ii)] $\beta(t)$ is convex and $\beta(t)=0$ if, and only if, $t=0$;
		\item[(iii)] there exists $\Gamma>0$  such that
		\begin{equation} r(u)-r(v)\le
		-\Gamma\beta(v-u), \qquad 0\le u\le v.\end{equation}
	\end{itemize}  
	Then, the process $\process{X}$ admits a unique invariant  $\uppi\in\mathcal{P}_p$, and for any $\kappa>0$ and $\upmu\in\mathcal{P}_p$ it holds that: 
\begin{equation}\W_p\left(\int_{[0,\infty)}p(t,x,\D y)\upmu(\D x),\uppi(\D y)\right)\le \left(\frac{\W_p(\upmu,\uppi)}{\kappa}+1\right)B_\kappa^{-1}(\Gamma t),\qquad t\geq 0,\end{equation} 
 where $$B_\kappa(t):=\int_t^\kappa\frac{\D s}{\beta(s)},\qquad t\in(0,\kappa].$$ Furthermore, $$\limsup_{u\to\infty}u^p\bar\uppi(u)<\infty.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

