{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.285305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0b1cb882d887644f6aa624f2a7c2643e2a7c805b12e07e04fc9345c3406254d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem annealed of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Let $f\in\mathbb{R}$, $u\in(0,1)$, $q\in(0,1)$, and
		$\zeta\in\mathrm{Prefix}_2(u,q)$.
		Assume:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[\emph{(i)}]
			\emph{(Tail optimality.)}
			$\zeta$ minimizes $\mathcal{P}\mathrm{arisi}$ over $\mathrm{Prefix}_2(u,q)$.
			\item[\emph{(ii)}]
			\emph{(Stationarity.)}
			$(u,q)$ is a critical point of
			$(u',q')\mapsto u'\!\left(\inf_{\zeta'\in\mathrm{Prefix}_2(u',q')}\mathcal{P}\mathrm{arisi}(\zeta')-f\right)$.
		\end{enumerate}
		Let $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ and let $\mathcal{N}_\varepsilon(f,\zeta)$ be the number of
		critical points of $F_{\mathrm{TAP},\zeta}$ with
		$\frac{1}{N}F_{\mathrm{TAP},\zeta}(\mathbf{m})\in(f-\varepsilon,f+\varepsilon)$.
		Then
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{\varepsilon\to 0}\lim_{N\to\infty}
			\frac{1}{N}\log\mathbb{E}\bigl[\mathcal{N}_\varepsilon(f,\zeta)\bigr]
			\;\geq\;
			\zeta(\{0\})\,\bigl(\mathcal{P}\mathrm{arisi}(\zeta)-f\bigr).
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.748792+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0b2937b6641fa8e0e19ef4cf849a2f17d0d5e5547e8f750053ba5fbb103c255","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 (Crossing count) of arXiv:2607.28865, 'First-Passage Percolation on Spread-out line graphs: Microscopic Regime'] Let
