{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:45:10.077013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0bf91ee34b8f94ab8471b377525e55d007d704a07cee810178f0ff9a81705ee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem_Omega_Tilde of arXiv:2504.15999, 'Infinitely many collisions between a recurrent simple random walk and arbitrary many trans'] There exists a set of environments $\widetilde\Omega$,
