{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.875963+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0dfef465c35254a4c645a050162f896b5b607625075c86c3ba22e3f90e88810","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem closed-monodromy-approximants of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Let $\gamma\in\pi_1(S)$ be an essential curve, and assume that the axis of $\gamma$ in $\widetilde S$ is not a leaf of $\widetilde\lambda$. Let $A,A_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_n(\mathbb{C})$ be the normalized (determinant-one) lifts of the monodromies $\rho(\gamma), \rho_0(\gamma)$ respectively. 
