{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.311497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d101460e00008231457edb8bcc7c923d0dc1d74c154f4be3d5fbec502b1d126e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm-SLLN-det of arXiv:2411.14876, 'Limit theorems for stochastic exponentials of matrix-valued L\'evy processes \\'] Let $L=(L_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a Lévy process in $\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}$ fulfilling (equation eq-nonsingular of the paper) and let $D=(D_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the determinant process of its stochastic exponential defined in (equation eq-detprocess of the paper). 
