{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.210410+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d19d76f091f7a3272a2748630f3b67d0ecd992c6c5cd6423d75792b4dc49c801","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2608.29013, 'Weighted Homology and Cohomology of Weighted Polyhedra'] Let $G$ be a discrete group acting on a space $Y$. Assume that $Y$ admits an equivariant triangulation and that the isotropy group at each point is finite. Let $X=Y/G$, and define a weight function $\lambda$ on $X$ to be the order of the local group at each point. Then we have
