{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.297216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d25585aef7231f4fdc274ed4bd0a7bba088c161ac6d96cf22a66912657b1292b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:uniform_approximation_fat_shattering of arXiv:2609.03129, 'A Closed-Form Formula for Consistent Lipschitz Regression on Metric Spaces with Sparse Neu'] Let $(X,\rho,\mathfrak{m})$ be a compact $d$-Ahlfors regular metric measure space, for some $d>0$, let $B,L>0$, and fix $\mathcal{F}\subseteq C(X,\mathbb{R})$. There exist constants $\varepsilon_0,c>0$ such that, if there is a fixed tolerance $0<\varepsilon<\min\{B/2,L\varepsilon_0\}$ such that, for every $f\in\operatorname{Lip}((X,\rho),[-B,B];L)$, there is some $\hat{f}\in\mathcal{F}$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

    \|f-\hat{f}\|_\infty
\le
    \varepsilon,
\end{equation}
then, for every $\varepsilon\le\gamma<\min\{B/2,L\varepsilon_0\}$,
\begin{equation}

    \operatorname{fat}_{\gamma}(\mathcal{F})
\ge
