    \left(
        \frac{L}{\gamma}
    \right)^d.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.044153+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d257b80e3ded9c43b0472c3b9097c597d1eb12a955ff7ca70c0ba78e3031d4f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 81 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Suppose   that $(\sfd_{0},q,p)$ are properly tight.
Then

