In addition, the restriction $L_{\lambda_*} : X^\perp \to Y^\perp$ is bijective with range $R(L_{\lambda_*}) = Y^\perp$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.490636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3848f9a63b589cedf57ce3388b18079e26d49f7096b3e347b64c02483dc524d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 (Definition and triangularity of $\Gamma$) of arXiv:2605.28677, 'Weak universality for stochastic reaction-diffusion models\\ with long-range correlated no'] Let $ (\pi^{(\n)} )_{\n\in\NN^{1+d}} \subset \RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!]$ such that for all $\beta$ and $\n$ it holds that $\pi^{(\n)}_{ \beta} \neq 0$ implies $ |\n| < | \beta| $.
Then 
\begin{enumerate}
\item the map $ \Gamma :  \RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!] \to  \RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!]$ defined by 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\Gamma z_{k}\coloneqq z_{k}\,, \quad 
\Gamma z_{\n}\coloneqq z_{\n}+ \pi^{(\n)}\,, \quad 
\Gamma 1\coloneqq 1\,, \quad \text{and}\quad 
\Gamma ( \pi_{1} \pi_{2}) = (\Gamma \pi_{1}) ( \Gamma \pi_{2})
\end{aligned}
\end{equation} 
for $\pi_1,\pi_2\in\RR[\![z_k,z_\n]\!]$
is well-defined on $\RR [\![ z_{k}, z_{\n} ]\!]$, 

\item for all $\beta,\gamma$ it holds that $ (\Gamma - \mathrm{id})_{ \beta}^{ \gamma}
\neq 0$ implies $ | \gamma| <
| \beta| $ and $\langle\gamma\rangle<\langle\beta\rangle$, and

\item if $ (\pi^{(\n)} )_{\n\in\NN^{1+d}} $ is such that $ \pi^{(\n)}_{ \beta'} = 0$ for all non populated $\beta'$, then for all $\beta,\gamma$
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
(\Gamma - \mathrm{id})_{ \beta}^{ \gamma} \neq 0 \quad \implies \quad \gamma
\prec \beta\,.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.169196+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d3855a06ae1b77810c9c2efa5a67e3e8cc9157d76d24ecb20a2871f85a1349ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L_strTWB of arXiv:2510.26724, 'Sharp Fuss-Catalan thresholds in graph bootstrap percolation'] Let $T$ be a TWG and $S\subsetneq T$ a partial TWG. Then, 
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\mathcal E(S)\geqslant 0$, with equality 
if and only $S$ is obtained from $T$ 
by removing one of its branches; 
\item $\mathcal D(S,T)\leqslant c\mathcal E(S)+2$; and 
\item $\mathcal T(S)\leqslant c\mathcal E(S)$, 
\end{enumerate}
for some constant $c$ depending only on $r$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.289436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d38622044e154766066eff60f278c8e930d813599847f02334daee9fd65e518d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lm3 of arXiv:2411.01849, 'A tamed-adaptive Milstein scheme for stochastic differential equations with low regularity'] For any $p\in[2, \frac{p_0}{l + \alpha+1}]$, there exists a positive constant $C$ such that, for any $t \geq 0,$ 
\begin{align*}
 \mathbb{E}[ \vert X_t - X_{\underline{t}}\vert^p|\mathcal{F}_{\underline{t}}]\vert \leq  
 C(t- \underline{t})^{p/2}
