{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.955602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d416f6b93c0f1fe83127f18db459231979dcbe2cbd106923bd3a313347ac8612","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition EstimImpo of arXiv:2602.08591, 'The Yang--Mills measure on compact surfaces as a \\ universal scaling limit of lattice gau'] We have, for all integers $k \leqslant n \leqslant m \leqslant l$,
    \begin{align*}
        &\mathbb{E}\Big[
