{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.141871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d42b6f3820f768d2619caa1932248c28e9e224c452c49b41c910a4b8ec8f3408","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (Cauchy-area theorem for Bernoulli width) of arXiv:2608.11031, 'A Bayesian Proof of the Bernoulli Theorem'] For any $x \in T$, the function $\Phi_x: [0,\infty) \rightarrow [0,+\infty)$ is nondecreasing and concave on $[0,\infty)$ with $\Phi_x(0)=0$. Moreover, it satisfies
