{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.861245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d51ed03511d22fecdc70c0244ad824faecd96c7cd4061f3a9ea70424f3dd9892","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $l \in \{1,2,3\}$ and $f$ be $l$-times weakly differentiable with all derivatives which are functions of polynomial growth. Let $u(t,x)=\E\bigl[ f\bigl(Y_T\bigr)\big|Y_t=x\bigr]$ and let $0\le 2i+j\le 4$. Then there is a constant $\tilde C$ and some $N \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for all $(t,x)\in[0,T)\times\R$,
