{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.994164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5a13342542738cf2f91625df5302b47ae6d5f0d8b75ba69675f5777ff074ccd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem rho bound of arXiv:2412.01086, 'Spectral radii of sparse non-Hermitian random matrices'] {k09}}] 
For an $n\times n$ matrix $A$ with $n>2$ and for $k\geq 1$,
\begin{align*}
C_n^{-\sigma_n(k)/k}\left( \frac{\| A\|^n}{\| A^n\|}\right)^{-\nu_n(k)/k}\| A^k\|^{1/k}\leq \rho (A)\leq \| A^k\|^{1/k},
\end{align*}
where
\begin{align*}
C_n =n^{3n/2}, \quad \sigma_n(k) = \frac{(n-1)^3}{(n-2)^2}k^{\frac{\log (n-1)}{\log n}}, \quad \nu_n(k) =\frac{(n-1)^2}{n-2}k^{\frac{\log (n-1)}{\log n}}.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.832128+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d5a40937db4db779cf13ec9a32f448a425aeb4045b82ee32014b23b64ceda00c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:tailbound_interval of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There exist constants $C, c > 0$ such that for all $S \geqslant 1$ and $y > 0$,
