{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.068193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6c00057982a17ab19275a79327a54472dfea669a5a3514fd7dda1eb038bddc6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor_uniform_random_cond of arXiv:2606.28575, 'Global smooth solutions by high mode Lie-Transport noise for Logarithmically Hyperdissipat'] Let $\nu>0$, $R> 0$, $M\ge 1$ and $\{\theta_k^n\}_{m\in I}$ time independent satisfying (hyp_noise of the paper). Assume $p \in (4, \infty)$, $-1/2 < r<- 2/p$. Let $\omega^{n,\omega_0}$ be the solution of (equation main_ito_cutoff of the paper) associated to $\{\theta_k^n\}_{k\in I}$ defined as in (hyp_noise of the paper) and some $\mathcal{F}_0$ measurable initial datum $\omega_0\in \mathcal{B}_p(M)\ \mathbb{P}-a.s.$ Let $\omega^{R,{\operatorname{det}},\omega_0}$ be the solution of (equation main_det_cutoff of the paper)
with the same \emph{random} initial datum $\omega_0$. Then for all $r_0 < -2/p$ and $\varepsilon >0$ we have 
