{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.628046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6e18f2eb0ec6c3055505fd3f2fba2999eb7d6efa8d647d34ec5465a2046bdc2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (\cite{ciech2021},Theorem 2.6) of arXiv:2605.13512, '2605.13512'] Recall \eqref{microLPT}. Let $c(x,y)$ be a macroscopic speed function which satisfies Assumptions \ref{ass:c} and \ref{ass:c2}, and let ${\bf v} =(x,y) \in \R^2_+$. Define ${\bf v}_n = (\ce{nx}, \ce{ny})$. Then we have the scaling limit
