{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.557862+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d79640a01d34d8f1bb3f8a17fb94f28534ad061c31809bcbc982f7b34b817549","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.30091, 'Computing lower expectations with respect to total variation distance and chi-squared dive'] Let $r$ be defined as above. Then
