{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.953054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d79911ee4adbcff49784688022dca3c8242fc82f6512bda1e30735db1ac085e8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.07365, 'A pathwise Ito formula \\for weakly differentiable functions'] Let $(\Omega, B, \mathbb{P}_x)$ be the canonical Wiener space defined as in Section \ref{sec:Bessel}
  and $\pi=(\pi_n)_{n\geq1}$ be a sequence of partitions of $[0,T]$ satisfying Assumptions \eqref{ass:partitioncond}, \eqref{ass:partitioncond2}.  Let $(h_m)_{m\geq1}\subset L^1(\mathbb{R}^d)$ be a sequence of nonnegative finite-valued Borel functions  such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\|h_m\|_{L^1(\mathbb{R}^d)}\to 0$ as $m\to\infty$;
\item for every compact set $K\subset\mathbb{R}^d$,
$$
\int_K\int_K \frac{|h_m(x)-h_m(y)|}{|x-y|^d}\,dx\,dy<\infty.
$$
\end{enumerate}
Then there exists a polar set $E\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ and a subsequence $(h_{m_k})_{k\geq1}$ such that, for every $x_0\notin E$,
$$
\lim_{k\to\infty}\ \limsup_{n\to\infty}\|h_{m_k}\|_{n,1,B}=0,
\qquad \mathbb{P}_{x_0}\text{-a.s.},
$$
where
$$
\|h\|_{n,1,B}
:=
\int_0^T
\sum_{i=0}^{m(n)-1}
\bigl(|h(B(t_i^n))|+|h(B(t_{i+1}^n)|)\bigr)(t_{i+1}^n-t_{i}^n)
$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.262632+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d79d024fd6e2120b4e9497f6cac3aeed1a1372c51d65b2035ac4480b5ccc30e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma kzetaestimate-long of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Retain the setting of Lemma (lemma:kzetaestimate-short of the paper), but forget the constraint that {\small$|\t-\s|\leq N^{\beta}N^{-\zeta}$}. On the same high probability event as in Lemma (lemma:kzetaestimate-short of the paper), we have 

