{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.157730+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7bc9d0301143f6ee080bf6554be933f446d8f762535b4a5269157d4985126ee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 (Arbitrary-order quasineutral expansion) of arXiv:2609.01589, 'Uniform stability of expanding simple waves for Euler--Poisson--Boltzmann: a singular comp'] Under the hypotheses of \cref{thm:main}, assume
\[
  \cE_{s,\eps}(t_0)\le C_0\eps^{4M+4}.
\]
Then
\begin{align}
  &\sup_{t_0\le t\le T}
  \left(
  \norm{n-n^a}_{H^s}+\norm{u-u^a}_{H^s}
  +\norm{\phi-\phi^a}_{H^s}
  +\eps\norm{\nabla(\phi-\phi^a)}_{H^s}
  \right)
  \le C\eps^{2M+2}. 
\end{align}
In particular, for every $M\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t_0\le t\le T}
  \left(
    \norm{n-\Nr}_{H^s}+\norm{u-(\Vr,0)}_{H^s}
    +\norm{\phi-\log\Nr}_{H^s}
  \right)\le C\eps^2. 
\end{equation}
Here each norm is taken after subtracting the corresponding composite or
simple-wave profile, so it is finite despite the distinct end states. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.432243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7bd607a1875c6acdcc554761d06e0f684d8ffd380ed8b20786d2bf0c2b8b246","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 (H\"older bump packing) of arXiv:2608.31157, 'Sharp Approximation Rates for Neural Networks with Affine Latent Parameterizations'] Let $d\in\N^+$ and $0<\alpha\le1$, and let
$\calF\subseteq C(\R^d)$ be a real-valued function class.  Let
$V\in[1,\infty)$ satisfy
\[
