{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.417871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d813c9931d9c07036c5e65ad2858b11cd13827b37376c1ce843df328db1a5a0f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2608.20252, '2608.20252'] A family $Q^N$ of probability measures on $\mathcal{D}([0,T], \Omega)$ is tight exactly when
