{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.717705+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d8821a11e1ffa6ccbf266295a8c0a454ea8cf980a0044f4a1cae67a1f0ec87f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm.IIC of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] Let $\mathcal C_\infty$ be the IIC of Bernoulli percolation on $\mathbb Z^d$, either with $d>6$ and sufficiently spread-out lattice,  or $d>10$ in the nearest neighbor model. There exist positive constants $C$ and $\kappa$, such that for any $\varphi : \mathbb Z^d \to [0,\infty)$,  satisfying  $\|g_{d-4} * \varphi\|_\infty \le 1$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\left[\exp\left(\kappa \cdot \sum_{x\in \mathcal C_\infty} \varphi(x)\right)\right] \le 1+C \, \|\varphi\|_1.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $d\ge 9$ and $\widetilde {\mathcal C}_\infty$ denotes an independent copy of $\mathcal C_\infty$, then
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb E\left[\exp\left(\kappa \cdot|\mathcal C_\infty \cap \widetilde {\mathcal C}_\infty|^{1-\frac 4d}\right)\right] <\infty.  
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.893964+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d88397385310045a51c0e120bb4d90eb70ebc82fb206693f4b9d3fade8e1b7b4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:lambsigm_intro of arXiv:2607.09946, 'Statistics on Yau's conjecture: Variance asymptotics'] For $M$ and $I$ as in (def:RRW of the paper), we define
\begin{gather}
\sigma(\phi_I^M)^2:=\fint_M{\mathbb{V}\mathrm{ar}}\left\{ \phi_I^M(x)\right\} dx,
\quad
\lambda(\phi_I^M)^2:=\frac{1}{\sigma(\phi_I^M)^2}\fint_M\mathbb{E}\left\{ \|d_x\phi_I\|^2 \right\} dx.
\end{gather}
and call them \emph{average variance} and \emph{average frequency} (consistently with the terminology introduced in [cgv2025StecconiTodino]). If $\sigma(\phi^M_I)=0$, we set $\lambda(\phi^M_I)=0$. We extend such notation to any setting in which the integrands in (eq:sigmalambdaRW of the paper) are constant, including non-compact manifolds $M$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.629711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d883be45e3bcd91b5dec9b07da0cbb5bad24f1a802224a1b0dd2963249a311ca","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.01362, '{Double cluster swapping for spin models: \\Pfaffian relations and sharpness}'] A spin model $\left< \cdot \right>_{G}$ satisfies Pfaffian relations 
