			\end{equation*}
		\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.331261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da8abccb608bc878ac6d7e086d463bd65dd9439fc14285c3c96858906d9ee997","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 16 of arXiv:2506.22020, 'Norm-dependent Lamperti-type MAP representations of stable processes and Brownian motions '] Let $(\rho,\Theta)$ be the underlying MAP of $\mathcal{R}$ with respect to the norm $\|\cdot\|_{\text{L}^1}$ in dimension $d=2$. For every $f\in C^2_b(\mathbb{R}\times\mathcal{S}^+)$ satisfying the boundary conditions
	\begin{enumerate}[i]
