{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.633647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_da92c9286469ebc23b3a14e731f281dbece129b79ca0e694b73ba0ceb8bd0662","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:absolute of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Assume that $\mathbf E|X|^{r+3}$ is finite for some integer $r \ge 1$.
