{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.992775+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db442094cbc2d36257fa0f37d09e159ac4b8c2fac295228c077d89830d36f02e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem OptimalPWConcentration of arXiv:2609.02541, 'A note on the norm of the embedding of $\text{PW}^2$ into $\text{PW}^q$'] Let $S \subset \mathbb{R}$ be a measurable set with $0 < |S| < \infty$ and $g$ be any function of $PW^2$ with $\|g\|_{2}=1$. Then
