{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.503520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_db4700e39acdc4e8ad0b2a1e98dbdd63c80f559c2438775d59656aedaa7aa91d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Finite-entropy criterion for the entropic CCLT) of arXiv:2608.30579, '2608.30579'] Let $(\xi,\eta )$ be a pair of random variables. 
    Let $\{(\xi_i,\eta_i)\}_{i\geq 1}$ be independent copies of $(\xi,\eta)$.
	  Define
	  \begin{equation}
					W_n = \frac{\xi_1 + \xi_2 + \cdots + \xi_n}{\sqrt{n}}, 
			\quad \boldsymbol{\eta}_{n}= (\eta_1, \ldots, \eta_n).	
	  \end{equation}
			Assume that
\begin{equation}
			\sigma^{2} \triangleq\mathbb{E}\,\operatorname{Var}(\xi  \vert \eta) < \infty, 
