{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:38.358811+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc051d1176167e3ae2ae9b04ed3b149f4e953c70118ee20a42882c6bf1874970","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Convergence of the energy and of the corrector) of arXiv:2604.21143, 'Quantitative homogenization for the critical long-range random conductance model'] Under Assumption~\textup{(U)}, there exists a constant $C = C(d, U, \lambda) < \infty$ such that, for every $\eps \in (0,1)$ and every $p \in \Rd$,
