{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.899380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc084e53be98361d1304acdcce105f8e3bfc819b843bb9eb9e2e13fecb04d05c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 23 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta} and \ref{Assumptions_basic} hold.
 Then the equilibrium measure $\mu$ has a compact
 support, \textit{i.e.} its support is inside $[-D,D]$ with $D>0$ depending only on the constants in the assumptions. Moreover, there exists an $H$-tuple of constants $\boldsymbol{v}$ such that for any $h \in [H]$ and $x \in [\hat{a}'_h,\hat{b}_h']$, we have
\begin{align}
V^{{\textnormal{eff}}}_h(x) \geq v_h& \quad \textnormal{if}\,\,x\,\,\textnormal{is in a void}, \\
 V^{{\textnormal{eff}}}_h(x) \leq v_h & \quad \textnormal{if}\,\,x\,\,\textnormal{is in a saturation},\\
 V^{{\textnormal{eff}}}_h(x) = v_h& \quad \textnormal{if}\,\,x\,\,\textnormal{is in a band}. 
\end{align}
If each interval $[\hat a'_h, \hat b'_h]$ has at
least one band, then $\boldsymbol{v}$ belongs to the $\amsmathbb{R}$-span of the $H$-dimensional vectors of coefficients of the linear forms $(\mathfrak{r}_{e})_{e = 1}^\mathfrak{e}$ in \eqref{eq_equations_eqs}, and the above conditions uniquely determine the equilibrium measure, \textit{i.e.} no other measure in $\mathscr{P}_\star$ satisfies them. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.919452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc161d0f053c39817e1267ed3948a1310714d2e4b68a6d7e623ea743a2cfbfb3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem TeLe2 of arXiv:2411.06974, '{\bf Distribution dependent SDEs with multiplicative fractional noise}'] Assume that $f\in C^\beta([0,T];\mathbb R^d)$ with $\beta\in (0,1]$,
