{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.859292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc1703dc7cc995841e21df001b7d3bcd6b456e11337f3c559177a1fa048e1f9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2608.21090, 'Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process conditioned to have restricted $L_2$-norm'] Let $0<\theta<\frac{1}{2\gamma}$. Then, for any $\delta\in(0,1)$, $\beta\in(0,\frac12)$ and $K>0$, there exists a $T_{\delta,\beta,K}>0$, such that for all $T\geq T_{\delta,\beta,K}$ and any $x\in\R$, $y>0$ with
    \[\abs x\abs\leq T^{\beta/2}\quad\text{and}\quad \left|y-\theta T\right|\leq K\,T^\beta\]
    it holds
    \begin{equation*}
        (1-\delta)\,C_\theta\,A(T)\leq\P_x(Z_T\leq y)\leq (1+\delta)\,C_\theta\,A(T),
    \end{equation*}
    with
    \[C_{\theta}:=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi}}\frac{4\sqrt{\theta}}{\left(1+2\gamma\theta\right)^{3/2}\left(1-2\gamma\theta\right)},\]
    and
    \[A(T):=T^{-1/2}\,\exp\left(-\frac{1}{8\frac{y}{T}}\left(1-2\gamma \frac{y}{T}\right)^2T-\frac{x^2}{4\theta}\left(1-2\gamma\theta\right)\right).\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.788838+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc18c7c2feef395a3d2e607e980dcd929a0337d5f739001cd4a6f48674547846","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] We have
