{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.568083+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc1a0bc13bcd0794070cbc213a0f639f267ac1fb4713b7f9432501c5f7d8c181","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 40 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $(X, d, \mu)$ be a Polish probability space. Suppose that either of the following equivalent conditions holds (by Lemma~\ref{l:isop_to_enl} and Proposition~\ref{p:symmetric_isop_enlargement}):
\begin{enumerate}
    \item it has a continuous isoperimetric function $I$ such that \eqref{eq:sym_iso} holds and that $v\mapsto \frac{I(v)}{v}$ is non-increasing;
    \item it has $R_s^I(v) = \Psi\left(\Psi^{-1}(v) +  s\right)$ as an enlargement function, where the distribution function $\Psi$ defined in \eqref{eq:Psi_def} is log-concave and is such that \eqref{eq:Psi_reflexive} holds.
\end{enumerate}
Then, we have 
\begin{equation}

    \Theta^I(s)=\Psi\left(-\frac{s}{2}\right),
\end{equation}
where $\Theta^I$ is defined in \eqref{eq:theta_I_def}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:38:13.627677+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc1a36033028155548eb0b8bb20b4c6cb4a70088353617e5abb5ec0775e022b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 7 (\cite{bahouri2011fourier},\,Proposition 7.7) of arXiv:2609.00598, 'Supercritical mean--field limit for magnetized Hamiltonian dynamics'] Let $s\in(0,1)$ and $\omega\in L^1(\mathbb T^2)\cap C^{0,s}(\mathbb T^2).$ 
Then there is some $C>0$ such that 
\begin{align*}
\big\Vert D_{x}\nabla_{x}^{\perp} V\ast \omega \big\Vert_{\infty}
\leq 
C\big(\Vert \omega\Vert_{1} 
+\Vert \omega\Vert_{\infty}(1+|\log\Vert \omega\Vert_{\infty}|\big)\log(e+\left\Vert \omega\right\Vert_{\infty}+\left\Vert \omega \right\Vert_{C^{0,s}})\big).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.029105+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc1f9f40fc81090618d8c36dc9f4dacd49bb7c8985b03cc14600ff2a56b9237f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 14 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let $x\in\R^n$, $r>0$ and $\phi\in\text{\rm SCL}\,(B(x,r))$ with linear modulus $C_1>0$, and let $\psi:B(x,r)\to\R$ be a semiconvex function with linear modulus $C_2>0$. If $\psi$ touches $\phi$ from below at $x$ in $B(x,r)$, then we have the following properties:
	\begin{enumerate}[\rm (1)]
		\item both $\phi$ and $\psi$ are differentiable at $x$ and $D\psi(x)=D\phi(x)$.
		\item for $C=\max\{C_1,C_2\}$ we have that
		\begin{align*}
			|p-D\phi(x)|\leqslant 3C|y-x|,\qquad \forall y\in B(x,\frac r2), p\in D^+\phi(y);\\
			|p-D\psi(x)|\leqslant 3C|y-x|,\qquad \forall y\in B(x,\frac r2), p\in D^-\psi(y).
		\end{align*}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.749474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc21db291362e384c40c53208f0af3d0dd2e6fa87a4e2260f316a6e080558e2b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 ({\cite[(1.16)) of arXiv:2608.18834, 'The Parabolic Anderson Model's Total Mass at Small Times: Geometry, Fluctuations, and Reno'] {BurchardSchmuckenschlager}}]

For every bounded domain $D$,
\begin{align}

|D|-\int_D u_0(t,x)\d x\gtrsim t^{1/2}.
\end{align}
In other words, the total mass cannot converge to $|D|$ at a faster rate than $t^{1/2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.045986+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc24e37a892bf8bc11567cd2ebb5e074e3ae675630707a79db0a0541178e8e3e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_an_tube_hitting of arXiv:2411.13972, 'The Stochastic Bessel operator at high temperatures'] ~\\
For any $\gamma<0$,
\begin{equation*}
