{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.404264+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd9eaa463de4e9af11da4a198efc4fda3ef4e4405399237fb56a54baa63b981c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 of arXiv:2609.03185, 'Uniqueness of tangent flows in free boundary flow'] There exist constants $C,\epsilon_0,\theta, T > 0$ and $p>1$ with the following property. Set $\epsilon=D_{\mathscr T^{\alpha,\mathscr C_+}_\tau}(M_{\tau_0}).$ Assume that $|\alpha|,\epsilon,T^{-1}\leq\epsilon_0, \tau+1\leq T_\alpha$, and $\tau_0\geq T$.

If $\epsilon>e^{-\frac{\tau_0}{8}}$, then
$$\left(\int_{M_{\tau_0+1}\cap B_{(1+\theta)R_\epsilon}(0)} d_{\mathscr T^{\alpha,\mathscr C_+}_{\tau+1}}^{2p}
e^{-\frac{|x|^2}{4}}\,d\mathcal H^n \right)^{\frac{1}{2p}} \leq C\epsilon,$$
and $M_{\tau_0+1}$ is an $\frac{\eta}{4}$-graph over $\mathscr T^{\alpha,\mathscr C_+}_\tau$ on $B_{(1+\theta)R_\epsilon}(0)$.

If $\epsilon\leq e^{-\frac{\tau_0}{8}}$, then
$$\left(\int_{M_{\tau_0+1}\cap B_{(1+\theta) \sqrt{\tau_0}}(0)} d_{\mathscr T^{\alpha,\mathscr C_+}_{\tau+1}}^{2p}
e^{-\frac{|x|^2}{4}}\,d\mathcal H^n \right)^{\frac{1}{2p}}\leq Ce^{-\frac{\tau_0}{8}},$$
and $M_{\tau_0+1}$ is an $\frac{\eta}{4}$-graph over $\mathscr T^{\alpha,\mathscr C_+}_\tau$ on $B_{(1+\theta) \sqrt{\tau_0}}(0)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.422889+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dda1ca6b86c48d3a2e245f836c02ecdd08686c37bd1e23ee5cebcf1d213b683b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cumulant-convergence of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] Let $a_1,\ldots,a_n\in\mathcal{A}$ be cactus field-type monomials and let $a_{i,N}$ be their evaluations at $(V_N,V_N^*,\mathbf D_N)$. Then, we have
