{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.752794+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ddb105af24218cc699a49d4ca6fb83018d9ce78932f62d2fc3c1ea459f2ee6f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2604.11682, 'Semilocalization for inhomogeneous random graphs'] Fix $x \in \vertices$ and $\nu > 0$. There exists a constant $C_{\nu} \geq 0$
