{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.224594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de54c77073fb17f66b39dc595fa9ff39a6490ce91f23e135dea0ab759960191f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Gonzalez and Qing \cite{GonzQing} of arXiv:2609.00324, 'Quantitative Stability for Fractional Yamabe minimizers'] Let $\gamma \in (0,1)$ and $a= 1-2\gamma$. There exists a constant $\bar{S} (n,\gamma)$ such that, for every $U\in \dot{W}^{1,2}(\mathbb{R}_{+}^{n+1}, y^a )$ with trace $TU =w$, the following inequality holds
    \begin{align*}
        \|w \|_{L^{2^{*}}(\mathbb{R}^n )}^2 \leq \bar{S}(n,\gamma) \int_{\mathbb{R}_{+}^{n+1}} y^a |\nabla U|^2 dxdy \, ,
    \end{align*}
    where $\bar{S}(n,\gamma) = d_\gamma^* S(n,\gamma)$. Equality holds if and only if
    \begin{align*}
        w(x) = c \left(\frac{\mu}{\mu^2 + |x-x_0 |^2}\right)^{\frac{n-2\gamma}{2}} \quad x \in \mathbb{R}^n,
    \end{align*}
    for $c \in \mathbb{R}$, $\mu >0$ and $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}^n$, and $U$ is the Poisson extension of $w$ given by the convolution with the Poisson kernel. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.888967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de57bc02436d5af79998f8aa4b7cc087406689fb09a81d9c94a4aa35848bfd64","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2608.29554, 'Limiting Behavior of a Class of Hermitian Yang--Mills Metrics, II: Exponential Approximati'] There exists a constant $C>1$, independent of $\epsilon$, such that for
