where $u$ and $v$ are words and $a$ and $b$ are letters, and where
 `$ {\mathbf 1}$' is the empty word.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.786262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_de72dc45054c89bf9df8c396c5e59c2ecff3a8e06039faa661a883f255c39184","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2604.00598, 'Allowing for Imprecision in the Game-theoretic Characterisation of the Poisson Process'] For all time points~\(s,t\in\posreals\) such that \(s\leq t\) and \(g\in\bfns\),
