where $z_2^{\ast0}=1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.299351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df7e8439e76512f30029be528b9cb7ac480a638252dda41c2fc326ae0f561649","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:beta-quotient-regimes of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ n \in {\mathbb N} $, $ \beta \in [0,1) $.
Then one has that
\bas{
\frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n}\le \begin{cases} \frac{2}{n}, & \text{ if } n\le (1-\beta)^{-1}\\
\frac{1-\beta}{1-e^{-1}}, & \text{ if } n\ge (1-\beta)^{-1}
\end{cases}
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.807038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df8315026796bc2b15d53c3eb6446e2fe50bfbaef90097103c736b4b7c13649c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition phiE1 of arXiv:2606.24304, 'Quantitative Homogenization of PDEs with Neumann boundary conditions: a probabilistic appr'] Divide $[t,T]$ into subintervals with the same length $\Lambda>0$.  For any $q>1$,
\begin{eqnarray}  
{\mathbbm E}\left[\max_k\left(\phi^{t,x}_{(k+1)\Lambda}
