{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.816846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df88193d092609f25dd6b2456bb9920a62f1b97a1ccd59e9952a57750ae50720","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main-order-m of arXiv:2607.17048, 'Concentration Inequalities for Incomplete U-statistics over Arbitrary Sampling Graphs'] Suppose for every $e=(i_1, i_2,\ldots,i_m)\in E$, there exists $\sigma_e>0$ such that 
\begin{equation} 
\mathbb{E}\Bigl[e^{\lambda \{h_e(X_{i_1}, \ldots, X_{i_m})-\mathbb{E}h_e(X_{i_1}, \ldots, X_{i_m})\}}\Bigr]\leq e^{\lambda^2\sigma_e^2/2}, \qquad\mbox{for all $\lambda>0$}. 
\end{equation}
If there exists a proper $K$-edge-coloring of $G$, then for all $t>0$, 
\[
\mathbb{P}(U-\mathbb{E}U>t)\leq \exp\biggl\{ - \frac{t^2}{2K\sum_{e\in E}\sigma_e^2}\biggr\}. 
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.829904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df8c1cafaa17eaac8b51ef371c45096df51260ad11d4fb2d8bc67110494ad2e5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Fr\'echet derivative of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] We say that $\Phi$ is \emph{Fr\'echet differentiable} at a point $x\in E$ if there exists a bounded linear operator $D\Phi(x):E\to F$ such that

\begin{align}
\lim_{\norma{h}_{E}\to0}\frac{\norma{\Phi(x+h)-\Phi(x)-D\Phi(x)h}_{F}}{\norma{h}_{E}}=0.    
\end{align}
The operator $D\Phi(x)$ is called the \emph{Fr\'echet derivative} of $\Phi$ at $x$.","status":"unverified"}

