{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.161359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e021c680fbc1f111b2a1fc11862fc1ef0372b2d381cf79f32a80f802e380abd4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PropBivIntegral of arXiv:2608.28949, 'The information geometry of product-reference discrete diffusion: Interaction growth compl'] For any pair $0 < a < b < 1$, we can write the KL product-reference
error over the interval $[a,b]$ as
\begin{subequations}
  \begin{align}

    \Gamma_{\scaleto{\operatorname{prod}}{5pt}}(a, b) & = \int_{\ensuremath{\varphi}(a)}^{\ensuremath{\varphi}(b)}
    \int_\eta^{\ensuremath{\varphi}(b)} \ensuremath{\mathsf{Q}_{\scaleto{\textsf{IGC}\xspace}{4pt}}}(\eta, \xi) \, d\xi \, d\eta.
  \end{align}
  Moreover, the associated \textsf{IGC}\xspace increment takes the form
  \begin{align}

    \mathsf{G}(a, b) & = \int_{\ensuremath{\varphi}(a)}^{\ensuremath{\varphi}(b)} \ensuremath{\mathsf{Q}_{\scaleto{\textsf{IGC}\xspace}{4pt}}}(\eta,
    \eta) \, d\eta.
  \end{align}
  Finally, the total correlation (\ensuremath{\mathsf{TC}}) and dual total correlation
  (\ensuremath{\mathsf{DTC}}) have the representations
  \begin{align}

    \ensuremath{\mathsf{TC}}(Z) \stackrel{(\ensuremath{\mathsf{TC}})}{=} \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
