{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.570480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e079a89e0a95152a8640300c6f0bb9167189bdb29f50ce6020da3d61a266bbf3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.tau-k-decomp of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] For every $k\ge 1$ and $n\ge 2k$, there exists an event
