	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:59:58.436820+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e0b54ea3d38e8cd871a74d5c19d0399ec379ad1840bcc07ccafa625a44591df5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.FKGinequality of arXiv:2604.24743, 'The impact of disorder and non-convex interactions on delocalisation of height functions'] For $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}^*$, let $J_1 , \ldots, J_n$ be independent random variables, and let $f , g : \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^n \to [0 , \infty)$ 
