{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.984145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e21b1a1e6b9905d61eeccb26dd410025107f3e6d19956210bce76fcf78d20d85","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor nmlinfinf of arXiv:2412.00822, '\textsc{Ideal Poisson--Voronoi tessellations \\ beyond hyperbolic spaces}'] Let $(\theta_{1},\phi_{1},r_{1})$ and $(\theta,\phi,r)$ be two corona points.
In the model of $\mathcal{M}$ given by the product of upper-half planes $\mathbb{U}_{2} \times \mathbb{U}_{2}$:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] If $(\theta_{1},\phi_{1})$ is sent at $(\infty,\infty)$,

$$
\emph{\text{NML}}((\infty,\infty, r_{1}),(\theta,\phi, r)) = \left \lbrace (z_{1},z_{2})\in \mathcal{M}\,;\;  |z_{1}-\theta|^{2} \cdot |z_{2}-\phi|^{2}=\frac{r_{1}}{r}\left(1+|\theta|^{2} \right)\left(1+|\phi|^{2} \right)\right \rbrace \; ;
$$
\item[(ii)] If $(\theta_{1},\phi_{1})$ is sent at $(\infty,y)$, for $y\in \mathbb{R}$,
{
$$
\emph{\text{NML}}((\infty,y, r_{1}),(\theta,\phi, r)) = \left \lbrace (z_{1},z_{2})\in \mathcal{M} \,;\;  \frac{|z_{1}-\theta|^{2} \cdot |z_{2}-\phi|^{2}}{|z_{2}-y|^{2}}=\frac{r_{1}}{r}\frac{\left(1+|\theta|^{2} \right)\left(1+|\phi|^{2} \right)}{1+|y|^{2}}\right \rbrace \;.
$$
}

\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.983647+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e21c85d6028901983d6c776118be021a6d85fffc610d31df4236c6372ef2117d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro_2 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] For a symmetric matrix $A$, 
