is a well defined sequence in $\mathcal{H}$, that is, the series in (equation eq8 of the paper) converges for all
 $n\in\mathbb{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.764262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3075e08378283fe3c2a338e93fbe0e8deef9999aef6b606ac2ffba4226663fd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:pathwise-cluster-product-green-energy of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] Fix $x\in\Omega_{\rm Fr}\cap\Omega_{\rm op}$, and let
