{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.739458+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e31c11fe63582a076ea4c362cf566a03122171fd04c2e8428400b7dfbd156936","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2605.02430, '\textbf{Scaling limit of the range of tree-valued branching random walks in random environ'] We keep the above notation: recall that $(\bT,\boo)$ is an infinite GW tree whose offspring distribution $\nu$ is supercritical, that we denote by $\tau_n$ is a GW tree with offspring distribution $\mu$ conditioned to have $n$ vertices for all sufficiently large $n$, and that $(\bT,\boo)$ and $\tau_n$ are independent. We assume that $\mu$ satisfies (\ref{hypostaintro}) and that $\nu$ satisfies (\ref{defmusiintro}).  We furthermore assume that there exists $\ttb \ino \big(\tfrac{2\alpha}{\alpha -1} , \infty \big)$ such that $\sum_{k\in \bbN} k^{1+ 2\ttb} \nu (k) \leko \infty$. 
Recall from (\ref{spacdefintro}) the definition of the spaces $\ftau_n$ and $\bcR_n$. 
We denote by $(T_H, d_H, \mathtt r_h, \ttm_H)$ the normalized $\alpha$-stable L\'evy tree and by 
$(T_{H, W} , d_{H, W}, \mathtt r_{H, W}, \ttm_{H, W})$ the normalized Brownian cactus with $\alpha$-stable branching mechanism as defined above. Recall that $\bbM$ is the space 
of isometry classes of pointed measured compact metric spaces equipped with the Gromov--Hausdorff--Prokhorov distance. 
Then, \emph{conditionally given the environment} $(\bT, \boo)$, the following joint convergence 
\begin{equation}

\big( \ftau_n, \bcR_n \big) \underset{n\rightarrow \infty}{- \!\!\! - \!\!\! - \!\!\! \longrightarrow }  \Big(\big(T_H,d_H,\mathtt r_H,\ttm_H\big)\, ;\, \big(T_{H,W},d_{H,W},\mathtt r_{H,W},\ttm_{H,W}\big)\Big)
\end{equation}
holds weaky on $\bbM^2$ equipped with the product topology. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.258396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e31cba1227fb4cada764f45be2da62a139f69fe4a91e5bdc262f6a8102283711","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 125 (\cite{LTDMLS}) of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Set $c=3-a-b$ and define the sets 
		\begin{flalign*}
			& \mathcal{A} = \{ (s, t, u, v) \in \mathbb{R}^4 : (s, t) \in \mathcal{T} \}; \\
			& \mathcal{W} = \{ (a, b, x, y) \in \mathbb{R}^4 : 0 < \min \{ a, b \} < a+b < 3, (x, y) \in \mathfrak{L}_{a,b,c} \},
		\end{flalign*}

		\noindent and define the map $\Phi :  \mathcal{W} \mapsto\mathcal{A}$ by setting 
