in terms of the concatenation of repeated bracket products of the letters in each subword as indicated. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:15:15.571540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3b9a241ef1ca87339fd97ea5697e07464b7ffc91a16d0039b7b493b2d8be4d0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cumulant-comparison of arXiv:2507.12502, 'Quantitative Edge Eigenvector Universality for Random Regular Graphs: Berry-Esseen Bounds '] For any smooth test function $f : \mathbb{R}^K \to \mathbb{R}$ with bounded derivatives up to order 4, and overlaps $\mathbf{X} = (X_2^{(\mathbf{q})}, \ldots, X_{K+1}^{(\mathbf{q})})$ at the edge:
\[
\left|\mathbb{E}[f(\mathbf{X}^{\tilde{H}_{t_*}})] - \mathbb{E}[f(\mathbf{X}^{W})]\right| \leq C(f,K) N^{-1/3+2\varepsilon}
\]
where $C(f,K) = \|f\|_{C^4} \cdot K^4 \cdot \text{poly}(d,\varepsilon^{-1})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.100033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e3bd0f03a167469cf8bdd1335b56fd2b09dd023be8bb365a75a820744d3ab25a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm:diffbounds of arXiv:2411.13030, 'Classification of the limit shape for 1+1-dimensional FPP'] Let $G$ be non-deterministic and $v\ge 0$. For each $n$, let $\gamma^n(v)$ be the geodesic from the origin to $(n, {\lceil v n \rceil})$. The following bounds hold almost surely:
\begin{equation}

\partial^+ \Lambda(v) \le \liminf_{n \to \infty} \frac 1 n \left( U(\gamma^n(v))+R(\gamma^n(v))-D(\gamma^n(v))\right)
\end{equation}
and
