{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.232686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e715665069b45ac4a6e1fc8e8321a5f2c320b2e82466bdf9a5c31894937caec8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 51 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] A sequence $Z_\bullet = (Z_1,Z_2,\dots)$ in $\prod_{k\ge 1}\calK(\S_k(\A))$ is the summary of some separable unital representation $\pi$ if and only if it has these two closure properties:
