    Then, for all $z\in \C$, $t\geq 0$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{L}\pr{\acc{(x,\xi)\in [0,1]^d\times \T^d\m;\m \bb{p(x,\xi)-z}^2\leq t}}\leq Ct^\kappa
    \end{equation}
    where
    \begin{equation}
        \kappa=\frac{1}{2S}\mm\text{and}\mm C= 14d\pr{\frac{\sqrt{\Xi}}{m}}^{\frac{1}{S}}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.042060+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e729f463100923aa7c1ac739ff6bf79240e0b5916fbc901800a0a7c79d344652","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 20 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Assume reversibility $\eqref{eq:ydetail}$ of the rates $r_x$.
