{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.625473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e852d085131cf5769ad7bb8b18cf54f4b2cb48cdfa57b00e196f354f89512935","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem: song4.1 of arXiv:2411.03512, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of Sublinear Expectation System and Applications'] For given $\phi\in C_{lip}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $\Gamma$ a bounded closed convex subset of $\mathbb{R}^d$, set $v(t,x):=\sup_{y\in \Gamma}\phi(x+ty)$. Then there exists a non-negative function $f^{\epsilon}:\mathbb{R}^d\times\mathbb{R}\to \mathbb{R}_+$ such that $v_{\epsilon}$ satisfies
