We can verify as above that the topology $\mathscr{Z}_2$ is not metrizable either.

\item[(iii)] $C([0,T];\newone{H}_{,w})\coloneqq$ the space of  continuous functions $\bv: [0,T] \to \newone{H}_{,w}$ endowed with the topology $\mathscr{Z}_3$ defined as in item (o).

\item[(iv)] $C([0,T];\newonep{V})\coloneqq$  the space of $\newonep{V}$-valued trajectories with the topology $\mathscr{Z}_4$ of the uniform convergence on $[0,T]$. $C([0,T];\newonep{V})$  is a separable Banach space.

\item[(v)] $L_w^{\beta}(0,T;\newone{V})\coloneqq$ the space $L^\beta(0,T;\newone{V})$ with the weak topology $\mathscr{Z}_5$.

\item[(vi)] The separable Hilbert space $L^2(0,T;\StokesH)$ with the topology $\mathscr{Z}_6$  induced by the norm. 

