{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.781517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8bb84d9e867994ee6371b56ae7eb282402dcf95978adb8e07a71920ef59fea5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 32 (Wiener isometry) of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For $k\in\N_0^N$, let $n = \abs{k}$. The map 
