{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.827372+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8bc922d98e73d8203dd11b5b6532ef5461d7878d08e4cf9211c08a0c03dfdbe","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition signature of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $x:[0,T]\to E$ be a path of bounded variation. Its signature over $[s,t]$ is
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Sig}(x)_{s,t}
=
\left(1,
\int_{s<u_1<t}\,\mathrm{d} x_{u_1},
\int_{s<u_1<u_2<t}\,\mathrm{d} x_{u_1}\otimes\,\mathrm{d} x_{u_2},
\ldots\right).
\end{equation}
For a word $w=i_1\cdots i_k$,
\begin{equation}
\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(x)_{s,t}}{w}
=
\int_{s<u_1<\cdots<u_k<t}\,\mathrm{d} x^{i_1}_{u_1}\cdots\,\mathrm{d} x^{i_k}_{u_k}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.671109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e8c8858ecee7162de5fd52d97bf6ff20c300ababb7782f0f73a65bf199f574b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 28 (Quantitative estimates for one block) of arXiv:2608.30027, 'Under Ricci flow, a 3-torus goes flat'] The constants in Theorem~\ref{thm:one-block-contraction} can be chosen together
