{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.368179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e91d123971de5c2a50bd247c4bbd66da43d186865a339cf082cf75476c2a85e0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:chen_mixed of arXiv:2412.01645, 'Regularisation by Gaussian rough path lifts of fractional Brownian motions'] We denote by $\mathcal{R}^{\gamma, \beta}([0, 1]; V\times E)$ the collection of all elements ${\color{purp}g}=(g^\bullet, g^\circ, \mathbb{g}^{\bullet\bullet},  \mathbb{g}^{\circ\bullet}, \mathbb{g}^{\bullet\circ})$, such that 
