{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.859705+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea3f808c9b06a8dd680d0963729574b855d0d8830d94fbc52e2a1a6ce30c861f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem overtake-bound of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Suppose that $(X_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$, $(X'_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ and $Y$ are mutually independent random variables, with $(X_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}} \sim (X'_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$. Suppose that, for $k \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$, there exists $\lambda > 0$ such that
    \begin{equation} 
    \prod_{i=k}^{\infty}\E{e^{\lambda  (X'_{i} - X_{i})}} < \infty.  
    \end{equation}
    Then, for any $\ell \in \mathbb{N}$
    \begin{equation} 
        \Prob{\exists j \in \mathbb{N}\colon Y + \sum_{i=1}^{k + j} X_{i} \leq \sum_{i=k}^{k+j} X'_{i}} \leq \left(\prod_{i=k}^{\infty}\E{e^{\lambda  (X'_{i} - X_{i})}}\right) \E{e^{- \lambda \left(Y + \sum_{i=1}^{k-1} X_{i}\right)}}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:13:22.516306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea419628d2f8fb3c230a403110bfede0cd1d79d55eb34b41a64a068d0f3c164f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor gamma 1 gamma2 capacity change of arXiv:2505.16093, 'Multiple chordal SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Moser system'] Let $\gamma$, $\tilde{\gamma}$ be two hulls starting at $x \in \partial \mathbb{H}$ and $y \in \partial \mathbb{H}$ with capacity $\varepsilon$ and $c \varepsilon$ , let $g_{\varepsilon}$ be the normalized map removing $\gamma$ and $\tilde{\varepsilon}= \operatorname{hcap}(g_{\varepsilon}\circ \gamma(t))$, then we have:

\begin{equation}
\tilde{\varepsilon}=
c \varepsilon\left(1-\frac{4\varepsilon}{(x-y)^2}\right)+o\left(\varepsilon^2\right)
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.610841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea4608c79d08ce6d013cdd9c53ce14098e35de2b9e9e60393b86592285cfbbf9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: recipe of arXiv:2604.05941, 'Banach spaces of continuous paths with finite $p$-th variation'] Fix any $p>1$. Suppose that $h\in C^1([0,1])$ is non-decreasing with $h(0)=0$, and that $\big[(h')^{1/p}\big]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}}\equiv 0$. Then, there exists a function $y\in V^p_{\mathbb{T}}$ such that
    \begin{equation}    
        [y]^{(p)}_{\mathbb{T}}(t)=h(t),\qquad \forall\,t\in[0,1].
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, if in addition $(h')^{1/p}\in C^{\alpha}([0,1])$ for some $\alpha\leq \frac1p$, then $y$ is also in $C^{\alpha}([0,1])\cap V^p_{\mathbb{T}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.167850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ea48a7454c3e54706543c28aa7d8ea5583d66df3a619f1e69b05c6855c697c05","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2604.17973, 'Schauder estimates and classical solutions of the Dirichlet problem for stochastic parabol'] Let $u$ be a quasi-classical solution of \eqref{eq:model-half-space}--\eqref{eq:model-half-space-bc} with $g\equiv0$. Assume that
\[
f\in C_x^{\alpha}(\bar Q_T^+;L_\omega^\gamma),
\qquad
f|_{\Sigma_T}\in C_{x,t}^{\alpha,\alpha/2}(\Sigma_T;L_\omega^\gamma),
\qquad
f(0,\cdot)|_{\partial\R_+^n}=0.
\]
Then
\begin{equation}
|D_x^2u|_{(\alpha,\alpha/2);Q_T^+}^{L_\omega^\gamma}
\le C\Bigl(
|u|_{0;Q_T^+}^{L_\omega^\gamma}
