    are attained by $(m+1)$-atomic measures. Equivalently, if $X$ is any random variable on $[a,b]$ with given moments $\mathbb{E}[X^k]$ for $k=1,\ldots,m$, then sharp bounds on $\mathbb{E}[p(X)]$ for any degree-$r$ polynomial $p$ are attained by discrete random variables supported on at most $m+1$ points. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

