\noindent where $\mathcal{N}$ is a standard normal random variable independent of $W$. The constant $\sigma$ can be explicitly computed; see (equation eq121 of the paper) (and in particular, $\mathbb{E}[H_{\Lambda}(t)] = a_{\alpha} e^{\alpha t}$, for $t \in \mathbb{R}$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

