{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.744738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecadf28ded723863e0f7431864b2550ae27d9beffbf4a9954ebab37a3850532b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2604.03548, 'Degree-preserving conservative processes and a unified approach for their hydrodynamics'] A sequence $\{P_{N}, N\geq{1}\}$ of probability measures defined on $D([0,T],H^{-m}(\mathbb T))$ is tight if the following two conditions hold:
