{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.205097+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee81f7372e05c1186a04908479a5fa3e14a30590520441f581ce66fe5f241d97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:ckreform of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] Consider the Crow-Kimura replicator-mutator equation 
	\begin{align}

		\partial_t \rho_t(x) = - \nabla \cdot (\rho_t(x) g(x)) + \frac{1}{2} \nabla \cdot (\Sigma \rho_t(x))  +  \rho_t(x) (\mathbb{E}_{z \sim \rho_t}[f_t(x,z)] -  \mathbb{E}_{\rho_t}[f_t]) 
	\end{align}
	with fitness landscape given by (equation eq:genquadfit of the paper).  This equation can be expressed in the form 

	\begin{align}
		\nonumber 
