    \end{displaymath}
    Moreover, $a \mapsto H\big( T_{a}(X) | \pi_{aT}  \big)$ is convex.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.650949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f00df8048a8820d67941117a7ade581a8a756555400202b6ae119ca0d9d8ebf3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem DCXSZ of arXiv:2411.04590, 'Singular stochastic delay equations driven by fractional Brownian motion: Dynamics, longti'] Assume the same hypotheses as in Theorem (SSS of the paper). Then $\phi_{\mathbf{X}}(\xi)$ is is Fr\'echet differentiable (with respect to $\xi$). In addition, for 
			$D_{\xi}\phi_{\mathbf{X}}:\mathscr{D}_{\mathbf{X}}^{\gamma}([0,r]\rightarrow \mathscr{D}_{\mathbf{X}}^{\gamma}([0,r] $, we can find a polynomial $Q_1$ such that
