where $\mathcal{C}$ denotes the class of convex sets in $\mathbb{R}^{mK}$ and $C_{d,m}$ depends only on $d$ and $m$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.374655+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f06742aac232277658de22305107a7d97216621484da358799319a7535ce53e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Schervish estimates of arXiv:2412.06420, 'Accuracy, Estimates, and Representation Results'] Assume $\mathsf{acc}_k:\mathsf{ConvHull}(\mathsf{Values}(V))\to\mathbb{R}$ is absolutely continuous for each $k\in\mathsf{range}(V)$.

