{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.225007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f12329e6f3a65ebb402ee74879f861b15263419d6e04d159df04ae924598e039","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma integrable of arXiv:2609.00324, 'Quantitative Stability for Fractional Yamabe minimizers'] Let $u_* \in \mathcal{M}_1$. Then $u_*$ is integrable if and only if the reduced functional $q$ is constant in a neighborhood of $0 \in K$. In particular, if $u_* \in \mathcal{M}_1$ is an integrable minimizer, then
