{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:56.869684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f259e5f3f4d434969d2cf26da3f44a74e3f2abfe183943f4076d02a41c65924a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Big_Bad_Tree_lemma of arXiv:2603.28520, 'The Supercritical Loop O(1) and Random Current Models: Uniqueness and Mixing'] Let $n\in \mathbb{N}$, $\mathtt{d}> 2$,$C>0, \lambda >1.$ There exists $C'>0$ with the following property: Suppose that $\alpha>0$ and $\nu$ is a percolation measure  on $\mathscr{T}_n^\mathtt{d}$ satisfying \begin{enumerate}
