{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.663517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2b06148cf29023bd51666e2b3cc09cf31f071d76ed1a993d4c10e08d28f942b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 (\cite{CT}) of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Let $(\xi^i,f^i,g^i,S^i)$  be two sets of parameters satisfying (H1)-(H5)  with $S^i_T\leq \xi^i$, q.s., $i=1,2$. Let  $(Y^i,Z^i,A^i)\in\mathcal{S}^2_G(0,T)$ be the solution to the reflected $G$-BSDE with parameters $(\xi^i,f^i,g^i,S^i)$,  $i=1,2$. Assume that $Y^i\in S^\infty(0,T)$, $Z^i\in BMO_G$ and $A^i_T\in \cap_{p\geq 2}L^p_G(\Omega_T)$ for $i=1,2$. If $\xi^1\geq \xi^2$, $f^1\geq f^2$, $g^1\geq g^2$ and $S^1\geq S^2$, q.s., then
