{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:55.645638+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2ce5f45f38d44d3b889983469c38de8c6780a0137fe80a8bdfccc52058a0647","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Shifted Wasserstein recursion) of arXiv:2605.24937, '2605.24937'] Assume~\eqref{eq:one-step-w2-framework}. For all $0\le n\le N-2$,
\begin{equation}
  d_{n+1}^{\,2}
  \;\le\;
  L^{2}(1-\eta_n)^{2}\,d_n^{\,2}
  +2\,(1-\eta_n)\,\overline a_1\,d_n
  +\overline a_0^{\,2},
\end{equation}
where
$\overline a_0:=\sup_{0\le k<N}\|a_0(\widehat X_k)\|_{L^{2}}$
and
$\overline a_1:=\sup_{0\le k<N}\|a_1(\widehat X_k,\widetilde Y_k)\|_{L^{2}}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.575796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f2ceb5e4d74e166de6d53c0a32ca34366dc9d13f2402f46131a1687de3911744","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 44 of arXiv:2606.14564, 'Upper tails for irregular graphs \\ beyond the mean-field regime'] There exist positive constants $\eta$ and $\sigma$ such that the following holds for all $p_H \le p \le p_H \cdot n^\eta$.
  For all $J' \subseteq J \in \cJ^*$, all large enough $n$, and all $G \subseteq K_n$ with at most $f \cdot \bigl(\log(1/p)\bigr)^2$ edges,
  \[
    \left|\bigl\{\varphi \in \Emb(J,K_n) : \varphi(J) \cap G = \varphi(J')\bigr\} \right| \cdot p^{e_J - e_{J'}} \le
