{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:30:07.918283+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f359fb1905b215d4300b65c80be523b2ac1596c1daddcf09fdf5e5bfa27c5127","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:P-sharp-lower of arXiv:2608.12147, 'The Average Singular Value of a Complex Gaussian Random Matrix Strictly Decreases with Dim'] For $N\geqslant3$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
 P_N\geqslant \frac1{3(N+1)}\Bigg[&A_0-\frac1{\pi(2N-1)}
 +\frac{W_{1,N}}{2N+1}
 +\frac{W_{2,N}}{(2N+1)^2}\Bigg],
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where
\begin{align}
\mathcal{H}_N^* & := \frac8{15}+\frac12\log\frac{2N+1}{7},\nonumber \\
W_{1,N}& := \frac1\pi\left(\mathcal{H}_N^*+\frac16-\frac1{2(2N+1)}\right),
\\ 
W_{2,N}& := \frac1\pi\left(\frac{N-1}{2}+\mathcal{H}_N^*-\frac1{12}+\frac1{4(2N+1)}\right).
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

