    \mathsf{ord}_{\mathrm{loc}}  W ( \bar{\omega } ) = 2 ( \alpha^{-1} - 1) \; , 
    \end{equation*}
    while
    \begin{equation*}
    \mathsf{ord}_H C_\alpha^\mathrm{crit} = \alpha^{-1} \; . 
    \end{equation*}
    Moreover the minimum of $ \underline{\mathsf{ord}}_{\mathrm{loc}}  W(\cdot) $ on the space of continuous function $\Omega$ is equal to $2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.666657+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f425c5dbed1bc48da6c3a9611beb015e4615f412392561b6ad633fee48796045","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 28 of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] Let $u$ be a continuous function defined on $[0,T]\times \mathbb{R}$. It is called a viscosity:\\
	\noindent (i) subsolution  of \eqref{PDE} if $u(T,x)\leq \phi(x)$, $x\in\mathbb{R}$, and at any point $(t,x)\in(0,T)\times\mathbb{R}$, for any $(p,q,X)\in\mathcal{P}^{2,+}u(t,x)$,
	\begin{equation}
		\max\bigg(u(t,x)-h'(t,x), \min\big(u(t,x)-h(t,x), -p-F(X,q,u(t,x),x,t)\big)\bigg)\leq 0;
	\end{equation}
	(ii) supersolution of \eqref{PDE} if $u(T,x)\geq\phi(x)$, $x\in\mathbb{R}$, and at any point $(t,x)\in(0,T)\times\mathbb{R}$, for any $(p,q,X)\in\mathcal{P}^{2,-}u(t,x)$,
	\begin{equation}
		\max\bigg(u(t,x)-h'(t,x),\min\big(u(t,x)-h(t,x), -p-F(X,q,u(t,x),x,t)\big)\bigg)\geq 0;
	\end{equation}
	(iii) solution of \eqref{PDE} if it is both a viscosity subsolution and supersolution.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.425193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f429556b2ececb3e71f0992adb83215127a45527934c408f8f71cbfb9d2aaf4d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 163 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that $A,B,C,\mathfrak{t}$ depend on $\N\rightarrow\infty$ and denote $\frac{A}{\N}=\hat A$, $\frac{B}{\N}=\hat B$, $\frac{C}{\N}=\hat C$, $\frac{\mathfrak{t}}{\N}=\hat{\mathfrak{t}}$. Then Assumptions \ref{Assumptions_Theta}, \ref{Assumptions_basic} and \ref{Assumptions_analyticity} hold for \eqref{eq_Hahn_ensemble} and the (simplified) equilibrium measure is given by the explicit formula of Theorem~\ref{Proposition_ZW_equilibrium_measure}. Assumption~\ref{Assumptions_offcrit} also hold for $\N$ large enough provided the distances between $\hat{\mathfrak{t}} \in (0,\hat{B} + \hat{C})$ and each of the following values
