        \limsup\limits_{T \to +\infty}\exp(\lambda_1 T)\left(\left(\Exp{P_{T}}-\Exp{Q_{T}}\right)\left[\log\left(\frac{d(R_{T/2}^*\nu)}{d\diffref}(\Phi_{T/2}(x_{T/2}))\right)\right]\right) < +\infty.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.899124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4a245deb7a51f5590eceab4c6606af3130132b7b4e8e8f392192c4a690c02fa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 27 of arXiv:2608.02103, '$p$-Adic Diffusion and Random Walks on $[0,1]$'] Let $\mathfrak{M}_n$ be the Markov 

    process 
    attached to $W_n$. Then for given two states $I^{(n)},J^{(n)}\in A_n$  the transition probability of $\mathfrak{M}_n$ is given by the solution of the following Cauchy problem for $u(\cdot,t)\in X_n$, and $u(x,\cdot)\in C^1[0,\infty)$:
