{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.231068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4aa664519776fa32340a2c970c77f9efe8176a51cc36fd0bca83e72df1fcae8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 24 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] For the \textbf{TASEP height function} $(\hTASEP(\lambda;y,t))_{y\in \Z,t\geq 0}$, assume that $(0,0) \in \lambda$ for a fixed down-right path $\lambda \in \Lambda$. For all $t\geq 0$, consider the down-right path
\begin{equation}
\lambda_t= (z^{t}_i)_{i \in \Z} := \{ w \in \Z^2 \, \colon \,  T_{\lambda,w} \leq t < T_{\lambda,w+(1,1)} \} 
\end{equation} such that $z^{t}_{0}=(x_t,x_t)$ for some $x_t \in \Z$. For $y \in \Z$ and $t > 0$, set $h_t(0)=x_t$ and recursively
\begin{equation}
h_t(i) - h_t(i-1) = \begin{cases} -1 & \text{ if } z^{t}_i-z^{t}_{i-1} = \eone , \\
 0 & \text{ if } z^{t}_i-z^{t}_{i-1} = -\etwo . 
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
 The \textbf{periodic TASEP height function} $\hpTASEP$ is defined as in \eqref{eq:CornerExtremalBasic} and \eqref{eq:CornerExtremalBasic2}, with respect to the periodic last passage times $\Tper$ from Definition~\ref{def:LastPassageTimes} and a down-right path $\lambda^{\per}_N \in \Lambda_{N,k}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.211653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4ae21a8ecd3d0d9ac90a054571e45c01d05750ebd0cf0f50406fff1136c9afe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem convex-opt of arXiv:2608.29018, 'Sharp Restricted Isometry Thresholds for\\ Global Minima of Rank-Restricted Matrix LASSO'] For $X\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{1}\times d_{2}}$, let $X=U\Sigma V^{T}$
denote its compact SVD. Suppose there exists $W$ such that 
\begin{gather}
\mathcal{A}^{*}[\mathcal{A}(X)-b]+\lambda(UV^{T}+W)=0,\nonumber \\
U^{T}W=0,\quad WV=0,\quad\normop W\le1.
\end{gather}
Then $X$ is a global minimizer of ((eq:matrix-lasso of the paper)) for every
$r\ge\operatorname{rank}(X)$. If, in addition, 
\begin{equation}
H\ne0,\mathcal{A}(H)=0\implies\normnuc{X+H}>\normnuc X
\end{equation}
then $X$ is the \emph{unique} global minimizer for every $r\ge\operatorname{rank}(X)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.800752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4aea69bc387fadf0f574fe6967f657ad06c8a6132a1a5221903902f78310b19","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 48 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Assume that $z \in \nU$. If $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, we define the following maps
\begin{align}

I_{s,t}^{n,z} &: \bZ_T \ni \bX \mapsto \int_{s}^{t} e^{i \langle \bX(r), z \rangle} \varphi_n^{z}(r,\bX(r)) \, \d r \in \mathbb{C},
\\

I_{s,t}^{z} &: \bZ_T \ni \bX \mapsto \int_{s}^{t} e^{i \langle \bX(r), z \rangle} \varphi^{z}(r,\bX(r)) \, \d r \in \mathbb{C},
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}

\varphi_n^{z}(r,\bX(r))&= i \; \duality{\bF_n(\bX(r))}{z}{}{} 
- \frac{1}{2} \Vert \duality{\newG_{0,n}(r,\bX(r))}{z}{}{} \Vert_{\ell^2}^2,
\\

\varphi^{z}(r,\bX(r))&= i \; \duality{\bF(\bX(r))}{z}{}{} 
- \frac{1}{2} \Vert \duality{\newG_0(r,\bX(r))}{z}{}{} \Vert_{\ell^2}^2,
\end{align}
with
   \begin{align}
     \newG_0: [0,T] \times \mathbb{V} \ni (t,\bX=(\bu,\phi))\mapsto (\bSi_0(t)\bu + \bG_0(t,\bu), 0)_{k=1}^\infty\coloneqq (\newG_{0}^k(t,\bu))_{k=1}^\infty \in 
     \ell^2(\nHB).
  \end{align}
Then the maps $I_{s,t}^{n,z}$  and $I_{s,t}^{z}$ are measurable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.275916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4aeaa92b6ede92ddab0e696a9852a5413cbb3efebc5c000452d4cb70dad326f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 1 (Poisson-gamma representation) of arXiv:2606.22066, 'A Bessel-zero obstruction to hyperbolic complete monotonicity of noncentral chi-square den'] For \(a,b>0\) and \(\theta\ge0\), \(p_{a,b,\theta}\) is a probability density on \((0,\infty)\), and
\begin{equation}

p_{a,b,\theta}(x)
=
e^{-\theta}\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}
\frac{\theta^m}{m!}\,
\gamma_{a+m,b}(x),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
\gamma_{\alpha,b}(x)
=
\frac{b^\alpha}{\Gamma(\alpha)}x^{\alpha-1}e^{-bx}.
\end{equation}
Equivalently, if \(N\sim\mathrm{Poisson}(\theta)\), then \(p_{a,b,\theta}\) is the density of a gamma law with random shape \(a+N\) and fixed rate \(b\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.076237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f4aeb14ccbafecd9aecbaa96a87f942da88d8f9a2232ce51911d9e2b3b562d3f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem convergence of conditioned ER graphs wrt resistance metric of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] If a sequence $(m_{n})_{n \geq 1}$ of natural numbers satisfies $n^{-2/3}m_{n} \to \sigma \in (0,\infty)$,
