{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.115476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f57d4cca5348f9f3177c3af2096986fa1afb0ea9be4c79609660eac0293de481","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem theorem-cvg-RFIM-partition-function of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $D \subset \mathbb{C}$, $a,b \in \partial D$ and $(D_{\delta};a_{\delta},b_{\delta})_{\delta}$ be as in Section (sec_assumptions_domain of the paper). Let $\lambda: \bar D \to (0,\infty)$ be a bounded and continuous function. Let $(H_{x})_{x \in \mathbb{Z}^2}$ be independent Gaussian random variables with mean $0$ and variance $1$ and set, for $x \in D_{\delta}$, $h_x = H_{x/\delta}$. Let $\xi \in \{-,\pm,+\}$.  Then, the rescaled partition function
    \begin{equation} 
        \tilde{\mathcal{Z}}_{\delta}^{\xi,\lambda, h}:= \exp\big(-\frac{\|\lambda\|_{L^{2}}^2}{2}\delta^{-\frac{1}{4}}\big) \mu_{\delta}^{\xi}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\delta^{\frac{7}{8}}\sum_{x \in D_{\delta}}\lambda(x)h_{x}\sigma_{x}\bigg)\bigg]
    \end{equation}
    converges in distribution as $\delta \to 0$ to a random variable $\mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\xi,W,\lambda}$ with Wiener chaos expansion
    \begin{equation} 
        \mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\xi,W,\lambda} = 1+ \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{C_{\sigma}^n}{n!}\int_{D^n} f_{D}^{(\xi,n)}(z_1,\dots,z_n) \prod_{j=1}^{n} \lambda(z_j)W(dz_j)
    \end{equation}
    where $W(\cdot)$ denotes white noise on $\mathbb{R}^2$ and where the functions $(f_{D}^{(\xi,n)})_n$ are as in Theorem (theorem_spin_correlations of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.120095+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f57fd47cb63fd8a0feb0ae00daeb284cd586d9686e63def97d5678b5065e1bab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition largeDeviation of arXiv:2608.17031, 'A shape theorem for periodic branching diffusion'] Fix $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $e\in S^{d-1}$. Let $\lambda_e>0$ be the minimizer in (equation eq:prelimCriticalSpeed of the paper), and recall that $\zeta_e = \lambda_e e$. Let $(Y_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the solution of (equation eq:SDETiling2.0 of the paper) under the measure $\mathbb{P}_x^{\zeta_e}$. Let $\hat{Y}_t:=(1/t)e\cdot(Y_t-Y_0)$. Let $I_e:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow (-\infty,+\infty]$ be the function defined by
    \begin{equation}
        I_e(\lambda)=\sup_{\eta \in \mathbb{R}} \{ \eta \lambda - [\gamma((\lambda_e+\eta)e)-\gamma(\zeta_e)]\}=[\gamma((\lambda_{e}+\cdot)e)-\gamma(\zeta_e)]^{*}(\lambda).
    \end{equation}
    For a set $A\subset \mathbb{R}$, let $I_e(A):=\inf_{\lambda\in A}I_e(\lambda)$. The following holds:
    \begin{enumerate}[(a)]
        \item For every closed set $\mathcal{C}\subset \mathbb{R}$, $\limsup_{t\rightarrow \infty}\sup_{x\in \mathbb{R}^d}\frac{1}{t}\log \mathbb{P}_x^{\zeta_e}[\hat{Y}_t \in \mathcal{C}]\leq -I_e(\mathcal{C})$.
        \item For every open set $\mathcal{O}\subset \mathbb{R}$, $\liminf_{t\rightarrow \infty}\inf_{x\in \mathbb{R}^d}\frac{1}{t}\log  \mathbb{P}_x^{\zeta_e}[\hat{Y}_t \in \mathcal{O}]\geq -I_e(\mathcal{O})$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.122045+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5811015a645842a28978989ff042b68dc994e454dcbfcffef3bced9cdb40898","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: interface exploration probability with number of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $I\subset \Lambda_{M}$ be a subset of $\Lambda_{M}.$ There exists a constant $c_{14}>0$ such that 
