{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:32:35.567157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f763928b7dca35ae7af909ca827a93ab56443721cbd2dd701db29ef4677ddb72","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.two-dependent of arXiv:2605.26082, 'Quantitative Einstein relation for reversible diffusions in a random environment'] Let $M_k\coloneqq(\Delta A_k^\lambda,\Delta\tau_k)$ for $k\ge 1$. The sequence $\{M_k\}_{k\ge 1}$ is strictly stationary and $2$-dependent under $\widehat{\mathbb P}_0^\lambda$: for every $r\ge1$ the law of $(M_j,\ldots,M_{j+r-1})$ is independent of $j$, and for every $I,J\subseteq\{1,2,\ldots\}$ with $\mathrm{dist}(I,J)\ge 3$,
