{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.899027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f78c7e515aae3ce07a7d80daf766af62921852fc0ca7cd302ac2abe712d96b0d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2606.20169, 'THEORY OF UNCERTAIN PROBABILITY:\\ CAN WE DERIVE THE PROBABILITY DENSITY FUNCTION OF UNCER'] If $\left(\mathcal{U},\mathfrak{U}\right)$ is an arbitrary measurable space, a function $\mathbb{X}$: $\Pi\rightarrow\mathcal{U}$ is a measurable map from $\left(\Pi, \mathbb{F}\right)$ to $\left(\mathcal{U},\mathfrak{U}\right)$ if 

