{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.405699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f8014468547ba466d92661c439d8c71abd0ec1f8084d090892906726c7c0d6b3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 8 of arXiv:2604.06516, 'From stochastic individual-based models to free-boundary Hamilton-Jacobi equations'] We have that for all $t>0$, $\Phi :\mathbb{D}[0,t]\times[0,t]\to\mathbb{R}$ a bounded measurable function and $x\in \mathbb{R}$:
