{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.644297+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f82fbeb145815804876c218965332c2c976d06eec6660c9e3a8a86f0cd06603e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:bridge_subg_tail of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $B^{(n)}_x=(B^{(n)}_{x;t}:0\leq t \leq n)$ be a uniform bridge of length $n$ ending at $x$, that is a uniform element from $\mathcal B^{(n)}_x$.
