{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.828359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f9a4e78af214e6481affaaad614a4a5733d0cb574db9cd4c06455d2d9a8627d1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: bound_integral_CGO_by_distance of arXiv:2609.00257, 'Stability estimates for the initial-to-final-state inverse problem'] Let $n\geq2$ and $V_1, V_2\in L^1((0, T); L^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n))$ with $\|V_j\|_{w_{\delta,\varepsilon} }< \infty$, for $j\in \{1, 2\}$. Let ${\bf u_1}$ and ${\bf u_2}$ be the CGO solutions (equation eq:CGO of the paper) to the Schr\"odinger equation, as constructed in subsection (sect: CGO of the paper), with potentials $V_1$ and $V_2$ respectively. Then, there holds 

