{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:04:30.598085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fbb55ca28595930d463ffd9686305c094c28d11a52638e3bf09cca3de09791ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mmt-unif of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] Fix any $t_{0} > 0$. There exists an $ \mathbf{r} >1 $ such that the following holds: for any $ p > 0, 2<  \beta < \mathbf{a}/2 $ and $t>t_{0} $, there exists a $C(t_{0})>0$ such that for any $u_{0}\in H^{\mathbf{b}}$ with $\mathbf{b}= (\mathbf{a}-3)/2$ 
