{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.628582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcc43b33ff54ced6ceb6d6dc837e1d632c3a84e9791a4c9b887df5097626f4b5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 222 (Estimates for the error integrals generated by the weight) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Assume that $1 \le N \le \Ntop, \, v \in \velocityarray = \{v^1,v^2,v^3\}$. Let $\tander^N \in \mathfrak{P}^{(N)}$, where $\mathfrak{P}^{(N)}$
