{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.677507+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fcdb2fce8b470e8ac84675ddc529ad8ed7bde29fa66215f2335a4ab3412e05db","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2609.03750, '\bf Pullback Measure Attractors, Zero-Noise Limits, and Moderate Deviations for 2D Stochas'] Suppose Hypotheses \ref{PEeqAssum-2.2}, \ref{PEeqAssum-2.3} and \eqref{PETNs-3.01} hold. Then, for every $\tau \in \mathbb{R}$ and $D = \{D(t), t \in \mathbb{R}\} \in \mathfrak{D}$, there exist ${T} := {T}(\tau, D) > 0$ and  $\epsilon_{0}\in (0,1)$ such that for all $\epsilon\in (0,\epsilon_{0})$ and $t \geq {T}$, the solution $v$ of \eqref{PEeq-2.15} satisfies
