    \]
    has a unique solution which is an element of $\widetilde{\mathcal{M}}_1(\mathbb{R^d})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.823524+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd9687d39ef603f80166c3acad49d4a34f39f96f52d45b75bf97d7acf47a52ce","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition redchain of arXiv:2607.18635, 'Remainders of generalised Taylor expansions and a priori bounds for rough differential equ'] We inductively define the map $C:{\mathcal T}_b\to \mathbb{N}$ by setting $C(\bullet)=1$ and
