		where the set of binary trees ${\mathcal R}^-(\rho)$ has been introduced in Definition (Def: operations binary trees2 of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.986495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd97c5ace872dff91401f6c21a1cec339933746f465af8e20df087f579883b52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma grandes vitesses of arXiv:2412.00865, 'On the spectral problem and fractional diffusion limit for Fokker-Planck with(-out) drift '] Let $s_0>0$ fixed, large enough. Then, the following uniform estimates, with respect to $\eta$,  hold: \smallskip

\noindent 1.  For all $\gamma \in (\frac{d}{2},\frac{d+1}{2}]$ and for $\nu \in (\gamma-\frac{d+1}{2},\gamma-\frac{d-1}{2})$,  one has
\begin{equation}
\left\| |s_1|^{\frac{1}{2}}|s|_\eta^{-\nu} (H_\eta - c_\eta m_\eta) \right\|_{L^2(\{|s_1| \leqslant s_0\})} + \big\| s_1 H_\eta \big\|_{L^2(\{|s_1| \geqslant s_0\})} \lesssim 1 ,
\end{equation}
2.  For all $\gamma \in (\frac{d+1}{2},\frac{d+4}{2})$,  one has 
\begin{equation}
\left\|\frac{H_\eta - c_\eta m_\eta}{|s|_\eta} \right\|_{L^2(\mathbb{R}^d)} + \big\| s_1 H_\eta \big\|_{L^2(\{|s_1| \geqslant s_0\})} \lesssim 1 .
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:36:49.843639+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd9891125bbe6a301d95686d278990ca517caa72e258661059683a21874b73ab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:dgt4-height-lower-stretched of arXiv:2609.02829, 'Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile'] Suppose (equation eq:dgt4-exp-moment of the paper) holds. Suppose also that there are
			$\gamma,a,A,s_{0}>0$ such that for every $s\geq s_{0}$,
			\begin{equation}
				\mathbb{P}(\zeta(0)\leq -s)\geq ae^{-As^\gamma}\, .
			\end{equation}
			There is $c>0$ such that, for all large $t$,
			\[
				\mathbb{E} u_t(0)\geq c(\log t)^{1/\min\{\gamma,d/2\}}\, .
			\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.362896+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fd9a3aeacd46caffc1976efb068d5abae94d6b6941f12d153512c9db39decd5d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition e:pnfi of arXiv:2411.13257, '\titlefont \vspace{-5ex} Inference by Multiple Identical Observers'] {\rm 

\smallskip\noindent{\bf Principle of  no future information} (PNFI). 
Let $P_A$ be a probability on $(\Omega, {\mathcal F})$ which satisfies (PN).
