{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:22:48.904160+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fda8370dff445e29a4c029c561f46d7745609da01066b89118b3fdacda2ea505","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.29316, 'Powers of the Dirac Operator on $S^1\times S^{n-1}$'] The order $2k+1$ conformally covariant differential operator $A_{2k+1}$ on the spinor bundle over $M$,
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
&A_{2k+1}=\sqrt{-1}\a^0\cdot Z(2k+1)\\
&\quad=\sqrt{-1}\a^0\cdot\prod_{l=0}^{k}(-\sqrt{-1}\a^0\dc-k+2l)\cdot\prod_{m=0}^{k-1}(-\sqrt{-1}\dc\a^0-(k-1)+2m),
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
has the leading term $(-1)^k\cdot\dc^{2k+1}$. And the square of $A_{2k+1}$ acts as
\begin{equation*}
\prod_{l=-k}^k (f+J+l)(-f+J+l)\text{ on }V(f,j,\X,\e).
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.323534+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdb95781c8cd18b061f6fa1a7245b8f5c79866e4fe71f8138a1e2bfa7678f4e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Cheeger theorem of arXiv:2606.01683, 'Singular-value gap of nonreversible Markov processes'] Consider a Markov jump process on a standard Borel space with generator (equation generator of jump process 2 of the paper), an invariant probability measure $\mu$,
    and jump rates bounded by $q(x,S) \leq q_{\mathrm{max}} < \infty$ for $\mu$-a.e. $x$. Let $\gamma$ be the associated 
    singular-value gap and $\xi$ the Cheeger constant defined in (equation Cheeger constant definition of the paper). Then
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\xi^2}{2q_{\mathrm{max}}} \leq \gamma \leq \frac{36}{5} \xi.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.722090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdbc72943d243085d00ab99a476f039ba02e0d823839f4a26b22e30e9418b0d6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cutoff of arXiv:2411.04157, 'Stochastic homogenization of dynamical discrete optimal transport'] Let $\tau,j_0,\alpha$ be as above. Let $U=\frac{\mathcal{L}^n}{\mathcal{L}^n(Q_{j_0,\alpha})}\in {\mathcal M}_+(\mathbb{R}^n)$
     be the Lebesgue measure normalized by the volume of $Q_{j_0,\alpha}$.  Then for any $\delta>0$ there is a cutoff function $\eta\in C_c^\infty(Q_{j_0,\alpha};[0,1])$ such that
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\eta(x) =1 $ whenever $x\in  Q_{j_0,\alpha}$ with $\dist(x,\partial Q_{j_0,\alpha}) \geq \delta$ 
        \item $\| \dive \left(j_0 \left(\eta \tau + (1-\eta)U\right)\right) \|_{\mathrm{KR}} \leq C|j_0|\alpha$,
    \end{enumerate}
where $C$ depends only on $R$ and $n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.458299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdbdabc7b7d7a5c6f46b054f4125d7c94bee5563d208bcfcc8c776fcbdc931e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 37 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma \in [1, \; 3/2)$ and fix $\lambda$ such that $0 < \lambda < 3-2 \gamma$. For every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$, let $L_n:=n^{1 - \lambda}$. There exists some $f: \mathbb{N}_+ \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} f(n)=0$, such that for any $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$,
	\begin{align*}
	\forall n \in \mathbb{N}_+, \quad	\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{  \frac{\Theta(n) K_n}{n \sqrt{n} } \sum_{z=1}^{L_n-1}  za(z) \int_s^t \dd r \sum_{x}   \nabla H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor x - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  )   \Psi_{x,L_n}^{\alpha,\beta}(\eta_r^n)  \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq \widehat{C} (t-s)^{2} f(n). 
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:11:44.381103+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdcdd45a5e1cf4eca72e2f129f2ce9e132c475e61b6f056cc8d66aad3857ba5b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2609.03116, '\bf \boldmath On the reconstruction of $n$-quasigroups of order $4$ and upper bounds on th'] Let $n \geq 2$, and $(A,G'''_n,p)$ be a partial $n$-quasigroup. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item if $(A,G'''_n,p)$ has more than one extension then all the extensions are cubical;
\item if $(A,G'''_n,p)$ has more than two extensions then it has a bicubical extension.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.619526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdcfaac78d3c269d18ff3c4675b7797e78bf4486a4a09f685bf917db279f484f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] There exists a unique Borel measure $\lambda_g$ on $M$ such that for every chart $(V, \varphi)$ of $M$, with $\varphi = (x^1, \dots, x^d)$, and every $B \in \Bcal(M)$ with $B \subseteq V$,
    \begin{equation} 
        \lambda_g(B) = \int_{\varphi(B)} \varphi_{\ast}\sqrt{\abs{G}} \; d\lambda_d,
    \end{equation}
    where $G \coloneqq \det[g_{jk}]$ is the determinant of the metric components $g_{jk} \coloneqq g\!\left(\frac{\partial}{\partial x^j}, \frac{\partial}{\partial x^k}\right)$ in the chart $(V, \varphi)$, and $\varphi_{\ast}\sqrt{\abs{G}} = \sqrt{\abs{G}} \circ \varphi^{-1}$ denotes the pushforward of $\sqrt{\abs{G}}$ on $V$ along $\varphi$. Moreover, $\lambda_g$ is diffuse, $\sigma$-finite, and satisfies $\lambda_g(B) < \infty$ for every $B \in \widehat{\Bcal}(M)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.365526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdd3fe469b3a9e3d37a646650617b0d4de3b3bd3d9845ea1acc535cc78620e7b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop compatibility of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $V,V'\in\mathfrak{C}$, $V\subset V'$, and $x,y\in\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$ such that for every $u\in V'\setminus V$ there is a point $z\in\overline{V}$ that separates $u$ from $x,y$ in $\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V'}$. Then
\begin{equation}
    \mathfrak{d}_{V'}(x,y)=\mathfrak{d}_V(x,y).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.801203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdd68b72cf64a8c3b715f4bbad57a4b56eb34864b20d4a090f058cc739188352","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Cf. Theorem 4.6, \cite{ab0}) of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is semicontinuous;
\item[(ii)] $\Ba_{F}$ is order closed;
\item[(ii')] $\Ba_{F}$ is uo closed;
\item[(iii)] If $f_{p}\too f$, then $\|f\|\le\liminf\|f_{p}\|$;
\item[(iii')] If $f_{p}\touo f$, then $\|f\|\le\liminf\|f_{p}\|$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.330277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdd889537ebfbe3e3632936db34ac115db2ced47417775ca69bf9e3fc1b71e04","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2506.22020, 'Norm-dependent Lamperti-type MAP representations of stable processes and Brownian motions '] Let $(\xi,\Xi)=(\xi_t,\Xi_t)_{t\geq0}$ be the underlying MAP of $Z$ from (\ref{item_a}) with respect to $\|\cdot\|_1$. The killing rate of $(\xi,\Xi)$ is given by
	\begin{equation}
		q(\boldsymbol{x})=\mathbbm{1}_{(0,\infty)^d}(\boldsymbol{x})\frac{1}{\alpha}\sum_{k=1}^d \frac{\Gamma(1+\alpha)\sin(\pi\alpha(1-\rho_k))}{\pi} \Big(\frac{x_k}{\|\boldsymbol{x}\|_1}\Big)^{-\alpha},\quad \boldsymbol{x}=(x_1,\ldots,x_d)\in(0,\infty)^d,

	\end{equation}
where $\rho_k\coloneqq\mathbb{P}(X^{(k)}_1>0)$ is the positivity parameter of $X^{(k)}$ from the description in  (\ref{item_a}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.237907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fddeec1afd138b1ce8945c9044f60d592df909148b2765da0db08e741ae128f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 113 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] If $\phi:\G\to\rmM_k$ is positive definite, then $\hann(\phi)$ is equal to
	\begin{multline}
	\rmH_\phi(B_0) - \frac{1}{2}\sum_{n=0}^\infty \sum_{s_{n+1}\cdots s_1 \in S_{n+1}}\big(\rmH_\phi(s_n\cdots s_1\,|\,P(s_n\cdots s_1)) \\ \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad - \rmH_\phi(s_{n+1}\cdots s_1\mid P(s_{n+1}\cdots s_1))\big).
	\end{multline} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.662777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fde035618cd3f11128162e5991c7d150df406ac1b6bcea0e770fbf28c07f26f9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 (\cite{HJPS2}) of arXiv:2604.23656, 'Doubly Reflected Backward SDEs Driven by $G$-Brownian Motion with Quadratic Generator'] If $\eta\in H_G^{\alpha}(0,T)$ with $\alpha\geq 1$ and $p\in(0,\alpha]$, then we have

	\begin{displaymath}
		\underline{\sigma}^p {c_{p,T}}\hat{\mathbb{E}}_t\bigg(\int_t^T |\eta_s|^2ds\bigg)^{p/2}\leq
		\hat{\mathbb{E}}_t\bigg[\sup_{u\in[t,T]}\bigg|\int_t^u\eta_s dB_s\bigg|^p\bigg]\leq
		\bar{\sigma}^p C_{p,T}\hat{\mathbb{E}}_t\bigg(\int_t^T |\eta_s|^2ds\bigg)^{p/2},
	\end{displaymath}
	where $0<c_{p,T}<C_{p,T}<\infty$ are constants depending on $p, T$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:33:01.776777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fde05ff50f5235dc241f1ace06aaaa996044888333558984a7e68180c632864b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2605.14630, '2605.14630'] For any $\ph\in\cL_0$ and $\psi\in\cL_1$, one has the relations 
\begin{align}
 \Lambda(\psi^{-1})(t) &= \bigbrak{\Lambda(\psi)(t)}^{-1}\;, \\
 \Lambda(\exp_\ast\ph)(t) &= \exp(\Lambda(\ph)(t))\;, \\
 \Lambda(\log_\ast\psi)(t) &= \log(\Lambda(\psi)(t))\;.

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:18:19.204253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fde94651adcb350887d79ed98d53f9ad87e4703c5dfae4ba465dc5a6d47ed957","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2608.28964, '2608.28964'] There exists a constant $C>0$, depending only on $\omega$, such that for any $N\in\N^+$ and $f\in H^1(\omega;\R^2)$,
	\begin{equation}
	\|(I-\mathsf P_N)f\|_{L^2(\omega)}\leq C\lambda_{N+1}^{-1/4}\|f\|_{H^1(\omega)},
	\end{equation}
    where $\mathsf P_N$ denotes the orthogonal projection in $L^2(\omega;\R^2)$ onto ${\rm span}\{\psi_j:1\leq j\leq N\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.606977+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdea442df01598223bb5e1999b9d686ce4e4cd248a73dd4e5a6e1654946346c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:MainTheorem of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] (Mean field large-population limit) Let $0<T<\infty$ be given and let Assumptions (A:molarBdd of the paper)-(A:AssumptionMomentFiniteness of the paper) hold. Then, the sequence of measure-valued processes $\{\bm{\mu}_{t}^{\zeta}\}_{t \in[0, T]} \in \mathbb{D}_{\otimes_{j=1}^{J} M_{F}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})}([0, T])$ is relatively compact in $\mathbb{D}_{\otimes_{j=1}^{J} M_{F}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})}([0, T])$ and it converges in distribution to $\{\boldsymbol{\xi}_t\}_{t \in [0,T]} \in C_{\otimes_{j=1}^{J} M_{F}(\mathbb{R}^{d}\times\mathbb{R}^{d})}([0, T])$ as $\zeta \rightarrow 0$, where each $\xi_t^j$ is the unique solution to
\begin{align}
   &\left\langle  f, \xi_{t}^{j}\right\rangle = \left\langle f, \xi_0^{j}\right\rangle + \int_0^t \left\langle (\mathcal{L}_{j}f)(x,v), \xi_{s}^{j}(dx,dv)\right\rangle ds\notag\\
      &\phantom{=} + \sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\int_0^t \int_{\tilde{\mathbb{X}}^{(\ell)} \otimes \tilde{\mathbb{V}}^{(\ell)}}\frac{1}{\bm{\alpha}^{(\ell)}!}K_\ell(\bm{x},\bm{v})\biggl(-\sum_{r=1}^{\alpha_{\ell j}}f\left(x_r^{(j)},v_r^{(j)}\right)+\int_{\mathbb{Y}^{(\ell)} \otimes \mathbb{V}'^{(\ell)}}\left(\sum_{r=1}^{\beta_{\ell j}}f\left(y_r^{(j)},{v'}_{r}^{(j)}\right)\right)\\
      &\phantom{=}\times m_{\ell}\left(\bm{y},\bm{v'}|\bm{x},\bm{v}\right)d\bm{y}d\bm{v'}\biggr)\lambda^{(\ell)}[\xi_{s}](d\bm{x}, d\bm{v}) ds.\notag
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.795356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdeec1e787407df4133ba64e66a93cbdebff5e5640db7a1ffe6de473041112cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2608.17509, '2608.17509'] Let \((T_L)_{L\geq1}\) be positive trace-class contractions on a Hilbert space. Assume that
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item \(\sup_{L\geq1}L^{-1}\operatorname{tr}(T_L)<\infty\);
\item there is a measurable \(r:(0,\infty)\to[0,1]\) with \(r\in L^1(0,\infty)\) such that, for every \(m\geq1\),
\[
\lim_{L\to\infty}
\frac{1}{L}\operatorname{tr}(T_L^m)
=
\frac{1}{2\pi}
\int_0^\infty r(\xi)^m\,\mathrm{d}\xi.
\]
\end{enumerate}
Then, for each \(t>-1\),
\[
\lim_{L\to\infty}
\frac{1}{L}\log\det(\operatorname{Id}+tT_L)
=
\frac{1}{2\pi}
\int_0^\infty \log\bigl(1+t\,r(\xi)\bigr)\,\mathrm{d}\xi,
\]
locally uniformly for \(t\) in compact subsets of \((-1,\infty)\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.970997+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fdf2af602caa2ffe81bc9020a315262d3714abf3c24b8b701cbf99d671ec377d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:rmulmc_discretization of arXiv:2506.23062, 'Shifted Composition IV\@: \\ Toward Ballistic Acceleration for Log-Concave Sampling'] Let $\hat{\boldsymbol{P}}$, $\hat{\boldsymbol{P}}{}'$ denote the kernels for~(eq:rm-ulmc of the paper) and~(eq:ULMC of the paper) respectively, and let $\boldsymbol{P}$ denote the kernel for~(eq:ULD of the paper) run for time $h$.
