{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.331512+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe8f24e15627509104b5d1540ed26f48ad10a962aedd26b922630fd23bc8c95e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:heat_content of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded open subset of $\mathbb{G}$ such that $\partial \Omega$ is smooth and completely non-characteristic. Then, 
