{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.652911+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe9fe8c76f8bbf88fd813635c139421e8efbdd9453e48976acbbf80aab6b99dd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:dy_dt_f-regular of arXiv:2411.12076, 'Explicit solutions of the SI and Bass models on sparse Erd\H{o}s-R\'enyi and regular netwo'] \begin{equation}  

		\frac{dy}{dt} +\left(p+\frac{q}{d}\right)y = \frac{q}{d} 
		\left(\frac{1}{e^{-pt}(1-I^0)}\right)^{d-3} y^{d-1}.
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.057051+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fea367ab7502822c27fcb91c88198f4a8c8496b6628d6f9e220df9770a09b3c9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:causal-reweighting of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Suppose that Assumption~(ass:reference-diffusion of the paper) holds.
Let $I=(r_0,r_1)$ and let $w_1,w_2$ be regular weights for the same reference
diffusion.  If $w_2/w_1$ is nondecreasing on $I$, then
