{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:41:29.030104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fec3870a9b90c5b5bf4592d68ccd9d6083e74294109b393fdee13ce83770c926","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.26565, 'A Horizon-Free Extrinsic Penrose Inequality'] There exist admissible minimal disks $\Gamma_0\prec\Gamma_1$, constants
	$0<t_0<t_1$, and a smooth function $v$ on the closure of the component of
	$M\setminus\Gamma_0$ containing $\mathcal E_+$. The function satisfies
	$v\to\infty$ along $\mathcal E_+$, its level sets are minimal disks, and
	\[
	 \Gamma_i=\{v=t_i\},\qquad i=0,1.
	\]
	On the component of $M\setminus\Gamma_0$ containing $\mathcal E_+$,
	\begin{equation}
	\operatorname{div}\left(
	\frac{\bar\nabla v}{|\bar\nabla v|}
	\right)=0,

	\end{equation}
	and on its lateral support boundary,
	\begin{equation}
	-\frac{\bar\nabla v}{|\bar\nabla v|}\cdot\nu_S>\tanh t_0.

	\end{equation}
	Moreover, $v$ and its minimal level-set foliation extend smoothly across $\Gamma_0$ to the side away from $\mathcal E_+$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.095886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fec444d9251d95b53b01fd27a01b7364693806fdc21ad6f281370e6d6f00d737","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem1444 of arXiv:2609.02795, 'Global smooth behavior in Kuznetsov and Westervelt type\\ viscous wave equations:\\ A unif'] Assume ((init of the paper)), and let $r\ge 2$ and $p>1$. Then
  \begin{equation} \label{1444.1}
	\frac{d}{dt} \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla u|^r \bigg\}^\frac{p}{r}
	+ a \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla u|^r \bigg\}^\frac{p}{r}
	\le a^{1-p} \cdot \bigg\{ \int_\Omega |\nabla v|^r \bigg\}^\frac{p}{r}
	\qquad \mbox{for all } t\in (0,T_{max}).
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:10.806784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fec4edb3c85e71998e6781d82224b127c4173eafe9c5aaa7cd95da3fbe405513","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] Let $e^\varepsilon_2$ be the stopping time defined by 
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
e^\varepsilon_2 = \inf \{ t \ge e_1^\varepsilon \; ; \; X_t^\varepsilon =0 \} \ .
\end{split}
\end{equation}
We have that
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \mathbb P (e^\varepsilon_2 > t)  = e^{f(1) t}  \ ,
\end{split}
\end{equation}
i.e. $(e^\varepsilon_2)_{\varepsilon>0}$ converges in law to an exponential random variable with parameter $-f(1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.775265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fec7719a983c584339fdad760dd6ae8cc1c0ba320c08ddbff6f43b924b3cfe45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Delta_g_1/d-1 of arXiv:2608.00399, 'The Heavy-tailed Frog Model'] For every $d \ge 2$ and every $0 < \alpha < d$, we have 
    \begin{align}
        \Delta > 
        \begin{cases}
            \frac{2}{d - 1} \text{ for } \alpha \ge 2, \\
            \frac{\alpha}{d-1} \text{ for } \alpha < 2.
        \end{cases}
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:15:36.156721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fec7d17e3c0cab922895658a1b1a2c393a1b12de736538e2e9f6a9d887ed6a29","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2609.01574, 'A linear bound for Fujita's freeness conjecture'] Let $Z$ be a normal projective variety of dimension $d\geq2$, let $x\in Z$ be a closed point, and let $\mathcal I_x\subset\mathcal O_Z$ be the ideal sheaf of $x$. Let $f\colon Y\to Z$ be the normalized blow-up of $\mathcal I_x$, and write $\mathcal I_x\mathcal O_Y=\mathcal O_Y(H)$. If $P$ is a prime divisor on $Z$ and $\widetilde P$ is its strict transform on $Y$, then
\[ 0\geq \widetilde P\cdot H^{d-1}
 =\begin{cases}
 -\mult_xP,&x\in P,\\
 0,&x\notin P.
 \end{cases}\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:15:16.642827+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fed11570449945daf272d680d2f0c82ab2c2864a803b8b0c9e1bad61100f1dd9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Cross-restart identity) of arXiv:2608.30715, 'Endpoint Energy Atoms Force Local Pressure Concentration in Three-Dimensional Navier--Stok'] For \(s<\sigma<\tau<t<T_*\),
