In general, the two terms on the right are not orthogonal in \(L^2\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.706364+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fed8e1d61bdaaf9b2fabb85646de2aa786f70204d7da71fcabc280bcb921273c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:asymp_miss_prob of arXiv:2412.00279, 'Optimal local storage policy based on stochastic intensities and its large scale behavior'] Under the same hypothesis as Theorem (thm:asymp_miss_rate of the paper), the optimal miss probability satisfies:
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to\infty} M_{\mathcal{C^*}}^{(N)} =  \frac{\int_0^\infty \lambda G_0\left(\frac{\theta^*}{\lambda}\right)L(d\lambda)}{\int_0^\infty \lambda L(d\lambda)}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.989904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee131587a418109488c3bdb9af7d327162f627a246c989c59cc046922122405","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Hada of arXiv:2509.02074, 'On the Kolmogorov-Feller weak law of large numbers for the Fr\'{e}chet mean on non-compact'] Suppose that $(M,d)$ is a Hadamard manifold. For any $x,x_1, x_2,\ldots,x_n \in M$, 
\begin{equation}
\|\mbox{Log}_{x}(\mu_{n}) \|_{x} \le  \|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mbox{Log}_{x}(x_i) \|_{x},
\end{equation}
where $\mu_{n}$ denotes the sample Fr\'{e}chet\ mean of $(x_1, x_2, \ldots x_n) \in M^n$, and $\|\cdot\|_{x}$ denotes the Riemannian norm induced by the Riemannian metric $\langle ~,~\rangle_{x}$ on $T_{x}M$. The inequality in ((ineq:key of the paper)) is strict unless $x,x_1,…,x_n$ all lie in a single totally geodesic flat submanifold of $M$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.256828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee1b18603588cc01979ed6a5eb0d1327e938e01f77afc4773c4b6638aa92157","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma jnestimate of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Fix any {\small$\mathrm{D}=\mathrm{O}(1)$}, and recall {\small$\mathfrak{t}_{\mathbf{Av}}=N^{-2/3-10\delta_{\mathbf{S}}}$}. With high probability, we have 

\begin{align}
\sup_{\t\in[0,1]}\sup_{|\x|\leq N^{\mathrm{D}}}\sup_{\r\in[0,\mathfrak{t}_{\mathbf{Av}}]}|\mathbf{j}^{N}_{\t+\r,\x}-\mathbf{j}^{N}_{\t,\x}|\lesssim1.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:10.966807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee206dda2d101414248024c30f63d7e010285f43e8a3f8d45dc4bab0eac78a6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 33 of arXiv:2606.12720, 'On McDiarmid's Inequality under Dependence \\ via Approximate Tensorization of Entropy'] {Marton's ATE (Theorem 1 \cite{marton2013})}


    Let $\mu$ and $\nu$ be probability measures on $\Omega^n$. Suppose $\mu$ fulfills the conditions in Assumption \ref{ass:marton} with constants $\rho_1,...,\rho_m, \rho > 0$. Then, the following ATE holds
    \begin{align*}
        \operatorname{D_{KL}}(\nu||\mu)
        \leq \sum_{k=1}^n \frac{\rho_k}{\rho} \cdot \nu\Bracket{\operatorname{D_{KL}}\Parent{\nu(\cdot | X_{-I_k}) || \mu(\cdot|X_{-I_k})}}. 
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.047324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee3e46bb81909f895c4ee1cb01d2748c77b890caf53442f00f28dc7d000b87d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2510.24562, 'Hard wall repulsion for the discrete Gaussian free field in random environment on $\mathbb'] For every $\delta>0$ there exists a constant $c_9=c_9(\delta)>0$ such that for $\bbQ$-a.a.\ $\omega \in \Omega_{\lambda,\Lambda}$ we can find $N_0(\omega,\delta) \in \bbN$ such that for all $N \geq N_0(\omega,\delta)$
    \begin{equation}
