Then $P$ is $\rho$-contractive on $S$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.305114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff58f6740b31b9eae4ea90fa2c75bcad6cf3f6231f0cf69b0399aa1413e24b84","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2608.21905, '\bf Ruin theory incorporating MIPP-type jumps'] Assume that $\hat{R}_n>0$ is the solution to
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
 \lambda\bigl(g_{n-1}^{\circ}(E[e^{R\xi}]) - 1\bigr) = cR,
\end{split}
\end{equation}
then the ruin probability admits the asymptotic representation
\begin{equation*}
\begin{split}
 \Pi_n(x)\sim C_ne^{-\hat{R}_nx}\quad\text{as} \quad x\to+\infty,
\end{split}
\end{equation*}
where
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
 C_n=\frac{c-\lambda^nm}{\lambda^nE[\xi e^{\hat{R}_n\xi}]\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}g_i^{\circ}(E[e^{\hat{R}_n\xi}])-c}.
\end{split}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.589270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff5a922d014fcba23673376c7aec3f6f1d09cd55e19d60a246c4b9f711c469db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eqn.41888 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p\geq 0$, there exists a constant $C>0$  such that for any $t\geq 0$,
