{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.788284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ff6dbb4bd5d002012025d74c73b85dc70a24ad9b1534f20eb06f2d0800c64c26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2604.00630, 'The contact process on a bipartite spatial network'] There exists~$C > 0$ such that the following holds for~$\lambda$ small enough.
